er scan and Gartax for the plot summary.',1),(96,'Island of the Undead','','Thanks to Nicholas Campbell for the cover scan.',1),(97,'Night Dragon','','Thanks to Ben Nelson for the character sheet.',1),(98,'Spellbreaker','','Thanks to Nicholas Campbell for the cover scans.',1),(99,'Deathmoor','','Thanks to Ben Nelson for the character sheet.',1),(100,'Knights of Doom','','Thanks to Ben Nelson for the character sheet.',1),(101,'Magehunter','','Thanks to Ben Nelson for the character sheet.',1),(102,'Revenge of the Vampire','At section 289, the player is told they must pay a gold piece to lodge at the inn. However, to reach that section, they must have bought a horse at section 276 which costs all their gold regardless of how much they have. This makes an important item impossible to get while playing fairly.','Thanks to Ben Nelson for the character sheet and Fireguard for the plot summary and errata.',1),(103,'Curse of the Mummy','','Thanks to Ben Nelson for the character sheet scan and Nicholas Campbell for the reissue cover scan.',1),(104,'Sorcery Spellbook, The','','',3),(105,'Shamutanti Hills, The','','Thanks to Brett Easterbook for the previously-used zigzag logo cover scan and to Ben Nelson for the white dragon logo cover scan. Thanks to Ryan Lynch for the remaining images featuring the original John Blanche cover art.',1),(106,'Kharé - Cityport of Traps','','Thanks to Brett Easterbrook for the previously-used metallic Dragon logo cover scan. Thanks to Ryan Lynch for the majority of the currently-used images featuring the original cover art.',1),(107,'Seven Serpents, The','','Thanks to the Ben Nelson for the previously-used British zigzag logo cover scan. Thanks to Ryan Lynch for most of the remainder of the images featuring the original cover art.',1),(108,'Crown of Kings, The','','Thanks to Brett Easterbrook for the previously-used zigzag logo cover scan and to Ben Nelson for the white dragon logo cover scan. Thanks to Ryan Lynch for the remaining images featuring the original cover art.',1),(109,'Sorcery! Box Set','','',2),(110,'2300 AD','','',6),(111,'Terror\'s Lair','','',7),(112,'Aztec Quest','','Thanks to sireeyore for the cover images.',1),(113,'Egyptian Quest','','Thanks to sireeyore for the cover images.',1),(114,'Greek Quest','','',1),(115,'Roman Quest','','',1),(116,'Handy Rotary Series','','',1),(117,'Powerhouse Series','','',1),(118,'Flying Machines','','',1),(119,'Balloon Buster','','',1),(120,'Wingleader','','',1),(121,'Jet Eagles','','',1),(122,'Patrol','','',1),(123,'Ground Target','','',1),(124,'Wingleader: Bomber','','',1),(125,'Two Seaters','','',1),(126,'Thieve\'s Quarter','','',1),(127,'Dragon\'s Hall','','',1),(128,'Midnight on Dagger Alley','','',5),(129,'Prisoners of Pax Tharkas','','',1),(130,'Ghost Tower, The','','',1),(131,'Escape from Castle Quarras','','',1),(132,'Soulforge, The','','',1),(133,'Test of the Ninja','','',1),(134,'Master of Ravenloft','','',1),(135,'Sceptre of Power','<li>Continuity: In the beginning of the book, you do not get Ulrik\'s cutlass if you attempt to use magic on him. Yet, you use the cutlass throughout the rest of the book.\r\n<li>Continuity: When you meet Thayne, you accuse him of sneaking into the alley. But, if you reach the alley after encountering the pirates, you hear him enter the alley through a door.\r\n<li>Continuity: Even though section 169 goes to section 97, the text does not explain how you get from one point in the story to the other. There needs to be a brief passage in between the sections.\r\n<li>In section 185, the path to section 239 should lead to 16.\r\n<li>In section 160, the path to section 241 should lead to 105.\r\n<li>In section 226, the path to section 267 should lead to 26.\r\n<li>In section 28, the paths determined by a dice roll, sections 10 and 179, are backwards.\r\n<li>In section 10, the paths determined by a dice roll, sections 190 and 208, are backwards.','Thanks to Jerry Wang for the errata.',1),(136,'Nightmare Realm of Baba Yaga','','',1),(137,'Sorcerer\'s Crown, The','The path from 184 to 232 should in fact lead to 196; there is no entry 232. Another error involves the fact that a Knock spell is used at one point even though no such spell is listed anywhere.','',1),(138,'Lords of Doom','The illustrator\'s first name is incorrectly listed as \"Diane\" rather than \"Diana.\"','',1),(139,'Curse of the Werewolf','','',1),(140,'Clash of the Sorcerers','<li> Continuity: Sections 102 and 119, independently, describe your revelation that Arno is part Drow. Each section then leads into section 172, where you have the exact same discovery again as if you never had the first one.\r\n<li> In section 23, the path to section 111 should lead to 17.\r\n<li> In section 183, the path to section 169 should lead...well, I can\'t quite figure out where actually.\r\n<li> In section 192, the path to section 212 should lead...well, I can\'t quite figure out where either.\r\n<li> Sections 91 and 180 do not fit into the rest of the book. This is a problem since section 180 is a victorious ending. They could be the destinations of the aforementioned 183 and/or 192 if it were not for the continuity error it would create (namely that Arno should be dead, yet you encounter him again).\r\n<li> Finally, although it is not technically an error, I notice that your hint is to get Rufyl searching for spell components as early as possible. The Dismissal spell that uses the planetar feathers Rufyl collects is never actually used in the book.','Thanks to Jerry Wang for the errata.',1),(141,'Gates of Death','One of the paths from section 110 leads to section 195. This is wrong; it should lead to section 2 instead.','',1),(142,'Trail Sinister','Section 36 ends abruptly, though presumably it\'s supposed to be a fatal ending.','',1),(143,'Vanishing City, The','','',1),(144,'Shadow over Nordmaar','Section 163 says to turn to one place if your roll exceeds 8 and to different place if it\'s less than 10; I\'m unsure which of these numbers is correct, but obviously both are not. Section 45 should lead to section 54, not section 189. The character bookmark lists your name as \"John,\" when it should in fact be \"Jonn.\"','',1),(145,'Spawn of Dragonspear','','',1),(146,'Prince of Thieves','','',1),(147,'Advanced Dungeons & Dragons Coloring Album','','',1),(148,'Rupert and the Secret Trail','','Thanks to Ryan Lynch for the cover images.',1),(149,'Rupert and the Seven Keys','','Thanks to Ryan Lynch for the cover images.',1),(150,'Rupert and the Miser\'s Hoard','','Thanks to Ryan Lynch for the cover images.',1),(151,'Rupert and the Haunted House','','Thanks to Ryan Lynch for the cover images.',1),(152,'Rupert and the Smuggler\'s Gold','','Thanks to Brett Easterbrook for the low resolution cover scan that was previously used here. Thanks to Ryan Lynch for the current higher resolution cover images.',1),(153,'Rupert and the Pirates\' Den','','Thanks to Ryan Lynch for the cover images.',1),(154,'Rupert and the Secret Treasure','','Thanks to Ryan Lynch for the cover images.',1),(155,'Rupert and the Mystery Moor','','Thanks to Ryan Lynch for the cover images.',1),(156,'Castle of Adventure, The','','Thanks to Ken G. for the cover scans and other details.',1),(157,'Island of Adventure, The','','Thanks to Ken G. for the back cover scan and other details.',1),(158,'Darkmoon\'s Curse','','Thanks to Nicholas Campbell for the British cover scan.',1),(159,'Demon Spider, The','','',1),(160,'Mudworm Swamp','','',1),(161,'Ghost Road','','Thanks to Nicholas Campbell for the cover scan.',1),(162,'Sugarcane Island','','',1),(163,'Journey Under the Sea','','Thanks to Ken G. for the British, Australian and Grey Castle Press cover scans.',1),(164,'Growing Up on Tékumel','','',3),(165,'Coming of Age in Tékumel','','',5),(166,'Beyond the Borders of Tsolyánu','','',5),(167,'Beneath the Lands of Tsolyánu','','',5),(168,'Target: Earth','','',1),(169,'Cosmic Kidnappers','','',1),(170,'Thieves from Space','','',1),(171,'Town in T