s impacting gameplay:\n\n<ul>\n<li>\nWhen Matabei triggers the \"Bandit Siege\" combat entry [p.150 in the Kenshin book] during the Naguni town incident, there is no mention of the Benefit to Matabei should he be victorious. BENEFIT H should be listed below the combat entry in the Kenshin book.\n</li>\n<li>\nWhen Lord Kenshin negotiates with the Wizard of Tabooka (p. 35 in the Kenshin book), it mentions the Wizard\'s price for assistance but not what the assistance entails. There is likely intended to be an increase in Troop Points, but the value is not specified. A less powerful wizard in the Matabei book grants 20 Troop Points.\n</li>\n</ul>','Thanks to le maudit for the errata.',2),(1835,'Doomsday Device, The','','',2),(1836,'King Takes a Dare, The','From le maudit: \"on page 27, where it reads, \'Tell the Kingpin reader to mark the section he is on and turn to page 21\', go to PAGE 56 INSTEAD; this is the correct entry! [21 makes no sense].\"','',2),(1837,'Dragonwand of Krynn','','',2),(1838,'Prisoner of Pharaoh\'s Tomb','','',2),(1839,'Unknown Title','','',1),(1840,'Unknown Title','','',1),(1841,'Unknown Title','','',1),(1842,'Unknown Title','','',1),(1843,'Unknown Title','','',1),(1844,'Unknown Title','','',1),(1845,'Unknown Title','','',1),(1846,'conte à votre façon, Un','','',7),(1847,'Theater Tree: A Combinatory Play, The','','',7),(1848,'Story As You Like It, A','','',7),(1849,'Oulipo: A Primer of Potential Literature','','',2),(1850,'Quest for the Auburn Pelt','','',1),(1851,'Space Gamer / Fantasy Gamer #77','','',8),(1852,'Alpha Complex','','',7),(1853,'Paranoia Player Handbook','','',4),(1854,'Solitaire Adventure, A','','',7),(1855,'Clones in Space','','',5),(1856,'Paranoia: Second Edition','','Thanks to Guillermo Paredes for the cover images.',4),(1857,'On the Trail of Blood','','',1),(1858,'Leda: Book the First of the Maduban Saga','','',5),(1859,'Dugal: Book the Second of the Maduban Saga','','',5),(1860,'Thakko: Book the Third of the Maduban Saga','