'),(2494,'User','You must untangle and foil a sinister plot to damage Sherlock Holmes\' reputation.'),(2495,'User','You are a young resident of Romney Marsh in Eighteenth-Century England. A meeting with an eerie stranger leads you to discover a sinister secret from your own past.'),(2496,'User','As an agent in London\'s Metropolitan Police, you must solve a series of mysteries which may be related to a plot to assassinate a Middle Eastern ruler.'),(2497,'User','After receiving a message from an old friend requesting help, you are drawn into a mystery involving a ghost from the Spanish colonial era.'),(2498,'User','It\'s the year 2066, and nuclear war has started on Earth. Fleeing the destruction, you launch yourself into space....'),(2499,'User','It\'s the year 1893. As a child living near the site of Sherlock Holmes\' supposed death, you find yourself drawn by chance into an investigation of what did exactly happen on the day of Holmes\' final showdown with Professor Moriarty.'),(2500,'User','While staying in an abandoned farm, you, your brother, and your friends decide to try out a new video game designed by one of you. After the game conjures up the spirit of an evil witch, you must save your friends by finding a way of dealing with the spirit.'),(2501,'User','You are an archaeologist working on an ancient Spanish ship wreckage near the Caribbean island of San Salvador. Can you save a man from falling victim to a centuries-old curse?'),(2502,'User','As the child of a shop owner in Chicago during the Roaring Twenties, you set out to free your family from the extortions of a gangster boss.'),(2503,'User','You play a researcher in a genetic engineering project in a remote region of Siberia. A series of strange events leads you into a sinister mystery....'),(2504,'User','World War I is raging across Europe. With the help of Sherlock Holmes and Dr. Watson, you must uncover a group of German spies who are sending messages from a beach in southern England.'),(2505,'User','In the months before the Battle of Trafalgar, you are a passenger aboard a stray ship from Admiral Nelson\'s fleet. Crew members are dying mysteriously, and you must find out who the murderer is. '),(2506,'LC','The reader\'s decisions control the course of a story about a strange wager made in nineteenth century Australia, involving the legendary creature known as the bunyip.'),(2533,'User','You enter a creepy old house to get out of the rain, but learn if you don\'t escape by morning you\'ll turn into a werewolf.'),(2536,'User','Superman battles some familiar foes and explores an alien world.'),(2537,'User','Supergirl hears a strange sound and wanders into typical superhero adventures.'),(2538,'User','It seems like everything\'s going wrong at once; supervillains are simultaneously attacking Metropolis with giant bugs and hijacking the space shuttle <i>Columbia</i>!'),(2539,'User','When the Bat Signal projects a death\'s head over Gotham City, Batman knows something is wrong....'),(2542,'User','As a deer, you wander around the forest looking for food and mates, all while trying to avoid danger.'),(2543,'User','You are a fox, and you must explore the nearby forest and farm in search of food.'),(2545,'User','As a squirrel, you must look for food in the forest during the winter while avoiding a variety of dangers.'),(2547,'User','As a common country mouse, you set out to explore a nearby forest and farm in search of food to add to your storage.'),(2548,'User','The reader controls the actions of Talien, a young Kuven, a leader of one hundred men. He gained his position after the premature death of his father at the hands of ogres, and he soon finds that a position of power doesn\'t make his life any easier....'),(2549,'User','Ceddwein, a thief turned guardsman, must travel with his military unit to recover a magical gem in order to defeat a demon.'),(2550,'User','When a dangerous magical artifact is left at his abbey, Alynn, a cleric of Cearn the protector, is drawn into a dangerous mission.'),(2551,'User','Lor the elf isn\'t having a very good day; after a near-death encounter with a weretiger, he finds that all is not well with the local royalty....'),(2552,'User','You visit the lab of Doctor W (rumored to be short for \"Wizard\"), a scientist you met in a high school class; adventure ensues.'),(2564,'User','You must travel back to 14th century England to become a knight and to discover the secret of the Order of the Garter, a group of outstanding knights with a mysterious symbol and motto.'),(2565,'User','To prove that birds evolved from dinosaurs, you must travel back to prehistoric times and photograph an Archaeopteryx.'),(2566,'User','You must travel back 350 years to Japan to recover the sword of Miyamoto Musashi, a famous samurai.'),(2567,'User','You must find the wreck of <i>Our Lady of the Pure and Immaculate Conception</i>, a Spanish treasure ship which hit a reef in 1641, and bring back some of its cargo of silver.'),(2568,'User','In order to find out who discovered the source of the Nile, you travel back in time and participate in the expeditions of Henry M. Stanley.'),(2569,'User','You must travel back to early twentieth century London and help Scotland Yard rescue a kidnapped Indian prince.'),(2570,'User','You must travel back to the Civil War era to find if Harriet Tubman was responsible for the rescue of a slave named Thomas Dean.'),(2571,'User','You must travel into the future in an attempt to make first contact with an alien race.'),(2572,'User','You must travel back to the Ice Age and discover what inspired a unicorn-like cave painting.'),(2573,'User','You must travel through time to find the historical basis for the story of Atlantis.'),(2574,'User','Your assignment is to travel to the American West in the 1860s to discover why the Pony Express only lasted eighteen months.'),(2575,'User','You must find out who fired the first shot of the Revolutionary War and retrieve his musket.'),(2576,'User','You must travel back to the Warsaw ghetto during World War II and discover the location of a milk can containing historical documents gathered by Emanuel Ringelblum in defiance of the Nazis.'),(2577,'User','You must travel back in time to find out the source (and ultimate fate) of a gold and sapphire ring worn by Queen Elizabeth I on her deathbed.'),(2578,'User','You must discover what happened to a diamond necklace that was an important part of the beginning of the French Revolution.'),(2579,'User','You travel back in time to discover why the famously kind and sensitive Queen Isabella permitted the Spanish Inquisition to take place.'),(2580,'User','Your mission is to discover the truth about the Seven Cities of Gold sought after by explorers of the New World.'),(2581,'User','Your mission is to discover the ultimate fate of the battle sword of Julius Caesar.'),(2582,'User','You have to find the plaster death mask of Pancho Villa, a Robin Hood-like bandit who was an important fighter in the Mexican Revolution.'),(2583,'User','You must find out who the first successful Western settler of Australia was.'),(2584,'User','To explain the disappearance of the dinosaurs you must travel back to the Great Extinction and observe the last surviving dinosaurs.'),(2585,'User','You travel back in time and search for the real man behind the legends of King Arthur.'),(2586,'User','You must discover who it was that shot down the Red Baron during World War I.'),(2587,'User','You must investigate the role of code-breaking in both theaters of World War II and bring back a copy of a cracked code from each.'),(2588,'User','You travel back to Columbus\' famous voyage in order to discover the ultimate fate of his flagship, the <i>Santa María</i>.'),(2589,'User','You must witness the founding of the Iroquois League of Five Nations and bring back a wampum bead to prove it.'),(2590,'User','You visit the Pilgrims in an effort to meet Miles Standish and participate in the first Thanksgiving.'),(2591,'User','You must meet Ben Franklin and learn the details of his famous kite experiment.'),(2592,'User','Your mission is to visit the Boston Tea Party and retrieve one of the tomahawks used during the event.'),(2593,'User','You must travel back in time to learn about George Washington and the Constitutional Convention.'),(2595,'User','You are flying your aircraft when suddenly a storm transports you to an alternate reality. You must find a way to safely return to Core Earth.'),(2614,'User','This was a hardback release separate from the paperback series.'),(2618,'User','Corporal Flynn Taggart, a marine, finds himself battling zombies and demon-like aliens after being sent to one of the moons of Mars, where scientists had been examining mysterious artifacts known as Gates.'),(2649,'User','A fellow space pilot has been kidnapped by pirates and sold into slavery on a distant planet. You must rescue the pilot and free the slaves from their evil captors.'),(2652,'User','You are kidnapped by a group of pirates who are looking for a treasure chest hidden in a remote island. Can you recover the treasure and bring the pirates to justice?'),(2655,'User','The reader makes choices leading either the Black team or White team to score goals. The team to reach three goals wins the game.'),(2696,'User','While visiting Disneyland (!), you find a flying saucer (!) in a cave (!) and end up travelling back in time (!) where you find the Dinobots (!). I\'m a little confused, really.'),(2697,'User','You are a human who has arrived to the planet Nebulos to deliver a few shipments of goods. Once there, you are drawn into a mission to foil a plan by the Decepticons to gain an advantage in the war against the Autobots.'),(2698,'User','Your aunt and uncle are astronomers, and your sighting of an unusual falling object in the sky soon leads to an encounter with the Transformers.'),(2699,'User','Since your parents are marine biologists, you get to visit an island in the South Pacific, where you end up battling Dirge, the fear-inducing Decepticon.'),(2700,'User','You must help the Autobots defend a shipment of microchips from the Decepticons.'),(2701,'User','You are a Nebulan working on an oil rig, but you are soon drawn into a battle against evil Transformers....'),(2702,'User','You explore Gull, the City of Terrors, in search of adventure (or, if you previously went through <a href=\"/Item/2704\">Deathtrap Equalizer Dungeon</a>, possibly a cure for your curse).'),(2736,'User','You have been killed, but the Guardian of Hell offers you a chance to be born again if you can overcome its dangers.'),(2737,'User','The Lords of Darkness have entrusted you with a mission to explore a frozen underground complex and bring back a map of it.'),(2754,'User','Your uncle Edgar builds a time machine and you get to test it out!'),(2755,'User','Your train trip to a relative\'s house turns out to be rather stressful due to the presence of spies from conflicting nations.'),(2756,'User','Your friend (a chemistry teacher) invites you to see his new discovery and (obviously) everything goes terribly wrong.'),(2757,'User','While visiting your grandmother\'s house, you are recruited to save a fantasy kingdom from evil magic.'),(2758,'User','Your Career Counseling class gives you a chance to work at a local TV station during spring break. This proves to be a dangerous endeavor, however.'),(2759,'User','On the way back from South America, your plane crashes in the Andes....'),(2760,'User','The wrong computer gets delivered to your house, and when you turn it on, you are sucked inside and forced to play potentially fatal video games.'),(2761,'User','After riding in your uncle\'s high-speed race car, you find yourself transported to 1915 where your name is Jamie and you have a different uncle with a different race car.'),(2762,'User','You accept a dare to spend the night in a supposedly haunted museum.'),(2763,'User','Your U.S. Junior Track and Field Team trip is disrupted by international espionage.'),(2764,'User','You go camping with a group from your school in an area presently inhabited by bank robbers (among other dangers).'),(2765,'User','When you flee your laser piano lessons by stowing away on a spacecraft, all manner of bad things happen to you.'),(2766,'User','You run low on gas and decide to find someplace to make a phone call. Sadly for you, the place you ultimately get stuck with is a rather sinister-looking mansion....'),(2767,'User','You\'ve just won a million dollars! If you can spend it fast enough, you\'ll get five million more!'),(2768,'User','You purchase a genuine magic book for a dollar at a tag sale at the Old Puritan Inn....'),(2769,'User','You run into nasty weather while out searching for your missing aunt Louise with your uncle Dave.'),(2770,'User','After hearing a century old legend about three outlaws trapped in time you find yourself one hundred years back in time on the day the outlaws robbed and burned the town of Goldspur.'),(2771,'User','Your science fair radio telescope project attracts the attention of aliens....'),(2772,'User','At the beginning of the Great Depression, you reach the city of Chicago intent on making your name as a gangster.'),(2970,'User','As a ninja trained in the deadly Way of the Tiger, you must leave your island home to stop evil monk Yaemon from performing a ritual that will leave your god trapped in the hellish Inferno.'),(2971,'User','You must return the Sacred Scrolls of Kettsuin to the Island of Tranquil Dreams.'),(2972,'User','You must travel to the city of Irsmuncast nigh Edge and sieze the throne from the evil Usurper.'),(2973,'User','As Overlord of Irsmuncast, you must govern your city wisely before embarking on a perilous mission.'),(2998,'User','Once you have secured the help from the Stumland realm in your fight against Dark Forces, you return to your Elf Kingdom to report to your father, the King. But unexpected changes have happened at home....'),(3137,'User','Somebody has planted a bomb just outside the Bank of England. As a private detective, you undertake an international investigation to discover the criminal\'s identity, motive and opportunity.'),(3138,'User','A large shipment of gold has disappeared on its way from Cape Town to Southampton, and you are hired to investigate.'),(3139,'User','The Watcher muses on the power of choice while showing several possible outcomes of Iron Man\'s encounter with the Living Laser.'),(3141,'User','You wake up only to realize that you\'ve forgotten about an important history test; in the adventures that follow, you often have an opportunity to ride the titular Blue Bazoo, a nerd\'s strangely modified moped.'),(3142,'LC','The reader makes choices dealing with going to the Yukon in search of treasure.'),(3143,'LC','By entering a contest advertised on the back of a cereal box, the reader is launched on a series of adventures whose outcome is governed by the choices he or she makes at the bottom of each page.'),(3144,'LC','The reader chooses the development of the plot while dealing with a difficult neighbor lady. Can she possibly be royalty?'),(3145,'LC','The reader\'s decisions control the course of a story in which Stacy, a Christian teenager, confronts sexuality, dating, and marriage.'),(3146,'LC','The reader makes choices that shape this story of the consequences of drug and alcohol use, including drunk driving and peer pressure to use drugs.'),(3147,'LC','As sixteen-year-old Ann, the reader makes decisions controlling the course of her life and her behavior in such areas as friendship, peer pressure, self-esteem, moral issues, and faith in God.'),(3148,'LC','The reader helps junior Matt Brand make decisions about various aspects of high school sports including competition, popularity, steroids, success, failure and other issues.'),(3150,'LC','The reader makes choices determining the course of Jeremy\'s experience at Windy Point High School.  Uses a Christian perspective to explore such aspects of school as grades, course load, and extracurricular activities.'),(3152,'LC','The reader\'s decisions control seventeen-year-old Donna\'s search for spiritual truth and meaning.  Uses a Christian perspective to explore the issues of occultism, cults, and the New Age movement.'),(3153,'User','You and your monkey companion must brave the jungle of peril to find the legendary pyramid of Oraz and the treasure within.'),(3154,'LC','While searching for a damaged space ship which crashed over the Planet of Terror, the reader chooses among various paths and thereby controls the course of the story.'),(3155,'User','Five of your friends have been kidnapped by an evil wizard. With your pet monkey Zetto, you must sneak into the wizard\'s castle, brave its many dangers and get back out again with your friends.'),(3156,'User','You must search a run-down amusement park to find a mad scientist before he can release his insidious misery gas on the world.'),(3157,'User','Your plane has been shot at, and now you must a find way out of a dangerous island.'),(3160,'User','When investigating the strange sounds which interfered with your TV, you discover a castle in the woods behind your house.'),(3166,'User','You win a trip to see three movies being filmed. Unfortunately, the day you visit the set a new special effects device malfunctions, causing all of the movies to become real.'),(3167,'User','Your uncle, an anthropologist, sends you a magical raven as a birthday gift.'),(3168,'User','A mysterious old man gives you the opportunity to become an explorer, a detective, or a movie star.'),(3169,'User','When exploring lava tunnels in an old volcano, you come across a magical world of fantasy.'),(3170,'User','A green light wakes you one night, and your attempts to locate its source lead you to treasure hunters.'),(3171,'User','Your first solo space flight leads you to various science fiction adventures.'),(3172,'User','You are sucked from your boat into a strange fantasy world.'),(3300,'User','This art book contains a large collection of illustrations featured in TSR publications, including a few gamebook covers.'),(3301,'User','This unusual large-size paperback includes lots of general background information on the series along with songs, recipes and maps.'),(3314,'User','This experimental product contains both a novella about Gilthanas and a lengthy appendix containing game material.'),(3581,'User','After a cross-country bike trip, you experience something horrible - an encounter with mysterious slime, a visit to the house of a mad scientist, or a night in a haunted house!'),(3582,'User','You are an assistant working for a space salvage operation. While everyone else is away on vacation, two opportunities present themselves. You can attempt to prevent a huge explosion or you can battle space pirates. Either way, you may end up with lots of money!'),(3583,'User','You volunteer to test the time-travel devices in an amazing new museum and are given the opportunity to explore the World of Fantasy Creatures, the Earth of the Future, or the World of Dreams.'),(3590,'User','You are a reporter in the future. You are given a choice: witness the capture of an intergalactic gangster or attend the test of a new matter-transmission device.'),(3591,'User','You go on vacation to visit your uncle and end up investigating various strange occurences with him.'),(3592,'User','You are an ensign assigned to the starship Enterprise. You are given the choice to work in engineering, on the bridge, or in the science laboratory.'),(3593,'User','Your job as a reporter allows you to discover the horrible truth - the Earth has been invaded by aliens!'),(3594,'User','You are accepted into the Galactic Starsquad and presented with two possible missions: enter a race to raise money for a new medical ship or deliver an antidote to a planet afflicted by a terrible plague.'),(3595,'User','You discover strange worlds in the Bermuda Triangle after your cruise ship is destroyed.'),(3596,'User','You\'re a young scout working for some sort of space patrolling organization, and you have a choice of missions: investigate the disappearance of intelligent life from planet 3CG, or battle a gigantic, world-destroying crystal in the Signus Arton system.'),(3597,'User','You are the last person left on space station Star Voyager One after the rest of the crew have disappeared due to causes unknown....'),(3598,'User','In order to become the Grand Master of your planet, you have to complete three dangerous missions: kill a huge monster, defeat an infamous criminal, and destroy a magic crystal.'),(3601,'User','You are a new recruit in the Special Corps. Aided by James diGriz, the Stainless Steel Rat, you must track down Professor Geisteskrank, an evil genius intent on destroying the universe.'),(3613,'User','You enter the secret door in your room and are given the chance to enter either the world of video games or the world of robots.'),(3632,'User','Young Jason chases his pet frog down a hole in the ground and finds a lot more than a frog waiting for him down there.'),(3637,'User','When he loses his arm in battle with terrorists, spy Jack Markson is fitted with a mechanical replacement and reborn as the Bionic Commando.'),(3640,'User','In an attempt to create a copy of Mega Man, Dr. Light accidentally makes him human. There\'s no time to change him back, as Dr. Wily has returned with an all-new batch of battle robots.'),(3781,'User','You\'re a fantasy hero with a daunting mission.'),(3782,'User','You\'re a single male looking for a mate.'),(3783,'User','You\'re a bum looking to improve your lot in life.'),(3791,'User','You journey to a remote village in search of two thieves who have stolen a magical bowl. If you do not find the bowl on time, it will be used to unleash an undead horde into the world.'),(3793,'User','\nYou find yourself teleported inside a mysterious tower. You must find a way to escape.'),(3796,'User','You have been assigned to enter a dangerous area in order to deliver a pouch of jewels which will be used to bribe a goblin chieftain.'),(3797,'User','Princess Saralinda is in trouble again. This time, she\'s vanished into the caverns of the evil Time Master.'),(3798,'User','The recently-won Magic Helmet of Cornwall has been stolen by giants, and you must travel through the mysterious Forest of Twisted Dreams to retrieve it.'),(3799,'User','Your intense dislike for the current reigning champion of TV wrestling induces you to attempt to fight your way to the top.'),(3800,'User','You are an employee of the Starstreak Express Messenger Service. You are given a choice of two important assignments: deliver a letter announcing the successor to a throne or return a priceless figurine to its rightful home planet.'),(3801,'User','Once again, you are an ensign assigned to the Enterprise to gain experience. This time, you get to choose between working with McCoy, Spock, or Kirk.'),(3808,'User','An army of men riding on dragons have destroyed the kingdom\'s harvest and threatened world domination; you must discover who they are and devise a way to stop them.'),(3809,'User','King Henry\'s daughter is to marry to son of his enemy, thus bringing peace between two kingdoms; alas, before the wedding can occur, the princess is kidnapped, and you must explore Henry\'s castle and find where she has been hidden before it is too late!'),(3810,'User','The kingdom is threatened once again, this time by the ghosts of past champions, guided my a mysterious evil....'),(3811,'User','King Henry\'s coffers are running low, but he knows of a dangerous old castle where you can probably obtain some treasures valuable enough to replenish them....'),(3812,'User','While being exiled by the king, Sir Ashley, the Falcon Knight, proclaims his innocence and begs you to clear his name. There\'s a traitor to root out!'),(3813,'User','King Henry\'s cousin is coming to visit, but before he does, you have been asked to make the countryside safe by investigating tales of a mysterious wolf-headed knight.'),(3815,'User','One fine spring day, a golden knight appears out of nowhere, to challenge and humiliate the king\'s knights. While this is happening, the castle\'s treasury is looted!'),(3816,'User','King Henry has been acting mighty strange lately. The Wizard and Warrior realize that this is because he\'s been replaced with an imposter!'),(3819,'User','The Half-Moon Carnival is headed towards Castle Silvergate. Why is King Henry so terrified? Why does he beg the Wizard and Warrior to \"release me from the past?\"'),(3822,'User','While away on a mission of mercy, King Henry and his knights discover their kingdom has been overrun by the fearsome Barbarian tribe known as the Dundals. With the king locked out of his own castle it falls on the Wizard, Warrior (and of course you) to find a means of infiltrating castle Silvergate and defeating the barbarian horde and their mysterious leader, Goldenhair.'),(3823,'User','A female knight in golden armor freezes King Henry\'s knights like statues. Unless she is defeated, the kingdom will be overrun by her army of female warriors!'),(3824,'User','As Grey Star, an orphan raised by the magical Shianti, you must begin your journey to find the lost Moonstone and stop Shasarak the Wytch-King from conquering Magnamund. Your first mission is to track down the Lost Tribe of Lara, a race of magical creatures who may be able to help you in your struggle.'),(3825,'User','Having found the Lost Tribe of Lara, you now must use their powers to locate the Shadow Gate to the Daziarn Plane so that you can proceed with your mission.'),(3826,'User','Now that you\'ve made it to the Daziarn, you must track down the Moonstone with the help of an old friend....'),(3827,'User','All is in preparation, and it is time to fight the final battle against Shasarak!'),(3832,'LC','As the twelve-year-old daughter of Texas pioneers, the reader makes decisions in order to survive captivity by Comanches.'),(3834,'User','The king\'s daughter has been kidnapped by an evil wizard and locked in The Castle of Doom. Together with your friends, you must journey to the castle and rescue her.'),(3841,'User','Bivotar and Juranda must find the three Palantirs of Zork in order to defeat an evil sorcerer named Krill.'),(3842,'User','The great hero Syovar is being held for ransom by Malifestro, an evil wizard. Bivotar and Juranda must rescue him with the help of two bumbling elves named Fred and Max.'),(3843,'User','Bivotar and Juranda must find the Helm of Zork in order to bring peace to the Land of Frobozz. Unfortunately, they are opposed by a riddle-spouting demon named Jeearr.'),(3845,'User','You are a little pig, and it\'s your birthday. Your parents have only given you a funny hat, and none of your friends seem to be around to wish you a happy birthday.'),(3859,'User','A World War II simulation.'),(3860,'User','A dinosaur racing game for younger players.'),(3864,'User','While traveling through space your ship is captured by a race of alien creatures. You must escape capture and prevent the creatures from taking over the planet Earth. '),(3866,'User','Some friends from an alternate Earth where everyone has an animal head meet an alien surfer and end up embarking on a journey through time and space.'),(3867,'User','Nico\'s opportunity to compete in the World Surf Championships is threatened when extradimensional adventure calls once again....'),(3868,'User','Nico tries once again to enter a surfing competition, but things are complicated when he arrives several millennia early.'),(3869,'User','Ulysses needs the Golden Udder back, but Nico has managed to lose it....'),(3870,'User','Claudia, Nico and Mikey play bingo at The Jaws of Death and win a trip to a health farm whose owner has a dark secret lurking in a labyrinth.'),(3871,'User','While Nico tries yet again to win the World Surfing Championship, an obelisk turns up with a familiar-looking figure carved on its surface....'),(3890,'User','This is a translation of the original <a href=\"/Series/28\">Adventures of You</a> edition of the title, not the expanded <a href=\"/Series/30\">Choose Your Own Adventure</a> edition.'),(3977,'User','Disaster strikes a small English village where reality and fantasy begin to intermingle.'),(4173,'User','This article deals with the author\'s experience writing solitaire adventures and includes some observations about the genre that he\'s made along the way.'),(4211,'User','Every five years, a spectral being walks through the small town of Valleyburg, while the countryside falls prey to demonic apparitions. Fourteen-year-old Jamie and his friends have made a brave decision: they will follow the ghostly wanderer to his destination. But as they enter the darksome forest, fiends from an alien realm descend upon them, leaving one determined survivor to face the horrors of the Timeless Night alone.'),(4212,'User','To save the Xhoromag universe from the Evil Forces, Jamie must reunite the Seven Crystals of Light. The Timeless One possesses the first. The second belongs to the mysterious race called the Quadrax, whom the Evil Forces are trying to exterminate using a terrible, yet majestic weapon: Spirale Flamboyante, the Spinning Sunswirl. To save the Quadrax and acquire the all-important Crystal, Jamie will have to destroy it... and uncover the secret of the Blue-Eyed Beings.'),(4213,'User','The third Crystal exists on a distant island on the Qyxxa Seas. They are said to be infinite, and they might even span more than one universe. To reach the island, Jamie must first confront the mysterious being called Qxuluxaqux, the Brainsphere of Q\'Thyd, and its eerie envoys, the Metal Souls. But even if Jamie reaches the ocean alive, can he cross it before the tenth Xhoromag Eternity comes to an end, stranding the Crystal out of his reach forever?'),(4214,'User','The quest for the four remaining Crystals of Light must wait, for the powerful Evil Force known as Xe\'Aaqax has devised a plan to plunge the entire universe into endless night. For this purpose, the dark entity requires a powerful gem called the Eye of Yraxanax, which Jamie must find first, and destroy, if saving Xhoromag is to remain possible.'),(4215,'User','The fourth Crystal belongs to an ancient being whose realm is a vast swamp-like region of the Fifth Plane. The Evil Forces have been trying to enter this sinister domain for over 100 years, but have fallen prey to a dark apparition named Xor\'Quud, the Silent Death, the One who does not exist. To reach Iâh-Xor\'s mysterious wanderer, who holds the fourth Crystal, Jamie must cross Xor\'Quud\'s territory... and survive.'),(4216,'User','From one swamp to another, Jamie finds himself wandering the jungles of Vexadann in search of the fifth Crystal, which used to belong to a vanished race. There is a mysterious world where the sun never rises or sets, but turns itself on and off in the sky. There, it is said, existence is dying, and there Jamie must find the fifth gem he seeks. But first, he will have to survive the onslaught of the Axrella human beasts, and save from their clutches a beautiful and enigmatic girl named Shania.'),(4217,'User','The Evil Forces have conquered the seventh Crystal and plan to use its power to cast Xhoromag into perpetual night, where they will reign supreme. To stop them, Jamie must embark on a perilous mission in the scorching Dexnaleqi desert, and descend into the botomless gorge of Nenxilaï to do battle with the evil entity Q\'Rehaxaqul.'),(4218,'User','The defeated Evil Forces have strategically retreated to the distant and mysterious realm of Exania, the Sixth Plane of Xhoromag. In this unusual universe, life has never evolved from its most pure and elementary form, and the supreme Evil Force, B\'Qrâhx, hopes to subvert this exotic lifeforce to gain the power to defeat the Seven Crystals. The final showdown begins in a world unlike anything the Five Planes have to offer.'),(4219,'User','B\'Qrâhx has been vanquished, but the Evil Forces have exacted their revenge. Jamie is now a prisoner of their very own universe, Gamorox, where Night has ruled for seven full Eternities. In a world entirely corrupted by darkness, can Jamie find enough strength to reach his enemies on the Wall at Night\'s End, and vanquish the ultimate form of evil?'),(4220,'User','Axéa, the first of the four entities Jamie must reunite, has chosen to live her nearly-eternal life in the mountains of Qataraq. There, various human races seek a being they refer to as the Creator, capable of granting the ultimate gift to the worthy: a look upon Time itself. Jamie doesn\'t know whether he\'s worthy or not, but since the Creator is most surely Axéa, he\'ll have to brave the mountains and the savage Unreals before discovering the strange truth behind the legends.'),(4221,'User','With Axéa\'s help, Jamie has discovered Iaxi\'s chosen realm. She lives inside majestic structures which fell from outer space, then were carved into giant towers by a population of slaves to the tyrant-god Vaxad. It is forbidden to enter the sacred Towers of Silence, but Jamie must reach them to communicate with Iaxi. Can he succeed without being executed as a sacrilegious infidel?'),(4222,'User','Every universe has a time-space discontinuity in its center. Xhoromag has one too, and this is where Exao, the third entity, has lived her nearly endless life. To find her, Jamie will have to enter the space between universes, the terrifying Negative Void known as the Ji\'Xuul, but before he can reach the edge of beyond, he will join with the last survivors of an ancient people and face the damned legions of the monstrous Qatharexxanieq.'),(4223,'User','Neither Axéa, Iaxi, nor Exao know where their final sibling Uxia has gone. She was last seen visiting the great Cloud Empire of Q\'Jan, and that\'s where Jamie will begin seeking her. But Q\'Jan is hardly a paradise, as corrupted beings wander the countryside and a once-proud race of people are forced to eke out a miserable existence. What happened to Q\'Jan? To find out, Jamie will have to reach Uxiani, the city on the edge of nothingness.'),(4224,'User','Uxia\'s trail leads Jamie to a volcanic wasteland named Qo\'Ixhâ, a burning realm under a burning sky. There, one tortured soul, her body charred beyond recognition by a lava pit\'s eruption, desperately hangs on to life, as terrifying creatures of pure flame converge around her. They are Xhatreqh, the ghosts of her own suffering, and to save her, Jamie will have to see her to her destination -- a mountain underneath a sun whose light may soon shine for the very last time.'),(4225,'User','To reunite Uxia with her three sisters, Jamie will have to reach the First Plane of Xhoromag. To achieve this, he\'ll have to recover the Third Ship of Xe\'Roxuul, which was built to reach that very destination. But nothing remains of the Xe\'Roxuul Empire -- nothing except ancient legends, and something about an underground city whose entrance can only be revealed by the enigmatic Night Suns.'),(4226,'User','To save one million of their children from the plague which would have wiped them out, the Roxuu built the legendary Third Ship. One trillion years later, it still awaits its final launch codes, deep in a timeless city beneath the surface of Xhoromag. It can take Jamie to Uxia, but even if it does -- even if Jamie can somehow defeat the ghostly Intangibles to get to it -- the First Plane of Xhoromag is not without its own dangerous inhabitants.'),(4227,'User','Before embarking on the final quest to defeat the mad Oaxu, Uxia and her sisters will need to recover their lost strength. For that purpose, Uxia leads them to the Pillar of the Universe, origin of the Lake of Life, source of the Rivers of Light. But Jamie and the entities are not the only beings seeking the otherworldly power of the Rivers. As it turns out, Jamie will soon have to face enemies he never thought he\'d see again.'),(4228,'User','The Third Starship of Xe\'Roxuul has brought Jamie and the T\'Qixia entities to the universe where the latter were born -- T\'Qixia itself. The final battle will now begin, as Oaxu the Destroyer, now calling himself RaôQwaan, summons every long-dead creature his evil mind can remember from T\'Qixia\'s distant past. How do you defeat a being with the power to control life and death? This is what Jamie will need to discover, before his own life is snuffed like a candle in the wind.'),(4288,'User','To discover why the Xhâ Niâs were born, sixteen-year-old Shania, the last of her wondrous and terrifying kind, must enter the Xhoromag Overrealms. There is one way to do this easily: reach the magnificent Qyazeÿazen, the Portal of All Time, the doorway to every dimension in the whole of creation. But such a natural wonder hasn\'t remained undiscovered -- or unprotected. To reach her goal, Shania will face the occupying armies of the Volderxaav Empire, as well as the mad ambitions of General Xaal Perdis, who believes Shania can show him the True Face of God. The young girl won\'t necessarily have to fight alone, for she\'ll find friends as well as enemies, but nothing will prepare her for what Zahren Qöhh, the Prince of Cruelty, has in mind for her. For this powerful warrior has a single goal: make the Xhâ Niâ race vanish from the universe!'),(4290,'User','\"Ruri\" means \"Buddhist holy blue\" and the title itself is a reference to the fact that long ago, people sent dolls floating down rivers believing that their misfortunes would disappear along with the dolls.'),(4300,'User','A young adventurer sets out to find some haunted mines beyond a forest. A much simplified version of the RPG\'s combat rules is used to resolve battles.'),(4373,'User','In this first adventure, you have to meet Hassan Sabba, also called \"The old man in the mountain,\" leader of the Hachachins sect (the name of which is actually the origin of the word \"assassin\" in many languages, including French and English).'),(4374,'User','In the first book of the series, your character had to find Hassan Sabba to discover the secret of the famed city of Shangri-La. Unfortunately, even the old man doesn\'t know the location of Shangri-La, since all the texts telling the stories of the location of this city have been destroyed or lost. Hassan Sabba only knows that a priest of Ancient Egypt named Antarsis traveled to a country far from Egypt. It took him a year to come back by foot, and from its description, Hassan is sure that Antarsis found Shangri-La. Thus, you\'ve been magically transported to Ancient Egypt and given the ability to understand every human language.'),(4375,'User','Prester John is still on his way to Shangri-La. Antarsis, the priest of Ancient Egypt, told you that he didn\'t know the exact path to Shangri-La but someone close to King Solomon did. That man, called Nikanor, is an advisor of the famed wise king. Antarsis assured you that Nikanor had been to Shangri-La and magically transported you to the tenth century B.C. to help you meet Nikanor. Before you went, the priest gave the \"Magic Eye\" (l\'Oeil Magique in French), a powerful magic item that enables you to instantly kill an enemy with its strong magic power (but only if the text allows you to use it). So now, we\'re on our road to meet King Solomon....'),(4376,'User','After Hassan Sabba and Antarsis, you found Nikanor at the heart of King Solomon\'s mines. Unfortunately, Nikanor hasn\'t been to Shangri-La but his magic powers enable him to tell you who will help you (it\'s the third time that Prester John hears that, he should be accustomed to disappointment by now...). A man called Souhsan will be your guide to Shangri-La. Of course, Souhsan doesn\'t live in this time era; that would be too easy. He will be born in 400 years, in the city of Babylon (another famous name). Nikanor creates an ice cocoon that will put you in a magical sleep, preventing you from aging. And thus at the start of book 4, your ice cocoon begins to melt....'),(4377,'User','Prester John found a tablet hidden in Babylon\'s Tower giving the next clue to Shangri-La. This time, the \"final advice\" given to him is more complete than what Hassan Sabah, Nikanor and Antarsis were able to reveal. There\'s a mention of Shangri-La itself; Prester John will have to cross \"the land of the holy cows,\" reach \"the land of the dragons\" and seek \"the roof of the world\" where Shangri-La lies. This clearly refers to India, China and Tibet, respectively. This time, there isn\'t any time travel; Prester John will walk his way to India by himself, lacking any specific person to look for.'),(4381,'User','You\'re Sinbad, prince of the thieves. You\'re bored, you want adventures, you want to fight awful bad guys and save pretty princesses. Your boredom ends when two important merchants ask you to transport a precious shipment and offer you lots of money for it. But the counselor of the Khan of Djaghathai proposes another mission: take the daughter of Baghdad\'s calife to Djaghathai to marry the Khan. This will seal a new frienship treaty between the two kings. And, as if you didn\'t have enough problems, an old beggar predicts that your destiny is to save an unknown nation from destruction. Which mission will you choose?'),(4382,'User','You\'re Fanwyr, the third son of a noble Urdo family and a proud warrior. The Urdos have blue scaly skin and pointed ears. They\'re amphibious, but live on Earth; more precisely, on a remote island surrounded by tall walls. At first, you must protect your city from a Sea Dragon attack, then defend your people from a dreadful pirate incursion and make some cruel choices....'),(4406,'User','This volume contains two items: one group adventure and one solitaire adventure.'),(4530,'User','This original German gamebook allows the reader to explore prehistoric times.'),(4604,'User','Caïthness is a human woman raised in the Fey Realm. She wants to know who her parents are, and thus she goes to Dorgan (the realm where the book takes place) to find information about them. She\'s described as a beautiful woman (Aura: 16), with good magic abilities (Magic: 14), average reflexes (Initiative: 12) and poor fighting abilities (Combat: 9). She has a dagger (damage 1 die) and the book of elements, containing her spells.'),(4640,'User','Alex Barcelona is hired to research the identity of a dead Yugoslavian seaman on board a merchant ship at the Barcelona\'s dock. With the help of Ana Durán, a high-class girl who assists him sometimes, he begins a routine case that will bring him into the shady environment of international weapon trading: fortunately Barna is a resourceful man... so much that he doesn\'t care about secret agents, high civil servants or police itself....'),(4642,'User','Chalán is a heavily indebted loan shark employee who accepts what appears to be a simple job - following and keeping watch over\r\na rich man\'s niece without her knowing.  Little does he suspect that the task will lead him into a web of crime and intrigue involving the girl\'s true origin, a blackmailer and (maybe?) even the IRA.  Of course, the true protagonist of this series, private detective Alex Barcelona (Barna for short) can\'t be too far away.'),(4673,'User','This book contains two short adventures (La Villa des Revenants and Les Diamants de lord Egremont) though the cover lists only the title of the first one.'),(4727,'User','You become involved in a strange adventure after investigating a Jewish temple under threat from vigilantes due to alleged golem attacks.'),(4889,'User','A mysterious bus was supposed to drop you and your friends off at the movie theater, but instead it takes you to the entrance of a terror-filled labyrinth.'),(4911,'User','The new edition and translation was issued under the title \"Varjovuoren valtias\".'),(5144,'User','Sunnydale is plagued by an unprecedented series of suicides; obviously, more than normal depression is to blame....'),(5159,'Cover','Hungry and alone, you look for food.  In the distance you see movement in the underbrush.  Standing still a man steps into full view of your darkvision.  He doesn\'t see you.  Lifting a large rock at your feet you heave it at your next intended meal.  Can your strength overcome the cunning of this foe?'),(5159,'User','Statistics: Height - 5, Body Points - 25<br>\r\nUsable Cards: tactics (2 points), luck (4 points)\r\n'),(5166,'User','It\'s the Twenty-fifth Century, and Venus has been colonized by mankind. Now the entire planet is in danger of being conquered by an evil race of lizard-like creatures. Together with Poncio, your pet robot, you embark on a mission to find the source of their power -- the evil Mandragor Tree -- and destroy it before the human race is exterminated.'),(5167,'User','It\'s one hundred years after the evil creatures from the previous volume were defeated. Now, the overpopulation of Earth, Mars and Venus has forced a group of colonists to travel to a new, hospitable planet in the Alpha Centauri constellation to find out whether it can be a new home for mankind. For that purpose, an enormous ship called the Alondra is prepared, transporting several families, plus plant and animal specimens, on board. After four years in space, a strange virus which only affects grown-ups forces all adults on board to go into hibernation, leaving the children alone to pilot the ship to its destination for the following two years. You are twelve year-old Camilo, the son of the ship\'s captain, and the ship\'s computer chooses you as the next captain....'),(5168,'User','The thriving civilization in the fourth planet has become decadent. The humans have abandoned any idea of progress and are now leaving all work to be done by robots. Seeing there is no hope for the human race, the old robot Poncio decides to install a device on all robots, which makes them forget the first law of robotics, and then expels all humans from the cities and forces them to live in the wilderness so that they will become apt for civilizing again. You play a young man who has become a hunter in the wilderness, and together with your girlfriend and Poncio, you must defeat an evil robot army which now threatens to exterminate all humankind.'),(5170,'User','These unbound cards alternate between introducing new game rules and using the rules in a solitaire adventure involving an escape from a dungeon.'),(5312,'User','This issue contains four mini-adventures plus some other articles.'),(5994,'User','Three kids are called by their adventurer uncle to help him look for Yeti in Nepal.'),(6148,'User','You must defeat a dragon and gain its treasure... except that this is a parody, not a real gamebook, so you\'re pretty much doomed.'),(6153,'User','The King of the Elder Fey has been betrayed by his own brother, who plots to take over his throne. As the legitimate heir, you must search the city of Suidemor for the fabled Forgotten Spell, which will set the King free.'),(6241,'User','Your uncle deciphers a coded message from the Sixteenth Century that reveals the existence of a tunnel leading to the center of the Earth. Determined to get there, he enlists you to accompany him on the journey.'),(6242,'User','A powerful ancient artifact has surfaced in a planet ruled by an evil dictator. As a member of an interplanetary knightly order, your mission is to infiltrate the planet and recover the artifact before it falls into evil hands.'),(6243,'User','An English aristocrat is found dead at his residence. The police believe they have the case solved, but your detective\'s instinct leads you to investigate further....'),(6244,'User','A mad scientist from the past has created a time-travelling device and is planning to use it to wreak havoc on mankind. Together with your friend Gloria, you must hop across time periods looking for a way to escape with your lives (and probably foil the scientist\'s plans).'),(6245,'User','You find yourself marooned on an island off the Brazilian coast. You must find a way to survive alone in the island and, eventually, reach home.'),(6246,'User','As Tom Sawyer, you have a series of adventures in and around your Missouri hometown.'),(6247,'User','You hear about an isolated plateau in South America where plant and animal species from the Mesozoic Era continue to exist, and you decide to lead an expedition to find it.'),(6248,'User','A storm leaves you stranded in an uncharted island, and you must find a way to return to civilization.'),(6249,'User','A wealthy man has died under mysterious circumstances. You must investigate whether his death was the result of a meeting with a supernatural hound, or whether there is a more mundane explanation for it.'),(6250,'User','A dying man gives you a belt that allows the wearer to become invisible. You must prevent this item from falling into the wrong hands.'),(6251,'User','A Romanian nobleman has hired your services as a solicitor, so you travel for a short stay in his castle. Once there, you find out he is an evil vampire. You must escape from the castle and destroy the vampire before he turns your fiancée into one of the undead.'),(6252,'User','You find yourself transported to the era of King Arthur, and must either explore the time you are in or find a way to return to the present day.'),(6253,'User','A kidnapped princess is hiding in an uncharted region of space. You must lead a crew of officers on a mission to find her.'),(6254,'User','You are Sandokan the pirate, scourge of the English colonizers of Southeast Asia. Your life, however, changes significantly when you hear about a mysterious woman with golden hair who lives in the island of Labuan.'),(6255,'User','The evil wizard Hangyord has stolen a powerful magic talisman. You must travel to Hangyord\'s castle and defeat him in battle in order to recover it.'),(6256,'User','You help a scientist develop a device that allows people to travel to other dimensions, and you get to test it out.'),(6257,'User','After your lemonade stand fails, you and your friends decide to set up a ghost hunting agency in order to make money during the summer.'),(6258,'User','It is the year 1846. A mysterious South American aborigine approaches you and offers to guide you to the fabled city of Eldorado.'),(6259,'User','You and your friend Gloria come across an alien spaceship on a remote field. You must decide whether to investigate it or leave it alone.'),(6260,'User','An evil alien race called the Snarks (no, really) is threatening to take over the galaxy. In order to defeat them, you need to find four parts of a magical item known as The Eye of Khoriand\'r.'),(6292,'User','You are drawn into an expedition to locate the fabled treasure of Aztec emperor Montezuma.'),(6294,'User','While walking down Mexico City you come across an old woman who is rumoured to be a reincarnation of a legendary ghost, and decide to investigate further.'),(6344,'User','You must infiltrate a city ruled by an evil tyrant and slay him in order to free the city\'s people from his scourge.'),(6507,'LC','Sonic, a blue super-fast hedgehog, and his Uncle Chuck once again confront Robotnik and his evil robots.'),(6534,'LC','A Cro-Magnon tribe is forced to confront its collective fear of the Neanderthal people they call ogres, when a young girl of the tribe, Shiva, befriends an ogre boy, and when Hiram, a young hunter from the tribe, is captured by ogres.'),(6550,'User','You are Ariona, a female bounty hunter out to avenge her father and defend the lands against an evil necromancer.'),(6564,'User','This is a translation of an unspecified French adventure.'),(6566,'User','Based on the reader\'s choices, this interactive work suggests other gamebooks to read.'),(6571,'User','This is an interactive horror story.'),(6572,'User','This is a vampire-themed issue, and its mini-gamebook ties in with the theme.'),(6574,'User','This is the Summer, 1997 issue (no month is included in the cover date).'),(6575,'User','This is a two-player fantasy adventure.'),(6658,'User','The Second Doctor, Jamie and Victoria get trapped in a bizarre parody of the Earth while the Fourth Doctor and Romana get entangled in strange events at UNIT.'),(6704,'User','After leaving Susan on Earth, the Doctor, Ian and Barbara attend a funeral on Venus, where the population is trying to cope with the impending death of the planet.'),(6735,'User','The Doctor and Ace find themselves in ancient Mesopotamia, face-to-face with Gilgamesh.'),(6746,'User','The Doctor takes Bernice to investigate the disappearance of an entire planetary system and discovers an ancient evil.'),(6747,'User','The Doctor and Benny visit Arcadia, a seemingly primitive planet controlled by a massive corporation with a hidden agenda.  You know, the usual.'),(6748,'User','The TARDIS crew becomes involved in typically dangerous events on an isolated research station investigating a mysterious alien race.'),(6749,'User','The TARDIS lands in early 20th-century Haiti, where dark forces are stirring.'),(6750,'User','A relaxing birthday trip for Ace, predictably enough, leads the TARDIS crew into yet another disaster.'),(6751,'User','Separated from the Doctor, Bernice finds herself in the murder-haunted past while Ace ends up in an apocalyptic future; however, they are not as far apart as it might seem.'),(6752,'User','A project to prevent Earth\'s magnetic field reversal runs afowl of the Cybermen.'),(6753,'User','The TARDIS lands in an alternate timeline where Silurians have reclaimed the Earth.'),(6754,'User','The Doctor and company face time-bending threats courtesy of (yet another) ancient evil.'),(6755,'User','The TARDIS crew are once again threatened by the consequences of temporal tinkering, this time tied to the Aztecs.'),(6756,'User','The Doctor is pitted against a decidedly unconventional opponent: the narrator of this book.'),(6757,'User','The Doctor advises Benny to sing in a punk band in an alternate version of the seventies where the threat of anarchy is quite serious.'),(7321,'User','This reference book provides information on behind-the-scenes personnel who worked on the program and offers plot summaries of the Doctor\'s many off-screen adventures, including comic strips, novels, role-playing games and gamebooks.'),(7331,'LC','The reader\'s choices control the course of Haley\'s sophomore year at a new high school as she navigates the social scene, deciding whether she wants to become a queen bee, a wannabee, a freak, or a geek.'),(7378,'User','This is a survey of the popular television series from its creation in 1963 through its 2005 revival.'),(7379,'User','A collection of essays and interviews dealing with science fiction and horror cinema.'),(7407,'User','Sete-Ka, an Egyptian prince, falls into a coma so that he can be tested by the gods; if he succeeds, he will grow up to rule Egypt, but if he fails, he will die.'),(7408,'User','A young prince has a vision of his father\'s death in a pirate raid, and he must find a magical sword to avert the prophecy.'),(7426,'User','This is an anthology containing four brief adventures.'),(7435,'User','There are no solo adventures in this issue.'),(7436,'User','There are no solo adventures in this issue.'),(7444,'User','This book describes the history of the board game <i>Risk</i>.'),(7477,'User','You are the superhero Crusader, and while minding your own business in your secret identity, you stumble onto a bank robbery carried out by agents of the crime cartel VIPER and the villain Pulsar.'),(7480,'User','Some editions of this are credited to \"Khara Khang;\" it is unclear whether the text is modified as well.'),(7516,'User','While traveling through the forests of Lupravia you are bitten by a creature of the night and must find a cure or become one yourself.'),(7522,'User','The great city of Zar awaits the addition of a new magic-user to the all-important Zarladen family that is charged with protecting it.  Lucin Zarladen has studied magic since early childhood and now must pass a test to show that he is ready to take his place on the ramparts of the city.'),(7529,'User','This title was announced and appeared in online bookstores before the series was released, but it disappeared shortly thereafter.'),(7531,'User','During your travels with the Doctor and Martha, the TARDIS is subjected to a mysterious power drain, and you must discover its cause.'),(7556,'User','In addition to the interactive story, this issue features website reviews and interviews with Joe Dever and several amateur authors.'),(7560,'User','You are Captain of the Guard of Cellandorn, but your city has fallen to the evil Sk\'Tuish. Now you must flee, regroup, and find a way to save your home.'),(7561,'User','While out on a hunting expedition with your trained Falcon, an unexpected event occurs that threatens her life. It is your job to rescue her. Can you succeed?'),(7576,'User','On the day before your birthday, your cat (who you discover has the ability to communicate with humans) takes you into one of several possible adventures, most of which involve time travel.'),(7579,'User','You are offered a summer job working the night shift in a strange warehouse, and you soon find out there is something odd going on inside....'),(7580,'User','The pottery fragment that you and your friends have been studying for a school project turns out to be more important than you had ever imagined, and you are soon on the run.'),(7581,'User','Having avoided capture by the dictatorship that now controls the United States, you and your friends make your way into a mysterious world located on the insides of the Earth. While initially your goal is to locate your lost parents, you are drawn into a mission to combat the evil forces fighting for dominance over both the Hollow Earth and the outside world.'),(7598,'User','This book is available in both illustrated and photographic versions.'),(7609,'User','You either cheat on your boyfriend, or you don\'t; both narratives play out in parallel.  Not exactly a gamebook, but clearly gamebook-inspired.'),(7610,'User','Originally designed for a contest, this book allows the reader to explore a 45-room maze.  Each room is represented by a two-page spread with text on the left and an illustration on the right showing links to other rooms.  The objective is to find a way to navigate from room 1 to room 45 and back in 16 moves.'),(7611,'User','Apart from the gamebook, this issue consists primarily of interviews (including website editors Demian Katz, Justin Rubaloff and Alex P., filmmaker Jason Scott and a number of amateur authors).  There are also a few puzzles and a comic.'),(7644,'User','This volume is numbered 15 1/2 in the series.'),(7653,'User','Follow and make the choices of the young rabbit, Jumpster Hopper, as he travels to the annual feast of the caretaker of Woodland Forest, the Noble Ranger.  His journey is actually a test, which he must pass in order to be given entry to the feast when he arrives.  The extra difficulty for Jumpster is that the arch-enemy of the Noble Ranger, the Dark Panther (and his followers) will be attempting to thwart Jumpster from passing the test.'),(7654,'User','Your mother has misplaced her diary at the marketplace and has asked you to go there and see if you can find it.  The likelihood of success seems slim but you never know what events may transpire that will even up the odds for you.  Will you recover the lost diary?'),(7656,'User','You must travel to Iceland and investigate the activities of an angry frost dragon.'),(7695,'User','A quiet night in front of the fire is about to turn into something more eventful and dangerous.  Can you rescue your flock from \"The Leader of the Pack?\"'),(7696,'User','Lone Wolf\'s quest to carry word of the loss of the Kai remains the same, but this time around he plays a much more active role in the battle to defend his monastery.'),(7733,'User','You are a surfer competing at Pipeline, a famous (and dangerous) surfing spot.'),(7744,'User','Part 1 of the Mahou no oukoku [魔法の王国] subseries.'),(7746,'User','Part 2 of the Mahou no oukoku [魔法の王国] subseries.'),(7748,'User','Part 3 of the Mahou no oukoku [魔法の王国] subseries.'),(7760,'User','This translation replaces the original\'s invisible ink with a red plastic decoder sheet.'),(7906,'User','This is a translation of an R. A. Montgomery title; not sure which one (he has a couple of racing-oriented books).'),(7914,'User','This is a translation of an Edward Packard title; not sure which one.'),(7918,'User','This is a translation of an Edward Packard title; not sure which one.'),(7920,'User','Inz, a young warrior in a world where magic and science coexist, must go on a quest for a rare flower in an effort to cure a plague afflicting his village.'),(7923,'User','You are a journalist visiting the set of a <i>Doctor Who</i> episode.'),(7933,'User','Your adoptive grandfather has been robbed and murdered!  You must track down his killers and find out his secret....'),(7987,'User','As a sword for hire, you join the garrison of a mountain fortress just before an army of trolls lays siege to it.'),(7988,'User','You are a Bosnian War veteran who works as a hired killer. Your latest job devolves into a hunt for vengeance....'),(7990,'User','You are a Bosnian War veteran who works as a hired killer. Your latest job devolves into a hunt for vengeance....'),(7992,'User','You are a Bosnian War veteran who works as a hired killer. Your latest job devolves into a hunt for vengeance....'),(7994,'User','You are a Bosnian War veteran who works as a hired killer. Your latest job devolves into a hunt for vengeance....'),(7996,'User','You are a Bosnian War veteran who works as a hired killer. Your latest job devolves into a hunt for vengeance....'),(8010,'LC','The reader is asked to help two twelve-year-old sleuths, \"Hawkeye\" Collins and Amy Adams, solve ten mysteries using Hawkeye\'s sketches of important clues.'),(8012,'LC','Hawkeye Collins and Amy Adams, two twelve-year-old sleuths, solve ten mysteries using Hawkeye\'s sketches of important clues.  The reader is asked to use Hawkeye\'s sketches to solve the mystery.'),(8013,'LC','Two twelve-year-old sleuths solve ten puzzling cases, using sketches of important clues. Includes hints for interpreting clues and brief explanations of investigative methods used.'),(8016,'LC','Two twelve-year-old sleuths, \"Hawkeye\" Collins and Amy Adams, solve nine mysteries using Hawkeye\'s sketches of important clues.'),(8017,'LC','Hawkeye Collins and Amy Adams, two twelve-year-old sleuths, solve nine mysteries using Hawkeye\'s sketches of important clues. The reader is asked to use Hawkeye\'s sketches and hints to solve the mystery.'),(8018,'LC','Two twelve-year-old detectives solve a series of mysteries using sketches of important clues.'),(8021,'LC','Two twelve-year-old sleuths solve ten mysteries using Hawkeye\'s sketches of important clues.'),(8022,'LC','Two twelve-year-old sleuths solve ten mysteries using Hawkeye\'s sketches of important clues.'),(8023,'LC','Two twelve-year-old sleuths solve ten [editor\'s note -- not true; there are only eight cases] mysteries using Hawkeye\'s sketches of important clues.'),(8079,'User','Supervillain Crazy Hippie has kidnapped Breadman\'s girlfriend Aloe.  Can he recruit sidekick Doughboy and save her?'),(8091,'User','You set out to reach California and strike it rich by finding gold.'),(8094,'User','At the time of the Battle of the Alamo, you can choose to fight for either the Mexican or the Texan side. '),(8098,'LC','\"Describes the events surrounding the sinking of the ship Titanic in 1912. The reader\'s choices reveal the historical details from the perspectives of a first-class passenger, a third-class passenger, and a crewmember\"--Provided by publisher.'),(8099,'LC','\"Describes the events of World War II and explains the significance of the war today. The reader\'s choices reveal the historical details from the perspective of a member of the Dutch resistance, a Canadian soldier, and an American soldier.\"--Provided by publisher.'),(8101,'User','You can choose to play a Mexican farm worker living in the American West Coast in the seventies, an immigrant domestic worker in the present day, or a young male worker in a meatpacking plant in the Midwest. '),(8106,'User','You explore the islands of the New World with Columbus, the Southwest with Coronado, or the Mississippi River with La Salle.'),(8108,'User','During World War 2, you can choose to be a Japanese-American interned in one of two concentration camps in California, or to play a teacher in a camp located in the South.'),(8112,'User','A group of children going for a picnic end up exploring a mysterious forest and having all sorts of fantastic adventures in it.'),(8126,'User','There are no solo adventures in this issue.'),(8134,'User','A duke\'s son has been kidnapped by an evil wizard living in a tower, and you are tasked with rescuing him. '),(8165,'User','A teenage couple go camping in the woods, and a ghost starts haunting them.'),(8166,'User','This is a single-page diversion, reminiscent of (but simpler than) <a href=\"/Series/294\">PageQuest</a>.  You create a character with two stats (HP and AP), wander through a maze fighting monsters, and try to come out alive and with as many items and experience points as possible.  The tongue-in-cheek adventure is available online as a free download.'),(8172,'User','You travel aboard a merchant ship with your father. If you survive long enough, eventually you will be captured by a group of pirates. You must find a way to escape with your life and rescue your father from exile.'),(8173,'User','As the winner of an essay contest, you are one of six students from around the world given the privilege to join Professor Snackport on an exploration of the newly-rediscovered \"Pyramid X.\" Needless to say, the mummies are not as quiet as one might hope.'),(8174,'User','While travelling down a road one night an apparition causes your car to wreck. You seek refuge in a nearby old house, without suspecting that it is inhabited by a family of ghosts who are out to kill you.'),(8175,'User','You must explore a dungeon inside a remote mountain which is rumoured to contain fabulous treasure.'),(8176,'User','You join an archaeological expedition to a Caribbean island and find that there is a zombie curse going out.'),(8178,'User','You are a vampire living alone in a deserted castle, and you must deal with a group of vampire hunters who have arrived at your door.'),(8179,'User','Your spaceship has become stranded in a planet populated by three alien races in conflict with each other. You must locate a spare part to repair your ship without being found out as a human by the planet\'s inhabitants.'),(8181,'User','While on a trip to Scotland, you have fantasy adventures based on several different myths of the British isles.'),(8240,'User','This is a novelization of the movie and only loosely related to the original game.'),(8261,'User','You are a new clone trooper about to go on his first mission for the Galactic Republic. Can you and your team locate a Republic legion that has mysteriously disappeared in a distant planet?'),(8262,'User','The reader is tasked with the challenge of running a science fiction convention.'),(8263,'User','You become stranded on an island populated by mad scientists and mutant creatures.'),(8264,'User','You are the child of an apothecary in China at the time of the Song Dynasty. Your parents want you to follow in their footsteps and lead a simple life, but you want to become a kung fu master and have adventures. '),(8305,'User','This collection, released for Free RPG Day 2008, contains quick start rules, a GM adventure, and a short solo adventure.'),(8308,'User','Baron Greenback plans to take over the world by replacing all world leaders with robot look-alikes from a secret base on the moon.  You must defeat him by advising Penfold, Dangermouse\'s assistant.'),(8312,'Cover','As a powerful student athlete, every choice you make sets the course for your track career--and your life. There are people who\'d like to see you win, and people who\'d do anything to keep you from it. And then there are people who believe that athletes should do anything to win--even if it means breaking the rules of the game.'),(8337,'User','Unbeknownst to the world at large, mild-mannered Dudley Serious keeps an incredible secret. When danger beckons, he becomes Captain Serious! One day, Dudley\'s attempts to woo his beautiful but airheaded boss are interrupted as the evil Cliche Master robs the treasures of Troy, and only he can save the day!'),(8338,'User','You hear about a dungeon where a beautiful princess is held against her will by an evil wizard, and you decide to rescue her.'),(8341,'User','A young woman has been found stabbed in the streets of London. Can you bring her attacker to justice?'),(8356,'User','Jughead is trying to get out of a date, so he joins his friend Dilton in testing the space rocket he just invented.'),(8360,'User','This article examines the history of gamebooks in an interactive format.'),(8362,'User','This story about a talking water drop helps children learn about the hydrologic cycle.'),(8407,'User','When an ice elemental attacks Tannatown out of the blue, you, the local hero, vow to find out why.'),(8420,'User','Your day takes a turn from the worse when your Internet date turns out to be a brain-eating zombie.  Oh, and you\'re a stuffed bunny.'),(8431,'User','You are a pulp-era private detective. A wealthy man hires you to safely deliver an ancient Chinese figurine to a museum.'),(8459,'User','You are travelling by ship through the Mediterranean when suddenly your ship is attacked by Barbary pirates.'),(8461,'User','You enter the city of Burgos in search of adventure.'),(8463,'User','During a journey through Galicia (Spain), you come upon a forest inhabited by mysterious creatures. You must either avoid being turned into a werewolf, or find a cure if you end up transformed into one.'),(8481,'User','The reader must find a treasure in a palace, interacting with other characters and using logic to find the successful path.'),(8711,'User','You are an inexperienced journalist looking to prove yourself... and you get a great opportunity when superheroes come to town!'),(8714,'User','James Jr.\'s on a field trip with his friends when he stumbles upon evidence that his uncle\'s old enemy, Goldfinger, is up to no good.'),(8716,'User','This is a solitaire adventure for Dungeons & Dragons, Fourth Edition.'),(8738,'User','You had a penpal in New Orleans who went missing after Hurricane Katrina. Her family had some connection with voodoo and so you think she may have become a zombie. A new girl at your school resembles your penpal and seems a bit zombie-like... is she your penpal, and a zombie?'),(8751,'LC','\"Describes the events of the American Revolutionary War and explains the significance of the war today. The reader\'s choices reveal the historical details from the perspective of a young girl, a patriot fighter, and a Loyalist determined to keep American under British rule\"--Provided by publisher.'),(8752,'LC','\"Describes the people and events of the Civil War. The reader\'s choices reveal the historical details from the perspective of a Union soldier at Gettysburg, a civilian during the siege of Vicksburg, or a Confederate soldier at Chancellorsville\"--Provided by publisher.'),(8752,'User','You can choose to experience the American Civil War as a Union soldier, a Confederate soldier, or a female civilian trying to survive.'),(8754,'User','This book contains the mini-adventure and Giak word list from <a href=\"/Item/1666\">The Magnamund Companion</a>, but it does not include any of the other content from the original edition.  As a bonus, it also includes a full-color map of northern Magnamund.'),(8762,'User','This collection contains 14 stories, 9 of which are interactive.'),(8764,'User','Your parents have sent you to a prestigious boarding school. Soon after you arrive, you find out that there is weird stuff taking place there...'),(8765,'User','While you are on a field trip with a substitute teacher, strange colorful meteors begin falling from the sky. It only gets weirder from there....'),(8769,'User','You can choose to be a French knight during the First Crusade, an English knight during the Hundred Years\' War, or a German knight during the Peasants\' War.'),(8770,'User','As a ninja in feudal Japan, you get to choose between three missions: to infiltrate an enemy castle; to use stealth and surprise to weaken an enemy army; or to work as a bodyguard for a powerful lord.'),(8782,'User','This book contains six stories: \"Meeting the Barbarian,\" \"The Lifeguard,\" \"Blood Rock,\" \"Luck in Love,\" \"Baxter and Bunny\" and \"Unfamiliar Ground.\"'),(8799,'User','This book tells the story of a professor and his studies about \"Risorgimento\" (\"The Resurgence\") and the Italian unification in honor of the 150th anniversary of the unification.'),(8802,'User','While out on a hunting expedition with your trained falcon, an unexpected event occurs that threatens her life.  Alone, you are the only person who can rescue her.  Can you succeed before it is too late?'),(8946,'User','Unofficial sequel to Armies of Death.'),(8948,'User','Unofficial sequel to The Citadel of Chaos. Not to be confused with Beggars of Blacksand which is a different adventure.'),(8954,'User','Unofficial sequel to House of Hell.'),(8957,'User','Unofficial sequel to House of Hell.'),(8958,'User','Unofficial sequel to Trial of Champions.'),(8959,'User','Unofficial spin-off from Deathtrap Dungeon.'),(8963,'User','Unofficial sequel to Beneath Nightmare Castle.'),(8967,'User','This book uses the programmed instruction format to teach about programmed instruction itself.  During the course of the book, many techniques are demonstrated including interactive branching.'),(8968,'User','In <i>Death Riders</i>, danger lurks at a fair held within a mining asteroid; in <i>Heart of Stone</i>, a farm is terrorized by something which can turn any substance into moon rock.'),(8969,'User','In <i>System Wipe</i>, the TARDIS crew witnesses the rebuilding of a devastated Earth and finds that an online game has taken on a life of its own; in <i>The Good, the Bad and the Alien</i>, an outing to the American West leads to predictable complication when crashed alien meerkat-people get involved.'),(8985,'User','You play seven short and different adventures, as a prisioner, warrior, martial artist, and other characters.'),(9070,'User','You must explore an ancient alien city in order to avert a terrible disaster.'),(9073,'Cover','Set within Orlandes City itself, nobles are being systematically murdered by a ruthless assassin no-one seems able to catch. Finding yourself thrust in the middle of a large conspiracy, you must make decisions that may put yourself and one other most precious to you in great danger. Can you locate the Assassin in Orlandes before it is too late?'),(9074,'Cover','Set in the coastal town of Myr, you have returned home after a long Summer in the mines of Durath Tor to find your hometown besieged by strange creatures. A dark presence has taken over the town and you are the only one who can rid the stronghold of Erid Buul, the mysterious new Lord and his ghastly cohorts.'),(9075,'Cover','Cruelly taken from your homeland of Orlandes, you find yourself in a far off land at the mercy of a gladiatorial arena. Somehow trying to find a way to escape overseas, can you also unravel a potentially dangerous mystery that puts two nations on the brink of war?'),(9076,'Cover','The mighty city of Falavia, the military backbone of Orlandes, is under attack from an army led by a man claiming to be a God. How did this come to pass you ask yourself? You’re sure it all started as some innocent adventure in search of treasure but somehow it turned into a nightmare. Also, why are people staring at you strangely? It’s not as if you look like you’ve recently been brought back from the dead or something. Oh yes, that’s right. You remember now…'),(9077,'Cover','Captured by one of Orlandes City’s most infamous brotherhoods, the Red Hand Guild, you are thrown to the mercy of the subterranean world deep beneath the streets of the great capital. Wading through the sewers and other dark menacing places, your goal is to reach Undercity, the City beneath the City! Only there can you find the help you need to escape this underground horror and bring down the dark brotherhood from within.'),(9078,'Cover','Two hundred years ago, the legendary City of Tarnath Tor was destroyed as it’s defenders, the mighty wizards valiantly tried to repel an orcun horde. Now just a place set within stories and myths, it has been lost to the outside world. A chance encounter with one who claims to be a time traveller sends you on a mission to recover some magical artifacts. This search will lead you to great ruins and the dark forces who have made it their home. Who is this wizard from Tarnath Tor and how can you trust him?'),(9079,'Cover','Cesaro Cortez, a famed explorer-conquistador, set out three years ago on his last great expedition. His ships never returned to an Orlandrian port and he was feared lost until a mysterious cargo appeared recently in Miramar. The nature of this cargo will put Orlandes in jeopardy, sending you on an epic journey to find Cortez, save the country and face your darkest fear!'),(9080,'User','This multimedia adventure is primarily in comic-book format, but it includes a CD (or downloadable files) providing audio endings.'),(9081,'User','This booklet, with tips on writing interactive fiction, was distributed as part of a writing contest.'),(9091,'LC','Monkey, a trickster, encounters many other creatures, some friendly and some dangerous, and the reader makes choices that help keep Monkey out of harm\'s way.'),(9092,'LC','Spider, who loves to play tricks, encounters many other creatures as he goes about his daily adventures, and the reader\'s choices help Spider trick the other animals and stay out of harm\'s way.'),(9093,'LC','Raven, who loves to play tricks, seeks food and shelter after a storm destroys her nest, and the reader helps her make choices as she encounters many other creatures, some friendly and some dangerous.'),(9094,'LC','Coyote seeks food and fun in the canyons and hills of the southwest, and the reader helps him make choices as he encounters many other creatures, some friendly and some dangerous.'),(9122,'User','The Westpark Scorpions Under-12s football team is playing against arch rivals, the Eastvale Lions. You decide what happens during the match and who will win.'),(9123,'User','The Westpark Scorpions Under-12s football team is playing against the Silverdale Snakes, known for playing rough and mean. You decide what happens during the match and who will win.'),(9124,'User','The Westpark Scorpions Under-12s football team is happy today because it rained all night, and the Scorpions players love a muddy game. But the team is up against the formidable North City Ants. You decide what happens during the match and who will win.'),(9125,'User','It\'s a big day for the Westpark Scorpions Under-12s football team. If they win today, they make it into the finals. You decide what happens during the match and who will win.'),(9126,'User','The City Devils soccer team is playing against Central FC for the Under-12 Champion\'s Cup. You decide what happens during the match and who will win.'),(9127,'User','The Rebels Under-12 basketball team had a bad start to the basketball season, but now the team is one game away from a record winning streak. This time, though, the game is against the tallest team in the league. You decide what happens during the game and who will win.'),(9128,'Cover','Evil wizard Malvel has stolen a magical dagger, and seeks to control the peaceful land of Gorgonia. Can YOU defeat the two terrifying Beasts that guard the dagger, Marlik the Drowning Terror and Klaxa the Armoured Enemy. Tom and Elenna will be by your side, but beware--by choosing the wrong path your Quest will fail and you may not survive...'),(9129,'Cover','Be the hero in this exciting adventure! Join Tom and his companions on a brand new Beast Quest, where your decisions determine the outcome. Meet old favourites Ferno and Sepron, and do battle with two new and terrifying Beasts: Aldroim--a huge shape-shifting Beast, and Cornix--a crow-like skeletal Beast who lures victims to their deaths!'),(9129,'User','An evil wizard has stolen a powerful magical cauldron, and you must recover it.'),(9130,'Cover','Be the hero in this exciting adventure! Join Tom and his companions on a brand new Beast Quest, where your decisions determine the outcome.\n\nSanpao the Pirate King has returned to terrorize Avantia, bringing with him two fearsome Beasts: Polkai the Shark Man and Dredda the Tunneling Menace!'),(9140,'Cover','In the fourth millennium, the Mandellian Empire of the Tau Ceti system is at war with the rebel army known as DWORF. And lucky you have been chosen for a dangerous solo mission to kill or capture the rebel leader, through mind-bending loops of time and space. But wait a minute. Just who are you anyway? And how did you even get here? Such secrets you must uncover if you are to unlock your destiny…'),(9141,'User','An evil wizard is terrorizing the kingdom. A young boy named Toby must venture into his lair to defeat him.'),(9153,'Cover','Based on the best-selling Fighting Fantasy gamebook system, The Shamutanti Hills is Book One in Steve Jackson\'s Sorcery! series. Your epic quest will take you across the mysterious hills to the cityport of Kharé, but only if you outwit the creatures, traps and wizardry you encounter along the way.\nPlay as either a warrior or as a wizard. If you choose wizardry, your survival will depend on your knowledge of the Sorcery! Spell Book\'s darkest secrets. With many other unique features to discover, Sorcery! is\na true challenge for novice and veteran adventurers alike.\nThe Shamutanti Hills iPhone App stays true to the original book, using Steve Jackson’s original text and John Blanche’s iconic illustrations. This highly anticipated iPhone App combines the user-friendly features of an e-book, with a new level of gamebook excitement.\nFighting Fantasy fans will love the classic story and original illustrations with a technological twist. No more dice, pencils, or bookmarks. All the special features are built in!'),(9154,'Cover','Deep in the caverns beneath Firetop Mountain lies an untold wealth of treasure, guarded by a powerful Warlock – or so the rumor goes. Several adventurers like yourself have set off for Firetop Mountain in search of the Warlocks hoard. None has ever returned. Do you dare follow them?'),(9155,'Cover','Countless adventurers before you have taken up thee challenge of the Trial of Champions, but not one has survived. Devised by the devilish mind of Baron Sukumvit, the labyrinth is riddled with fiendish traps and hideous creatures of darkness to trick and test you almost beyond the limits of endurance!\n\nDown in the twisting labyrinth of Fang, unknown horrors await you!'),(9156,'Cover','The Citadel holds a dark and dangerous peril for anyone foolhardy enough to venture through its gruesome gates. And yet venture you must for your mission lies at the heart of the Citadel, with the dread sorcerer, Balthus Dire!'),(9157,'Cover','Are you ready for the most unusual Fighting Fantasy adventure yet?\n\nYou begin this adventure not knowing where you are or who you are. All you know is that you are some kind of creature of instinct, understanding little. During the course of the adventure, it may be possible for you to begin to control your bestial nature, to find out more about yourself, and even to learn your destiny. But even if you know all this, success is by no means certain, for the traps and terrors of Trolltooth Pass are many ... Are you ready — to become the Creature of Havoc?'),(9158,'Cover','Terror stalks the night as Zanbar Bone and his bloodthirsty Moon Dogs hold the prosperous town of Silverton to ransom. YOU are an adventurer and the merchants of Silverton turn to you in their hour of need.\n\nYour mission takes you along dark, twisting streets where thieves, vagabonds and creatures of the night lie in wait to trap the unwary traveller. Beyond lies the most fearsome adventure of them all – the tower stronghold of the infamous Zanbar Bone! Part-story part-game, this is a book with a difference - one in which you become the hero! YOU decide which route to take, which creatures to fight and which dangers to risk.'),(9159,'Cover','Meow, Mewl & Maul. \nOnly you can do it all. \n\nYou are Holden Catfield. But your family calls you Holden. Or sometimes Mr. Catfield. You’re a cat! And you just woke up spooned behind the knees of Julie, the daughter in the dysfunctional family you live with. It’s a brand new Caturday! What are you going to do? Unlike dogs, you do what you want!\n\nIf you decide to go back to bed, turn to page 17. Venture outside and visit your girlfriend on page 8, or head further downtown to page 35. The choice is yours! But beware, being a cat isn’t all napping in sunbeams and curling up on laps. There are funny noises coming from the upstairs bathroom, a tomcat in the alley who doesn’t like to be crossed, and a strange man on the corner who is always giving you free samples of catnip...\n\nInspired by the gamebook fad of the ’80s — You Are a Cat! is lavishly illustrated from the first-person feline floor purrspective. The complete package from writer & artist Sherwin Tjia, whose graphic novel The Hipless Boy was nominated for a Doug Wright Award & four Ignatz Awards, the kittenish & catactular You Are a Cat! is a catventure you won’t forget & the closest you’ll come to being a cat without dying & reincarnating as one'),(9172,'Cover','D\'ordinaire, vous n\'êtes que l\'une des très nombreuses personnes qui concourent à la bonne marche et à la réputation d\'Automobiles Citroën.\n\n<p>Cette fois-ci, c\'est VOUS et vous seul qui allez être chargé de mener à son terme le projet de la nouvelle voiture de haut de gamme, projet connu sous le nom de code Y30.\n\n<p>Vous serez responsable de tout à chaque étape, depuis la conception de départ jusq\'à la mise en vente.\n\n<p>Pour cela, il vous sera nécessaire de faire preuve -- comme d\'habitude dans votre domaine -- de qualités de PERFECTIONNISME, de RESPONSIBILITE et de RIGUEUR.  Et vous devrez aussi, bien entendu, respecter les délais impartis.\n\n<p><b>C\'est de vos propres choix que dépendra votre succès dans cette grande aventure qu\'est la réalisation d\'une voiture...  Et à vos propres erreurs qu\'un échec serait imputable!</b>'),(9256,'User','You are a female fighter pilot on a dangerous mission.  This adventure requires some dice-rolling and score-keeping.'),(9258,'User','Your summer vacation is interrupted by magical happenings.'),(9260,'User','This entry concludes the story started in the previous issue.'),(9261,'User','This article discusses the history of <a href=\"/Series/11\">Fighting Fantasy</a>.  It is divided into sections representing years in the history of the series, and each section provides gamebook-style links to other sections (i.e. \"To find out what happens to the finished manuscript, turn to 1982\").'),(9313,'LC','A seventh-grade computer whiz solves ten puzzling cases using his knowledge of logic and computers.'),(9314,'LC','The reader is asked to supply the answers to eight mysteries which are solved by young computer whiz Chip Mitchell.'),(9340,'User','The reader is challenged to transform the word \"CAT\" into the world \"GOLD\" in 45 steps with no repeated words by applying a series of letter operations.  The book consists of linear text containing clues to the transformations.'),(9348,'LC','When King Tut\'s mummy vanishes while being sent from Egypt to a special exhibition in St. Petersburg, Russia, ACME detectives Ben and Maya set out to find the thief.'),(9402,'User','A brief Western-themed adventure.'),(9476,'User','You awaken in a prison cell in a damaged, zombie-infested building and have no memory of who you are.'),(9479,'LC','Presents a situation where a child is lost at the zoo and encourages critical thinking on the part of the reader to resolve the problem.'),(9480,'LC','A little girl considers seven different ways to get the toy she wants from her playmate. Includes questions about feelings and making choices as each alternative in the story is considered.'),(9481,'LC','A young boy considers eight ways to get someone to play with him. Text encourages problem solving by looking at alternatives and possible consequences.'),(9482,'LC','A little boy considers eight things to do while he waits to take his turn. Presents questions about behavior and feelings for an adult to ask the child as each alternative in the story is considered.'),(9483,'LC','Using a story about two friends, Jenny and Eduardo, explores the various ways Jenny might react when Eduardo calls her a dummy, and the consequences of her possible reactions.'),(9484,'LC','Illustrates the use of problem-solving skills, critical thinking, and conflict resolution through an example of mother-child separation.'),(9519,'User','This \"interactive \'Choose Your Own Kill\' gamebook\" is based on the <i>Hitman</i> video game series.  The reader is encouraged to play multiple times to meet a series of Challenges (similar to Xbox 360 Achievements).  '),(9584,'User','This very brief article provides a bit of history of the <a href=\"\"\"/Series/30\">Choose Your Own Adventure</a> series, including a section about gamebooks.org.'),(9644,'User','Together with your party of fellow adventurers, you must infiltrate and explore an ancient tomb in order to prevent an evil deity from being released onto your world.'),(9678,'User','This book contains a solitaire adventure, a two-player scenario, and role-playing material for game masters.'),(9680,'User','In what seems like a community of hobbits, Santa Claus has lost his sleigh and needs your help to find it.'),(9687,'User','Your uncle dies, leaving you his most prized possession: a map to a hidden valley in New Mexico that acts as a portal through time and space.'),(9690,'User','You are a young dragon, a \"dragonlark.\"  The queen has been kidnapped, and you want to help find her.'),(9730,'User','This gamebook-style adventure used simple web technology: the story was explored by clicking hyperlinks within the pages of text.  It was once available by commercial subscription, but the website (www.clinkadventure.com) no longer appears to be available.'),(9755,'User','Preparations for your first day of school are disrupted when you learn that multiple supervillains have just escaped from prison!'),(9756,'User','You are a dragon, you own a mysterious magic clock, and it\'s your birthday. Unfortunately, the local villagers are up to some mischief.'),(9757,'User','The disappearance of your best friend sets you on the trail of a mad scientist who is turning the city\'s residents into Frankenstein-like creatures.'),(9760,'LC','The reader\'s choices guide three teenagers as they explore the ruins of an amusement park with a shady history.'),(9802,'User','Flying Buffalo offers a service to create a character from your own photographs; there are probably a variety of custom books floating around as a result.'),(9826,'User','This set reuses the cover of the old <a href=\"/Item/823\">red box</a> Basic Set and includes a solitaire tutorial adventure.'),(9827,'User','\nThis short downloadable adventure continues the story begun in the Dungeons & Dragons 4th Edition <a href=\"/Item/9826\">Starter Set</a>. While recruiting help to recover the item stolen in that story, you run into an elf who offers you a side quest to enter a haunted tower and recover a magical sword stolen long ago by a now-dead evil paladin.'),(9849,'User','You are on a pirate ship seeking treasure.'),(9865,'LC','\"Describes the fight for survival while exploring the Sahara, Sonoran, and Gobi Deserts\"--Provided by publisher.'),(9867,'User','You can experience the sinking of the RMS Titanic as a surgeon\'s assistant, as a governess working for a wealthy family, or as a young boy travelling with your father. '),(9870,'User','You must undertake a mission for the United States Special Forces. You may choose to do it as a Green Beret, as an Army Ranger, or as a Navy SEAL.'),(9872,'User','You can try climbing the Kilimanjaro, the Matterhorn, or the Everest.'),(9876,'LC','\"Describes the people and events involved during the colonial years before the Revolutionary War. The reader\'s choices reveal the historical details from the perspectives of an indentured Virginia servant, a Massachusetts colonist, and a resident of Philadelphia just before the revolution\"--Provided by publisher.'),(9878,'LC','\"Describes the people and events involved in the Salem witch trials. The reader\'s choices reveal the historical details from the perspectives of an accused witch, the family member of an accused witch, and an accuser\"--Provided by publisher.'),(9879,'User','You can choose to be a Viking participating in the Lindisfarne raid, to campaign with Halfdan Ragnarsson across England, or to fight at the battle of Stamford Bridge. '),(9880,'User','As a samurai in feudal Japan, you may choose to fight in the Gempei War, to battle alongside Oda Nobunaga, or to have adventures as a wandering ronin. '),(9881,'User','You can choose to have adventures as a member of Spartacus\' revolt, as a young gladiator-in-training, or as a veteran gladiator.'),(9886,'User','Three stories from three different time periods:  In the first you can choose between being a soldier and a scholar during the first or Qin dynasty, a time during which the emperor has forbidden the teachings of Confucius.  In the second story you are a young girl/woman during the rule of Tang dynasty Empress Wu.  The final story is of a silk trader journeying to the western silk road city of Dunhuang to exchange fine silks for a jade statue desired by the Ming dynasty emperor.'),(9887,'User','You can choose to perform espionage and sabotage missions in World War II as a member of the Danish resistance, as an agent for the German Abwehr, or as an agent for the American OSS.'),(9888,'LC','\"Describes the role pilots played during World War II. Readers\' choices reveal various historical details\"--Provided by publisher.'),(9889,'User','During World War II, you can choose to be a German sailor aboard the ship Bismarck, a U.S. Marine stationed in Pearl Harbor, or a U.S. Navy sailor participating in the D-Day invasion.\n'),(9901,'User','This solo dungeon really was computer-generated, making each copy unique due to random rearrangement of elements.'),(9958,'User','This title may not have been produced under the Outlaw Press label, but it was self-published by Outlaw Press founder James L. Shipman II.'),(10009,'User','This article provides an overview of solitaire gaming, including gamebook-style diversions.'),(10012,'User','This review column covers early <a href=\"/Series/1466\">Dwarfstar Games</a> releases.'),(10019,'User','This issue includes interviews with <a href=\"http://www.gamebooks.org//Person/31\">Steve Jackson</a> and <a href=\"/Person/3468\">Michael Ward</a>.'),(10023,'User','This issue contains six mini-adventures plus some other articles.'),(10024,'User','This issue contains five mini-adventures plus some other articles.'),(10025,'User','This issue contains three mini-adventures plus some other articles.'),(10052,'User','A man has been murdered in his retreat, which is located in a remote Caribbean island. You lead a team of investigators to try to find out who did it and why.'),(10058,'User','A strange virus is killing the entire population. As one of the few survivors, you must brave the deserted countryside in order to find your family.'),(10063,'User','An evil wizard is planning to take over the world. As a warrior-mage, you must journey to his castle and destroy him.'),(10074,'User','You must locate and hunt down an evil leader who is planning to raise an army of werewolves\nand conquer the world.'),(10079,'User','An evil warlock has kidnapped a princess who is set to marry soon. You must locate and rescue the princess before the wedding is called off.'),(10108,'User','This book contains five short stories.'),(10113,'User','Created by Steve Jackson (UK), this beautifully-designed game captures the concept and encounters of its source material very well, but randomisation is generated by distributing Encounter and Treasure cards about the dungeon meaning that, in theory, no two playing dungeons can be the same and, crucially, making every playthrough unique. Adventure Sheets, dice, and six plastic miniatures are included. Several ideas not lifted from the book are also included to avoid this being a slavish copy of the original. A feature called Key Challenges allows players to attempt to establish what the correct three-number combination opens the Warlock\'s treasure chest at the end of the game (similar to Cluedo.)'),(10116,'User','This article introduces the popular role-playing game.'),(10118,'User','This letter column contains four submissions with questions and comments about the magazine and the <a href=\"/Series/11\">Fighting Fantasy</a> series.'),(10119,'User','This competition challenges readers to write a multi-player adventure for <a href=\"/Series/233\">Fighting Fantasy: The Introductory Role-Playing Game</a>.'),(10129,'User','This volume contains two items: one group adventure and one solo adventure.'),(10138,'User','You are Elisabeth, a young woman with an incredibly broad range of interests; unfortunately, the world is about to end.'),(10147,'User','Unofficial prequel to House of Hell.'),(10150,'User','This free download adds more options to <a href=\"/Item/8802\">The Wounded Falcon</a>; it cannot be played on its own.'),(10158,'User','This article looks back at <a href=\"/Series/30\">Choose Your Own Adventure</a> and gamebooks in general.'),(10179,'User','You are a young sleuth, the child of the Dallas police chief, and you have decided to investigate JFK\'s assassination!'),(10198,'User','You must command a starship on a secret mission.'),(10200,'User','Yet again the kingdom is in danger. A huge red dragon is on the loose, terrorising all who stand in its way. Its impenetrable hide, vicious claws and fiery breath make it a fearsome opponent.'),(10209,'Cover','You\'re a cat! It\'s a pretty peaceful life. But one day the man in the family you live with comes home feeling sick, passing out on the floor. When he awakes, he isn\'t the same. He tries to bite everyone! Quickly you\'re out the door with the others, who get into a car and beckon you to come with them, but this whole thing is frightening. Your thoughts stray to your girlfriend down the alley. What will you do? Inspired by the gamebook fad of the 80s - You Are a Cat in the Zombie Apocalypse! is the much anticipated sequel to the first book in the Pick-a-Plot series!'),(10211,'User','This booklet contains information about <a href=\"/Item/10179\">Who Killed John F. Kennedy?</a> in the form of a brief, humorous gamebook.'),(10213,'User','You are a god, and you must guide your people through a series of difficult challenges in order to establish a thriving civilization.'),(10215,'User','You are trapped inside a television, where you experience fantasy, science fiction or horror adventures.'),(10216,'User','You are an amnesiac with strange memories -- some of them alien!'),(10217,'User','You are Mudskipper, the detective; your first case involves a bank robbery.'),(10218,'User','You are a teenager granted superpowers by a mysterious rock.'),(10248,'User','While on vacation you see a flying saucer outside your window and decide to investigate.'),(10265,'User','On the way to the mining colony on the planet, Crag, your transport ship explodes. Fleeing in an escape pod, you and two other survivors must find safe harbor.'),(10266,'User','The kingdom of Paleth has been invaded by an army of animated skeletons commanded by the necromancer, Leto Nesk. Now it falls upon you to journey across a dangerous land in search of aid before all is lost.'),(10278,'Cover','You’ve risen through society after dealing with Eltane and saving the city, capturing the affections of the Duke’s daughter along the way. The mysterious death of a friend arouses your suspicions and once again you find yourself at the heart of conspiracy that takes you back to your home village and a meeting with your old adventuring party from your youth.'),(10279,'Cover','Your return to Rema takes you further to the east, to the City-State of Callae, renowned throughout the world as a city of great learning. Your final destination is the Emirates of Akbir, ruled by a sick Emir who has remained neutral to Orlandes’ political leanings over the years. His successor threatens to send that relationship into turmoil. You must secretly enter a harsh desert world of political power struggles and strange magics to ensure a stable future for both Rema and Orlandes!'),(10280,'Cover','Nurroth, north of Orlandes City, is often viewed as an uncultured den of pirates and thieves. As a professional thief yourself, you get more than you bargain for after completing your most recent job. Clearly, you’ve stolen something you shouldn’t have. The Nurrothian Lords are on your trail, and you’re soon caught in a political tangle between Nurroth and Falavia. But a thief’s life is never meant to be easy…'),(10281,'Cover','Travel to the secluded Isla des Misticos, home to the enigmatic Mystics. You are the daughter of the Earth Queen, leader of the Mystics, and find yourself in dire peril from the outset. As you uncover a plot to end your life, you also discover new magical abilities through the power of songs. Can you escape from your predestined fate?'),(10282,'Cover','In the remote Orlandrian coastal town of Casporur, home to the giant statues that rise out of the ocean called the Children of Asuria, something is amiss. The emissary from Orlandes City has been sending messages which are growing more and more alarming – they talk of tremors and civil unrest. When the emissary goes missing, it’s up to you to investigate the disappearance. A new darkness stalks the land. Is this the second coming of Asuria?'),(10283,'Cover','You are a clone raised by the mysterious Silene Monks. Once the guardians of peace and justice in the galaxy, they have long since been superseded by modern technology. Now they spend most of their time hanging out and playing video games.\n\nBut you are not like the rest of your clone brothers. You have been chosen for a special destiny. Make the right decisions and you’ll complete your training, explore a universe full of adventure, and prove yourself a hero. Make the wrong decisions and you’ll be dead. Really dead. Its hard to emphasise just how dead you will be. So here’s a pre tip for you: try to make the right decisions.'),(10284,'Cover','Believe me, because I know these things are there, lurking in the darkness for millennia, and ready to prey on us again.\n\nAfter receiving a desperate letter from one of your students, you become embroiled in a sinister mystery on the grounds of Miskatonic University. Their ancient stones are home to a dark, evil force. As you teeter on the edge of madness, you will discover an ancient, sinister cult. What are their intentions? And why has Philip Lewis gone missing?\n\nBe careful out there, keep your wits about you, and perhaps you will uncover the secret of the Sons of Uruzime.'),(10285,'Cover','You’re a stuffed bunny and it’s the end of the world.\n\nWhen you slowly catch onto the fact that your latest date is in fact, the newest member of the living dead, there’s only one thing to do – run! …or, should you hang around a bit longer? After all, this is probably the best a date has gone for you in a while. This choice (along with many others) are entirely up to you…\n\nZombocalypse Now is a comedy/horror reimagining of the choose-your-own-ending books you grew up with. You’ll be confronted with undead hordes, internet dating, improper police procedure, and the very real possibility that you’ll lose your grip on reality and wind up chewing the carpets.\n\nThe zombie apocalypse has never been this much fun.'),(10286,'Cover','Sector 106 of Mega-City One is short of senior Street Judges and only the most experienced Judges have been reassigned to fill this shortfall… foremost among them yourself, Dredd! What begins as a routine patrol arresting juves and skysurfers, turns into a race against time, as mysterious “Voices of Dredd” find their way into the hands of the local perps. Riding your Lawmaster bike and armed with your trusty Lawgiver, you must pit yourself against Sector 106’s brutal criminal underworld.\n\nQuick Dredd! The countdown has begun…'),(10291,'Cover','Choose your own path through the adventure of a lifetime in a post-apocalyptic wasteland filled with mutants, strange wasteland dwellers, gun duels, otherworldly artifacts, and more! Roll dice to fight your battles and avoid certain death in this sci-fi fantasy thriller!\n\nWestward Dystopia is the first volume in a series of interactive fiction gamebooks set in the post-apocalyptic world of tomorrow. Centuries ago a terrible war laid waste to humanity, irradiating the globe and changing the lives of those who would survive forever. This event came to be known as The Razing, and the specifics regarding its provenance have passed from history into the fickle realms of myth and legend.\n\nYou are an artifact hunter burdened under the weight of an unhappy past. You came of age while living in one of the few isolated cities left in the Wasteland--the technological marvel that is the city of Root. You were betrayed by your homeland and you fled, seeking solace in the pursuit of wires and gears unearthed with some hardship from a seemingly inexhaustible treasure trove. The wastes abound with secrets to uncover, but your time has nearly run out. History may be repeating itself. Some secrets should remain buried, while others are necessary to humankind\'s continued survival!\n\n- Original Art by Fighting Fantasy veteran artist Tony Hough and David White!\n- Open-ended design featuring numerous options for progression with six vastly differing endings (and one secret ending)\n- Storyline and character-oriented older teen/adult-level prose: Combat takes a back seat to choice and exploration.\n- Simple combat rules using easy-to-learn RPG stats and standard six-sided dice.\n- Upgrade your weapons and armor.'),(10292,'Cover','Choose your own path through this prequel adventure set in a post-apocalyptic wasteland filled with mutants, strange wasteland dwellers, gun duels, otherworldly artifacts, and more! Roll dice to fight your battles and avoid certain death in this sci-fi fantasy thriller!\n- Experience the beginning of a clash of cultures: A wasteland city slowly resurrecting the powers of technology VS a wasteland mutant tribe!\n- Infiltrate the mountainous fortress of Spire using stealth where possible and deadly force when necessary, in your very first mission: To rescue three young innocents.\n- You\'re not in it alone! A small group will infiltrate the Spire with you. A deadly sniper, a renowned technician, a solemn medic, and a deeply flawed brawler in search of redemption form your team.\n- Will you save the prisoners in time?\n- Uncover the bizarre secret behind the mutants\' oracle!\n- Witness the beginnings of a tribal civil war!\n\nSpire Ablaze may be played on its own, or as a companion to Book 1: Westward Dystopia. Each volume is its own adventure which adds to the overall story of this mysterious post-apocalyptic world!'),(10313,'Cover','Welcome to Legend of the Wayfarer! This is a game system which is used for a\nseries of short gamebooks where you character can explore a world of fantasy of\nmagic, grow your character and perform great deeds (of course, you can use this\nsystem for other things. There’s not a law against that. Yet).\nThe idea of the system is to be simple yet flexible. The idea of the gamebooks are to\nexplore and interact with the world around you.'),(10314,'Cover','The town of Deepbridge is holds many strange inhabitants and you have no idea what you might walk into. Yet, there are many rewards for the daring adventurer and this is the perfect place to begin your legend.'),(10315,'Cover','A man has been accused of a crime and faces exile unless you can prove him innocent. To do this, you must brave an ancient and mystical forest, under the control of the fickle and dangerous Faerie Lord and his subjects. Dare you enter?'),(10316,'Cover','Looking for company, you hire yourself out as a guard to a caravan. Little do you know however, what a cursed journey it will be. Can you survive the bandits, strange creatures and wild folk and finally make it back to the comforts of civilisation?'),(10317,'Cover','The world is littered with many ancient ruins holding magic and treasures beyond the understanding of humanity. They also hold many dangers. You have decided to find one of these ruins and liberate these treasures. However, despite been left uninhabited for hundreds of years, pernicious sorcery keeps these treasures protected.'),(10318,'Cover','Baron Rogaris’s lands seem like a quiet place to stay, but there is opportunity here. People have lost things and people need to find things. If you can find these items, it will become very profitable for you. Of you could end up dead and forgotten in a ditch. But that’s the life of an adventurer such as yourself.'),(10319,'Cover','You think that going to a tavern will result in you having a few ales and then\nheading to bed, but in Spireport, things are never that simple. Who knows\nwho you will meet in this town? Who knows where you will spend the night?\nWho knows if you will leave Spireport alive?'),(10320,'Cover','In the foothills lives a group of warrior monks who protect a nearby village\nwith their well-honed martial arts skills. If you can prove to them your worth,\nyou will also be able to learn their secrets. Stripped of all of your\npossessions and cast out into the mountains, you have to return to them\nwith a blue flower that only grows in one of the most inhospitable regions of\nthe mountains to learn their skills. Will you manage to prove equal to the\nchallenge, or will you not come back from your search?'),(10321,'Cover','The largest city of the north holds a vast selection of exciting adventures\nand strange locations to visit. Despite being a beacon of safety,\nWinterbridge, still has its dangers however. Will you be able to brave them\nand earn the rewards it could yield up?'),(10324,'User','An earlier draft entitled The Resurrection Girl was published online on 22nd May 2003.'),(10335,'User','Sequel to Ulysses Ai\'s amateur gamebook The Hypertrout.'),(10339,'User','Sequel to Ulysses Ai\'s amateur gamebook Contractual Obligation.'),(10343,'User','Based on BBC Tv\'s Bottom comedy series from the 1990s, this adventure was written in tribute to the late Rik Mayall.'),(10348,'User','Sequel to Richard Evans\' amateur gamebook A Shadow in the North.'),(10354,'User','Sequel to Ulysses Ai\'s amateur gamebook Planet of the Spiders.'),(10356,'User','Sequel to Tammy Badowski\'s amateur gamebook Grim Holiday.'),(10365,'User','Sequel to Ulysses Ai\'s amateur gamebook The Golden Crate.'),(10377,'User','Unofficial sequel to Revenge of the Vampire.'),(10382,'User','Forum project to write a collaborative gamebook section-by-section.'),(10385,'Cover','The Courts of the Principality of Shabak are as dangerous as its mountains or forests. To uncover a plot by secret conspirators to overthrow the rightful rulers of Bakulan and Shabak will require skill, cunning and the favour of the Gods. Will YOU overcome these shadows, or will YOU succumb to the night?'),(10385,'User','Sequel to Hugh Eldred-Grigg\'s amateur gamebook Midnight Deep.'),(10386,'User','Sequel to Hugh Eldred-Grigg\'s amateur gamebook Shadows of Steel.'),(10397,'User','Sequel to Ulysses Ai\'s amateur gamebook Wrong Way Go Back.'),(10404,'User','Sequel to Ulysses Ai\'s amateur gamebook The Dead World.'),(10406,'User','Sequel to Philip Sadler\'s amateur gamebook Hellfire.'),(10407,'User','Sophie Frost was only 7 years old when this was written!'),(10462,'User','Unoffficial sequel to Deadline to Destruction.'),(10463,'User','Unofficial sequel to Caverns of the Snow Witch.'),(10469,'User','The only mini-adventure included (to date) in Fighting Fantazine to use a system other than Fighting Fantasy. Instead, this adventure is based on Joe Dever\'s Lone Wolf series.'),(10478,'User','Unofficial sequel to Scorpion Swamp.'),(10479,'User','Unofficial sequel to Spectral Stalkers.'),(10497,'User','This collection of amateur gamebooks by various authors was assembled by Ulysses Ai. Five of the gamebooks had been previously available, but the remaining eight were specially written for this collection.'),(10498,'User','This collection of amateur gamebooks by Stuart Lloyd is accompanied by practical criticisms written by Lloyd giving an insight into his creative processes and his own perspective on his work.'),(10499,'User','Unofficial prequel to The Citadel of Chaos.'),(10500,'User','Unofficial sequel to The Citadel of Chaos. Not to be confused with The Beggar from Blacksand which is a different adventure.'),(10501,'User','Unofficial sequel to Trial of Champions.'),(10502,'User','Unofficial prequel to The Forest of Doom. One of the earliest amateur Fighting Fantasy gamebooks to appear on the internet, possibly even the very first.'),(10503,'User','Unofficial prequel to The Citadel of Chaos. One of the earliest amateur Fighting Fantasy gamebooks to appear on the internet, possibly even the very first.'),(10504,'User','Unofficial sequel to House of Hell.'),(10505,'User','Unofficial sequel to Trial of Champions. Only available to play online - adventure remains unfinished.'),(10506,'User','Unofficial sequel to Midnight Rogue.'),(10507,'User','Unofficial first prequel to Beneath Nightmare Castle.'),(10508,'User','Unofficial spin-off from Khare - Cityport of Traps and The Seven Serpents, to the point where it even cross-refers the player to sections within these two books in places.'),(10509,'User','Unofficial spin-off from Chasms of Malice. Another potential contendor for earliest amateur Fighting Fantasy gamebook to ever appear online, but there are differing views on the actual date of its first appearance which could be anywhere between 1998 and 2001.'),(10510,'User','Unofficial sequel to Island of the Lizard King.'),(10511,'User','Unofficial second prequel to Beneath Nightmare Castle. Acts as the sequel to another amateur gamebook, Nightmare Castle - Rise of Skarlos.'),(10512,'User','Unofficial sequel to Appointment with F.E.A.R.'),(10513,'Cover','Vonotar The Traitor still lives - can you survive the Ice Halls of Terror? You are Lone Wolf, the last of the Kai Lords. Shocking news has reached your homeland that Vonotar The Traitor still lives and now rules over the Ice Barbarians of Kalte. The King has just vowed to your people that Vonotar will be brought to justice for his crimes. But it is a promise that only you, Lone Wolf, can fulfil. In the ICE HALLS OF TERROR, you must brave the terrible dangers of the ice kingdom in your quest to capture your most hated foe. But be warned! It is a challenge that will test your skill and endurance to the very limit. '),(10517,'User','28 years after Out of the Pit, this second compendium of additional monsters was published.'),(10519,'User','This module for the Advanced Fighting Fantasy RPG system combines material from the gamebook, boardgame, and Nintendo DS versions of The Warlock of Firetop Mountain, as well as Return to Firetop Mountain.'),(10555,'User','Originally written using a bespoke system by the author as a Windhammer Competition entry, this was later re-worked using <a href=\"/Series/11\">Fighting Fantasy</a> rules in a play online version.'),(10556,'User','Originally written using a bespoke system by the author as a Windhammer Competition entry, this was later re-worked using <a href=\"/Series/11\">Fighting Fantasy</a> rules in a play online version.'),(10560,'User','Although this amateur gamebook is listed on Fightingfantasy.com it is not currently available and it is uncertain whether it was ever published online at all.'),(10561,'User','Although this amateur gamebook is listed on Fightingfantasy.com it is not currently available and it is uncertain whether it was ever published online at all.'),(10562,'User','Although this amateur gamebook is listed on Fightingfantasy.com it is not currently available and it is uncertain whether it was ever published online at all.'),(10563,'User','Although this amateur gamebook is listed on Fightingfantasy.com it is not currently available and it is uncertain whether it was ever published online at all.'),(10564,'User','Although this amateur gamebook is listed on Fightingfantasy.com it is not currently available and it is uncertain whether it was ever published online at all.'),(10565,'Cover','The sickest, darkest deeds were undertaken in the name of Hitler during World War 2. In this choose your own story adventure you are a U.S. Marine sent to investigate the strange reports from Nazi occupied Ukraine.\n\nReports from local operatives have sent chills down the spine of Allied Command and even days before you begin your mission you find yourself haunted by sinister dreams. Your objective is to parachute deep into enemy territory, infiltrate the hidden facility, find the truth and return alive.\n\nAs your plane approaches the objective, a freak accident leaves you left without supplies in hostile territory with only your training and wits to guide you.\n\nHere you are the hero and only you can decide which paths to follow in this interactive gamebook. Manage situations as they unfold. There are multiple paths through and multiple ways to die.\nCan you discover what monstrosities lurk in the darkness?\nCan you survive them?'),(10566,'Cover','With three times the size of Book I and deeper and more varied choices, you are invited to continue your mission. In this choose your own story adventure you find yourself deep behind enemy lines with the sick truth closer to you than ever before. Who can you trust, and what could possibly explain the madness that already lies behind you?\n\nAs you descend into the catacombs of the town, the full insanity of the Nazi plot starts to unravel. Technology combined with ancient mysticism is creating a weapon that threatens to win them the war.\n\nHere you are the hero and only you can decide which paths to follow in this interactive gamebook. Manage situations as they unfold. Multiple paths lead to multiple endings.\nCan you stop the weapon being built?\nCan you survive?'),(10567,'Cover','Lost Town is the first installment in a series of choose your own adventure style books—the first of many to come. It marks the beginning of The Wyldemere Chronicles, its pages following the subterranean exploits of Devon, Sara, and Fang.\n\nSubsequent books will introduce new characters, people such as Bulldirk, the one-armed blacksmith, Katie, the beautiful thief with a penchant for ruby rings and throwing knives, and Ashel, a blind mage whose tower has the unfortunate habit of transporting itself to random locations every other Tuesday—just to name a few. All books, regardless of storyline and characters, will be based in or around the lawless town of Wyldemere .\n\nThree hundred years ago:\n\nWyldemere is a thriving seaport, a haven for sailors on their way to the southern isles. It’s said that coin changes hands faster on Barter St. than women change their minds. In part due to the amenities which spring up during economic booms, and in part due to Wyldemere’s singular geographic location, it’s considered one of the top destinations on the continent.\n\nWyldemere is within a day’s ride of virtually every type of terrain imaginable: There are the Cragstone Mountains and Iron Caves to the South, the Dreaming Desert to the East, Deeperdelve Wood to the West, the Bogslump Swamps to the Southwest, the Gildoren Grasslands to the Southeast, and, of course, the Deedlebrine Sea and islands to the North. It’s said that if a person can’t find what they seek in Wyldemere, they can’t find it anywhere.\n\nTwo hundred years ago:\n\nNothing, as most people know, lasts forever. Least of all good fortune. Dark days of blood and tears are here. The beating drums of war have come to the peaceful kingdom of Lariella . Trenches are dug. Armor is donned. Bunkers are built. And new seaports with high walls topped by cannon are raised—the blue and gold flags snapping in the salty breeze of a new age.\n\nShortly after the dark and bloody days of war reach their dark and bloody conclusion, Lariella falls into economic collapse. Entire towns are all but leveled (including Wyldemere), and the royal coffers are empty. Few know how close the kingdom came to total annihilation at the hands of the Malkynie invaders—their barbarian neighbors to the east. Some say it will take generations to recover. Others say they never will.\n\nPresent day:\n\nWhat once was the thriving seaport of Wyldemere, is now a dingy, fading shadow of its former self, a sprawling, disorganized confusion of slouching buildings and twisting streets, a hodgepodge of new, old, and in-between construction. It has become one of those forgotten places, little more than a name on a map that most folks haven’t even heard of, a place for cutthroats and card sharks, conmen and drunkards, a place where one is either very rich or gutter poor, very lucky, very ruthless, or very dead.\n\nNot to suggest that Wyldemere is without its charms, mind you. After all, it’s still within a day’s ride of some pretty incredible locales. And the ruins beneath town are said to be a marvel, a shifting labyrinth whose unplumbed depths call to young men such as Devon, to those born on the wrong side of the divide (down by the docks), promising them, in sweet, singsong voices, that they’ll find the fabled halls of gold before the denizens of Lost Town find them.\n\nNeedless to say, most who go down there never come back out. And the ones who do rarely return with more than a few baubles, some bumps and bruises, and an empty stomach for their trouble. We can only pray that Devon, Sara, and Fang will be the exceptions to prove the rule. For you see, as chance would have it, that’s where they’re headed this very moment, straight into the gaping maw of high adventure, into a heady amalgam of sword and sorcery from which only the nimblest of mind and stoutest of heart shall return.\n\nIf you hurry, you just might catch them!'),(10568,'Cover','Greetings, sexual adventurer! Welcome a world of erotic potential where you, the reader, get to choose your path through a veritable dungeon of carnal possibilities! But select wisely, friend, because every wrong decision you make on the way to the shuddering climax of this erotic quest will lead to your gruesome death!\n\nDon’t just be a player, be a playa! This is fantasy roleplay in the truest sense, where the wildest desires you can imagine will come true (within reason). Life is a Sextrap Dungeon - are you ready to plunder its treasures?'),(10569,'Cover','The bombs have fallen, wiping out hundreds of millions in the blink of an eye. Law and order has crumbled, civilization has collapsed and warmongering nomads fight over what little resources remain. Radioactive fallout blows across the bleached wastelands of former cities, bringing mankind to the very brink of extinction.\n\nIt’s time to hit on some honeys!\n\nIn this erotic adventure you play the role of a post-apocalyptic booty hunter with a singular mission: to turn a total catastrophe into a total cat-ass-strophe! Don’t just be a player, be a playa! This is fantasy roleplay in the truest sense, where the wildest desires you can imagine will come true (within reason)! When there’s no more room in hell… the douche will walk the Earth.'),(10570,'Cover','You asked for it and now you\'ve got it! For the first time in Sextrap Dungeon history, you get to play an actual woman! That\'s right; Sextrap Dungeon: Clock Tease is a sex-positive story of female empowerment, so get ready for a hot injection.... of feminism!\n\nTime travel! Imagine being given a chance to travel into the days of yore and influence the events that changed history. To journey into antiquity and right mankind’s wrongs. To mold the shape of our present day and bring about a new utopia!\n\nNow forget all that guff and imagine getting dicked up and down by the very best history has to offer. Genghis Khan, Ramses the Great, Sigmund Freud, take your pick - ain’t no scrubs in these yesteryears!\n\nThis third standalone installment of the Sextrap Dungeon series is the best yet! It’s an erotically charged history lesson! It’s Bill and Ted meets Mills and Boon! It’s the ultimate page turner, or at least it would be if only the pages weren’t so damned sticky!'),(10583,'Cover','The year is 2078 and life in New America is rough.\n\nIn this Choose Your Own Adventure erotica you play as Aelia, a New America native whose life is changed forever when she encounters a mysterious outsider named James. Together you discover all the secrets that the Committee doesn\'t want you to find out! Discover sexuality for the first time in a dystopic land where love is forbidden.\n\nChoose whether to live an erotic life on the run or give your lover up.\n\nPick your path and control your adventure with Elodie Wood\'s debut science fiction erotica.\n\nFrom choices small (Does James have brown eyes?) to big decisions that could end the tale, this interactive erotica can be read again and again to find new branches and options. '),(10584,'Cover','This is an erotic story with a difference - in this tale YOU get to choose what happens! Modelled after the choose-your-own-adventure books of old, this is kinky literature for the modern age. Read through and select from the different options available to control the action. There are over thirty different strands and a dozen endings to this tale of BDSM domination.\n\nIn this interactive adventure, you\'ll go on a trip to a fully kitted-out dungeon with your submissive Jenna. Once inside, you\'ll be in control of everything from the clothes she wears to the punishments she receives. You even get to pick what kind of happy ending you want this story to have!\n\nIf you\'re tired of stories that don\'t quite pan out the way you want, or if you\'re simply a fan of kink in all its forms, then this is the book for you. Take control, and step into the dungeon to discover what happens next!'),(10585,'Cover','Choose your path in the erotic showdown between characters of the Dragon Age and Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic video game universes! Contains sexy scenes, only read if you are 18+! Features the following sexy pairings:\n\n~ Bastila Shan and Morrigan\n~ Mission Vao and Wynne\n~ Juhani and Leliana\n\nTaking place between Dragon Age Origins and Dragon Age 2, and between Star Wars KotOR 1 and 2, this adult parody allows you to guide the action with a fully interactive branching storyline. Spoofing a potential storyline where the characters of Star Wars KotOR enter the Dragon Age universe, you choose how various characters carry themselves both in and out of the bedroom.\n\nYou’ve heard of adult parody movies of popular films and tv shows. Now have the same experience, in erotica, with your favourite video game characters! Get your copy today and explore a thrilling and sexy parody, fully interactive! '),(10586,'Cover','The main character is a ruthless, ambitious, know-it-all brat, who attempts to knock the smartest student at the university, Mark, off his pedestal via blackmail. But Mark shows her what it really means to be ruthless, with his superior intellect and his insidious invention: The Ratchet! Now she has to suppress her arousal or find herself a blonde airhead bimbo!\n\nYou get to choose how the main character will deal with the consequences of her less than wise actions! The results are always hot and steamy!\n\nThis Choose-Your-Erotic-Adventure book contains themes of mind control, bimboization, nanobots, and graphic MF and FF sex.'),(10587,'Cover','In this serie of Interactive Erotica, I (the writer) am talking directly to you (the reader). You\'re a character in the story.\nIt\'s one of your closest friend and you had a crush on her for years. You keep being nice to her in the hope that one day she\'ll realize she likes you in that way. Here she finds out you still love her and will tell you bluntly why you\'re not the man she\'s looking for. Actually, in her eyes, you\'re not even a man. You\'re less than that. '),(10588,'Cover','An interactive story where I (the writer) tells you (the reader) what\'s happening. You\'re a character in the story.\nHere, you are a married woman on a business trip. I\'m a dark stranger who saw you walking in. I\'m the kind of man your mom warned you against, I have no pity and no clemency, I\'m ready to do everything in my power to satisfy my desire. Today, it\'s you. I want you and I\'m going to get you and I\'m going to tell it to you straight. I want you in my room right now. I don\'t know you but I\'m going to fuck you.'),(10589,'Cover','Kari’s BFF tricks her into attending a fetish expo, promptly losing her as they arrive. She can find her friend or maybe, just maybe find the secret to her own heart’s desires? Only a choice can open the door. If she dares.'),(10590,'Cover','A prisoner of the Roman Empire, you find yourself sold into slavery to the wealthy House of Felatius and the voluptuous Servilia, known throughout Rome for hosting wild parties and for her insatiable sexual appetites. Having caught her eye, you must keep in Servilia\'s good graces while also planning your escape.\n\nThis 50,000 word Erotic choose your own story puts you in control, utilising e-book technology to eliminate the page flicking of yesteryear and allow you to enjoy seducing beautiful slave girls, an exotic African woman, a curvaceous farmers wife, a sophisticated young noblewoman and the lusty Servilia herself. Featuring numerous paths to multiple endings and where leaving a woman unsatisfied will lead to a much more serious outcome than a cold shoulder!\n\nSpurtacus features several steamy sexual encounters including, in the best traditions of the Roman Empire at its most decadent, a full on orgy.'),(10591,'Cover','Do you ever read an erotica book and wish the main characters would have a threesome instead of a two way? Or that you could decide if they get it on in a strip club or while hiking in the woods? In this 25,000-word pick your erotic adventure, Matt, a Navy SEAL, and Lily, his long-time girlfriend, let you choose what sexual adventures they undertake. A sexual massage parlour or an erotic Sunday drive - you pick! '),(10592,'Cover','A tale of dark fantasy and transformation, wrapped around a puzzle with a prize for the first to solve it! John begins his day only to discover he is the star of a mysterious screenplay. On a whim, he begins to make edits, and finds the world around him changing to match.\n\nYou are in control. You choose his path through this strange and torturous journey, lost to temptation. What will happen? Can the world as we know it survive? In the end that is up to you.\n\nWritten using Inklewriter\'s interactive story creation software, this massive and sprawling story encompasses twenty five thousand words, hundreds of branches, and over 15 different endings. Including several secret, hidden endings. Find 3 for free product. Find them all and solve the puzzle for an amazing Grand Prize!'),(10593,'Cover','A tale of dark fantasy and transformation. Alice finds herself in a world gone mad, a world where some strange force is at work transforming women, all women, everywhere.\n\nYou are in control. You choose her path through this dark mirror of our world as she struggles against the terrible forces fighting to alter her, to claim her. What will happen to her? Who and what will she become? In the end that is up to you.\n\nWritten using Inklewriter\'s interactive story creation software, this massive and sprawling story encompasses twenty five thousand words, hundreds of branches, and over 24 different endings. Including one secret hidden ending for those with the luck or determination to find it.'),(10649,'User','Produced as a Limited Edition of 100 and available by internet mail order only, this merchandise set comprised a unique Lone Wolf ballpoint pen and an A4 numbered certificate with the lyrics to the Sommersang. Each certificate was hand-numbered and signed by Joe Dever. '),(10650,'User','Full-colour maps measuring 233mm x 328mm of the Lone Wolf world. Each is supplied signed by Joe Dever.'),(10651,'User','Advertised as \"A Game Kit for all Fighting Fantasy Players!\" this boxed set of useful gaming equipment contained two green dice, two embossed pencils with erasers, a pad of 50 Adventure Sheets, an iron-on transfer, and a pin-badge. Complete sets are very hard to find and this has become highly-prized by collectors.'),(10665,'User','A small pin-badge featuring Wizard Books\' revised FF logo.'),(10666,'User','Produced to tie-in with Wizard Books\' re-issues of the series, this 2004 Calendar featured the revised cover art from several of Wizard\'s editions.'),(10667,'User','Only available as part of the Limited Edition boxed set of EIDOS\' Deathtrap Dungeon PlayStation/PC game, this deck of 82 cards features characters from the game in a 4-8 player game based on the Chinese card game Zheng Shan Yu. '),(10668,'User','Adapted from the Fighting Fantasy book of the same name.'),(10672,'User','Produced by Otherworld Miniatures in a limited run of 1,000 pieces, this metal minituare is an accurate re-creation of Russ Nicholson\'s illustration of Zagor from The Warlock of Firetop Mountain. There are, in fact, two different versions: the first was available exclusively at Fighting Fantasy Fest in London on 7th September 2014 and has a stand and label reflecting this; the second is the standard retail version available from Otherworld\'s website which makes no mention of the FFF event.'),(10673,'Cover','In this Choose Your Own Adventure interactive erotica game, you play as the bachelor or bachelorette tasked with choosing the winning contestant through five rounds of personal and revealing questions. Will you finally discover your Perfect Date? '),(10674,'Cover','The world ended in a conflagration of atomic war. Even worse, a strange mutagenic virus has been spread across the globe mutating the survivors of the wasteland into impossible pulp fiction monstrosities. Most of the mutated people are driven by their basest needs: once their stomach is full they care only for fornication.\n\nBut Nita Redfield knows nothing about the Wasteland that now covers the earth. Daughter to one of the few lucky people who hid themselves inside massive Bunkers before the bombs dropped, she has grown up safe and untouched by the harsh and perverted world above her. But all of that is about to change. Calamity has struck her bunker, causing chaos and mutation all around her.\n\nYou get to make Nita’s choices as she learns to deal with the changes to her body, her libido, and the dangers that now lurk all around her. Can you lead her to the relative safety of the world outside of the Bunker, avoiding all the peril that now lies within its metal walls?'),(10675,'Cover','Champion Girl: The youngest, newest member of the Megatropolis Amazons. This indestructible youth, although still naive, packs a heavy punch. She stands, along with her sister Amazons, as defender of the Megatropolis and always able to defeat any foe in the end. But what would happen if she WAS defeated?\n\nIn this non canonical story set in the “Heroines Perilous World” you the reader get to choose what decisions Champion Girl makes during her first day of fighting crime in Megatropolis. Peril lies around every corner, with every decision you make leading to her first day ending in shame and defeat.'),(10676,'Cover','Archbaroness: founder and leader of the Megatropolis Amazons. Paragon of Megatropolis City. She stands as defender of the city, always able to defeat any foe in the end. But what would happen if she WAS defeated?\n\nIn this non canonical story set in the “Heroines Perilous World” you the reader get to choose what decisions Archbaroness makes during a normal day of fighting crime in Megatropolis. Peril lies around every corner, can YOU get her through the day without being defeated? More importantly do you even want her to go undefeated?\n\nThe choices early in the day can make a big difference, choosing between sending Archbaroness into her day with a mind clear of distracting sexual desire but with lowered powers or at her full power but with a mind addled by the cravings of her needy body. Keeping track of this behind the scenes Archbaroness has a hidden power and horny meter, each opening and closing certain options in the story.'),(10677,'Cover','Discovering her husband of 12 years has been visiting a stripper named Candy, will she try to rekindle the passion, or make an even bolder choice?'),(10678,'Cover','When a small plane crashes into an island paradise, only two of the thirteen passengers get to survive, which will it be? What will happen? How will the island paradise effect their ‘sextivities’?\n\nIt’s all to you to decide…'),(10679,'User','When a second year veterinary student is invited to spend a much needed summer vacation at her best friend\'s home the holiday starts off with a surprise... What will happen? That\'s up to you my darlings!'),(10680,'Cover','You\'ve never really gotten along with your Eastern European stepmother Irina - it\'s always felt to you like she\'s been looking down her nose at you since you met, and you suspect she\'s just after your father\'s money. When he passes away, she stuns you with a proposal - she\'ll fight you for it! The winner gets every last cent, and the loser will be lucky to escape with just a beating.\n\nYour fate is in your hands in this interactive story. Attack with punches, slaps, wrestling holds, and underhanded dirty moves. But your stepmother is no slouch; she wants that money, and she\'s ready to destroy you to get it. Choose your moves wisely wisely and you\'ll find yourself with a fortune and your beautiful stepmother as your plaything; choose poorly and you\'ll be at her mercy - if she has any.....'),(10685,'Cover','Every year on our anniversary my husband, Liam, does something extra special to show how much he cares about me, and it’s always something naughty. After six years of raising the bar I can’t wait to find out what he has planned for our seventh anniversary. He knows all about my fantasy to share him with another woman, but he’s already turned down the perfect opportunity once. Maybe someday he’ll be ready for the adventure. Maybe tonight’s the night. Anything can happen.'),(10686,'Cover','Married young, recently divorced, she thinks she\'s ready to get back in the game. But when she receives an invitation to an exclusive, adults-only club, she wonders is she ready for this?'),(10688,'Cover','The story begins with beautiful and overworked Kari going home after a dreadful day at the office. But what happens then? Does she get trapped in the elevator with the dreamy supervisor Forbes, or will the rugged janitor seduce her? And then what?'),(10689,'Cover','After a memorable stay at the Society for Erotic Adventures with her husband, Joss returns on her own to begin her new job as staff writer for the hotel. Upon her arrival, she learns that most staff members are initiated, not trained. Seeking an interesting angle for her story -- and more curious than she might like to admit -- Joss puts herself, her safety, and her marriage in Serafina¹s strange and possibly magical hands. Joss\'s initiation reunites her with the charismatic and mysterious Tilson, and she embarks on an adventure more powerful and more dangerous than she ever anticipated.'),(10690,'Cover','Stowing away on a merchant ship after her escape from the harem at Topkapi Palace, Layla finds herself captured by a band of women pirates with a supernatural secret.'),(10691,'Cover','Alyssa just inherited a castle, heated by an underground hot spring. It\'s her first night and she decided to spend it alone and explore. You choose what rooms she will explore; will she visit the pool? the kitchen? the bedroom? Maybe you\'ll even discover that Alyssa isn\'t as alone as she thought.'),(10693,'User','A Limited Edition metal \"slotta\" miniature produced by Citadel Miniatures in the mid-1980s. Based on the cover image of Warlock magazine issue 10 drawn by John Blanche, itself a re-working of a reader-submitted competition-winning entry to draw the \"Warlock\" himself.'),(10694,'User','A green pencil with built-in green eraser sold to promote the release of the You Are The Hero coffee table book.'),(10695,'User','A book-shaped eraser sold to promote the release of the You Are The Hero coffee table book.'),(10696,'User','A pair of dice (one black, one white) sold to promote the release of the You Are The Hero coffee table book.'),(10697,'User','Produced by Citadel Miniatures, this was a separately-available blister pack of all six plastic miniatures that were originally included with The Warlock of Firetop Mountain board game.'),(10703,'User','This app draws together all four volumes of Herbie Brennan\'s Demonspawn series into one digital gamebook.'),(10705,'User','Step into the backyard fighting zone - a small circle of grass where the crowd has gathered to watch you box. Today you\'re the hero of a choose your own adventure erotic boxing story - the world\'s first and probably only male/female interactive erotic boxing novel.'),(10736,'User','A bear has been killing your neighbour\'s chickens, and she asks you for help killing it.'),(10744,'User','You enter a tavern in search of adventure (as usual).'),(10755,'User','You have been assigned to explore an ancient ruin located in an uninhabited planet.'),(10757,'User','A friend of yours has been sentenced to death for the murder of the son of a feudal lord. In order to prove your friend\'s innocence, you must track down the evil creature responsible for the deed and slay it.'),(10758,'User','Given away free to all attendees of Fighting Fantasy Fest on 7th September 2014 in London, this pack of FF-related merchandise contained: an event programme, an exclusive version of the Otherworld Miniatures metal Zagor mini-figure, a Pax Britannia novel (by Jonathan Green), a code to get a free download of Tin Man Games\' Temple of the Spider God app for Android, a postcard of the cover art from Wizard\'s Series 1 re-issue of Forest Of Doom, two dice, and a Wizard Fighting Fantasy book. A special version was given to those who purchased the first 100 tickets to the event, which contained the Wizard 25th Anniversary hardback edition of The Warlock Of Firetop Mountain (signed By Steve Jackson and Ian Livingstone) and a glossy A3 poster commemorating the event. All this came contained in a yellow backpack with the FFF event logo printed on it.'),(10759,'User','\nYou must handle another day at the job you hate as best as you can. Can you even get out of bed?'),(10760,'Cover','You were born at Queen\'s Hospital in Romford, on February 25th 1990. \'Congratulations, it\'s an Essex girl!\' announced the midwife. So begins your glittery, glam and G-stringtastic life as Shampayne Sullivan. What happens in her story? You decide.'),(10763,'User','A large format poster book of Lone Wolf art by Gary Chalk. Complete copies (in fact, copies full-stop!) of this beautifully-illustrated art book are incredibly rare and sought-after by collectors.'),(10764,'User','This 330ml Lone Wolf mug features the official Lone Wolf logo and title.'),(10765,'Cover','You are a couple months out of your mother\'s belly. You\'re brand new! You don\'t even have a name yet. Well you do -- but it\'s not very nice. The couple that own you fight all the time. So much so that to hurt the other person, one of them stuffs you in a plastic bag and flings you into the canal! As the bag begins to fill with water colder than you\'ve ever experienced, a wild panic grips you!If you decide to claw your way out, scrabble furiously to page 16. If you decide to just stay still and do nothing, curl into a fetal ball on page 8. Or you can simply cry out for your mommy on page 6. The choice is yours! But don\'t take too long to decide. The water is already up over your paws, and the only warm thing you have to cling to is the memory of your mother\'s tongue licking the back of your head. Inspired by the gamebook fad of the 80s You Are a Kitten! is the alarmingly charming prequel to the cult hit You Are a Cat! and its sequel, You Are a Cat in the Zombie Apocalypse! Lavishly illustrated from the first-person feline floor purrspective, this thrilling and thoughtful finale brings the saga of Holden Catfield to a stunning and unforgettable conclusion.'),(10766,'User','Stephen receives a phone call from his cousin Laura. Her father, Miles, has disappeared. Intrigued by this, Stephen and Laura take the train to the West Country of England. Miles\' cottage has been ransacked and asomeone has been rummaging through all of Miles\' belongings. Stephen and Laura, decide to start tidying things up and, as they do so, they uncover a strange tin box which contains a map and a curious stone which glows. The mysterious Quince suddenly appears and informs the pair that the map is for a nearby tin mine. Quince promises to guide Stephen and Laura through the mine in return for the glowing stone. Wasting no time, they set off into the mine and come across a brick wall which appears to have been built recently. It\'s blocking their path... \nAt this point the interactive daily phone-in part of the story began.'),(10771,'Cover','Knightmare: Shadow Of The Opposition is a post-Series 8 adventure where Lord Fear has rebuilt his dungeon and reassembled most of his henchmen, causing Treguard to send YOU as his dungeoneer to put another stop to the technomancer\'s evil ways.'),(10786,'Cover','On an abandoned moon base, the Twelfth Doctor discovers a flesh-eating horror that leaves only the bones of its victims behind. Can the Doctor stop this monstrous being before it\'s too late?'),(10789,'User','On your way to your birthday celebration in a remote area, your plane crashes into a jungle. Can you escape from the jungle with your life or will you perish while exploring the ancient ruins located therein?'),(10795,'User','While trekking through a forest you come upon the tracks of a wild boar, and you decide to hunt it down for glory.'),(10802,'User','This gamebook contains four separate detective mysteries: The Case of the Unholy Ghost, The Mystery of the Morgue Marauder, The Mystery of the Murdered Marvellous Mask, and The Thief of Memories.'),(10818,'User','A set of seven different designs of badge sold to promote the You Are The Hero coffee table book.'),(10819,'Cover','It\'s challenging, exciting, <i>and</i> educational! This book contains 20\nstories and over 50 programs that can be used on Apple, Atari, Timex,\nCommodore or other home computers. So simple to understand, even\nan eight-year-old can program the computer--and become absorbed\nin an exciting story at the same time. THE MYSTERY AND ADVENTURE\nCOMPUTER STORYBOOK is loaded with clues that the child\nprograms into the computer. He is rewarded with exciting graphics\n(maps, mazes, coded messages) that will unravel the sequence of\nmysterious events. These stories combine text and computer programs\nto create a variety of fun, interesting plots. Programs that are\nsimple enough for an eight-year-old, stories challenging enough for a\ntwelve-year-old--that\'s how the MYSTERY AND ADVENTURE\nCOMPUTER STORYBOOK introduces your child to the wonders of\nthe computer <i>and</i> keeps him interested in reading.\n\n<p>The authors, Stuart and Donna Paltrowitz, are the creators of the\n<i>Mystery Maze</i> and <i>Close Escapes</i> series of computer software.'),(10851,'User','A 16-page supplement for Star Bastards giving additional information on its worlds, species, etc.'),(10860,'User','Two different versions exist of this boxed set, one in white and one in light pink.'),(10861,'User','Unofficial prequel to Deathtrap Dungeon.'),(10885,'User','The mayor of your hometown has promised you a reward if you can slay the evil creatures that dwell in a nearby dungeon.'),(10917,'Ad','The Brotherhood is a secret society of scholars that guards the knowledge accumulated by humanity over the centuries; wherever there is a great library, one of its members is nearby. However, they have yet to gain access to the Alhambra library, which holds the extensive and valuable scientific heritage of the Arab world.'),(10931,'User','Someone is killing a group of burlesque dancers, one by one. You must find out who the killer is and stop him or her.'),(10945,'User','While escorting a merchant wagon traveling through the wilderness, you are ambushed by a pack of goblins. You must fend off the attack and find the goblins\' lair in order to recover a stolen item.'),(10946,'User','This Limited Edition hardback single volume contains the 2nd edition core rulebook, the Out Of The Pit bestiary, and the Titan sourcebook. '),(11016,'User','French publisher Scriptarium produced this 35mm resin miniature in a certified Limited Edition run of 200 in early 2017.'),(11026,'LC','\"What if you, as a girl trying to adjust to her new stepfamily, suddenly found yourself in Samantha\'s world at the start of the 20th century? Join Samantha on exciting adventures. Your journey back in time can take whatever twists and turns you choose, as you select from a variety of options in this multiple-ending story.\"--Provided by publisher.'),(11035,'User','You can choose to play Greek hero Odysseus as he faces the cyclops Polyphemus, as he encounters the witch Circe, or as he confronts the would-be-usurpers of his throne in the island of Ithaca.'),(11049,'Cover','Rise of the Shadow King is a Dungeon Saga Adventure Gamebook in which YOU are the Hero. Set in the fantasy world of Mantica, you can immerse yourself in a quest to defeat the Shadow King, master of undeath. This is a classic adventure where you have plenty of opportunity to battle the undead denizens of Mantica, travel across plains, swamps, forests and an ancient fortress as you journey towards your ultimate goal. You might even stumble upon a Zombie Troll!'),(11072,'User','A virus has exterminated nearly all of mankind. As a survivor, you must face several dangers, including armed brigands and genetically-engineered creatures.'),(11075,'User','The computers of the world have become self-aware, and are looking to destroy mankind. You must find a way to help humanity survive, and probably even to stop the uprising.'),(11089,'User','You can participate in the building of the American Transcontinental Railroad as a Chinese laborer, as an Irish laborer, or as a railroad engineer.'),(11112,'User','Choose to be a Japanese-American spying on the Japanese in the Phillippines, a member of Women\'s Auxillary Air Force operating a wireless transmitter in occupied France, or a pilot flying a spyplane over occupied Europe.'),(11113,'LC','\"Explores various perspectives on espionage in World War I. The reader\'s choices reveal the historical details\"--Provided by publisher.'),(11113,'User','Choose to be a repatriated German-American spying and committing sabotage for the fatherland, a woman in occupied Belgium spying for \"La Dame Blanche\" or a British agent spying on the Russians after the fall of the Tsar.'),(11114,'User','You can choose to be a spy for the revolutionary \"Culper spy ring,\" a woman spying for the British or a slave spying with hopes of earning his freedom.'),(11115,'LC','\"Explores various perspectives on espionage in the Civil War. The reader\'s choices reveal the historical details\"--Provided by publisher.'),(11115,'User','Choose to be a member of the Pinkerton group spying for the Union, a southern woman who lives in the north and is spying for the confederacy, or a slave who spies for the north while working in a confederate military camp.'),(11120,'User','You visit a research lab where dinosaurs have been brought back to life. Due to an accident, two of them escape, and you get to help try to recapture them before anyone gets hurt.'),(11128,'User','You can experience the Vietnam war as a U.S. Marine, as a young Vietnamese man who is being forced to choose a side in the war, or as a young American man who has to choose between being drafted or opposing the war.'),(11141,'User','It\'s been a few months since the events in the <i>Inside Out</i> film. As Riley prepares for a new day at school, Sadness is put by mistake on a train to the Mind World. You can choose to play Sadness as she tries to return to the Emotions\' headquarters, or the other Emotions as they have to figure out the day without Sadness\' help.'),(11145,'User','A pair of dice (one red, one green) sold to promote the release of the You Are The Hero coffee table book.'),(11150,'User','<p>The second of TeleText\'s three Knightmare-based FastText adventures was presented by Channel 4 on 22nd December 1993 and took a Christmas theme by being set in Winteria.\n<p> This adventure was retrieved from VHS and reconstructed by Mark Lain and Paul Kelly in August 2017 to be playable online using the same four-colour system, but now presented as mouse-clickable options. This version can be accessed here: http://www.castleteletext.com/pages/Page%20458.htm'),(11186,'Ad','Starship Deadfall is a science fiction adventure gamebook in which the reader plays as the main character, having to make choices, battle adversaries and much more.\nThis first book in the Bionic Agent series takes place aboard a Xeno-Biological Research starship which is under attack by a rival faction known as the Leading Weapon Syndicate.\nYou the reader get to choose to play as a character from one of several factions, arm yourself with weapons and gadgets, explore the starship and complete various missions.\nMassive in scope and huge replay-ability, this is a sci-fi adventure in which YOU the reader determine how the story unfolds and whether or not you complete your mission or survive.'),(11195,'User','Participate in three major realms: in the air, on the ground and at sea.  Within those realms are two or more choices respectively: be an observer or a pilot of an aeroplane, operate artillery or a machine gun or a tank, go aboard a British submarine or dreadnought.'),(11196,'User','Choose from the battles of Stalingrad, the Bulge and Okinawa.  Within those battles you can choose (respectively): German infantry or Russian tank division, a couple different roles in the USA 101st Airborne Division, a US Navy fighter pilot flying either F6F Hellcat or F4U Corsair.'),(11197,'User','Three main story paths: the battle at Shiloh, the battle at Chattanooga and several different engagements with cavalry.  Six sub-choices, being either Union or Confederate infantry, artillery or cavalry.'),(11198,'User','Three story paths (battles): Bunker Hill, Saratoga, King\'s Mountain.  Six different characters to play: Colonist, British Soldier, Nanny to the children of a Hessian general, drummer boy, member of loyalist militia and member of patriot militia.'),(11230,'User','Texas, June 1865, 2 months after the U. S. Civil War has ended.  Federal troops arrive to enforce the emancipation proclamation, which freed the slaves in the Confederacy.  There are three stories in which you play a former slave in Texas.  You can be a single man who finds himself free and can then decide whether to stay where he was or to leave, a young girl who wants to travel to Arkansas to find her mother, or a young boy who is encouraged to leave school and work on a farm to support his family.'),(11234,'User','The planet Earth is in chaos because of the pit people, imaginary people who have arrived to eat all of the letters from words. Jorge and Alice, two smart young people, must adventure in the Country of Imagination to find a solution to  the world\'s problem, or else watch the fall of humanity in the near future....'),(11239,'User','This appears to be a promotional poster given to stores carrying the <i>Ace of Aces</i> product line.'),(11243,'Cover','Spezial-Abenteuer für die Deutschen Spielertage \'84.'),(11264,'User','This is a joint publication sharing the titles of two different fanzines.'),(11270,'LC','Poison Ivy takes over a seed bank filled with the world\'s most historical and priceless plant seeds. With your help, Batman will stop the Seed Bank Heist!'),(11271,'LC','At a Gotham City charity event, the Riddler kidnaps several wealthy guests and demands a huge ransom. With your help, Batman will solve the puzzle of The Riddler\'s Ransom!'),(11272,'LC','Mr. Freeze blankets Gotham City in a blizzard, turning the city into an enormous snow globe. With your help, Batman will melt the super-villain\'s Summer Freeze!'),(11273,'LC','The Joker transforms dozens of Gotham City citizens into laughing (and robbing) fools! In this interactive story, YOU CHOOSE the path Batman should take. With your help, he\'ll take down the Joker\'s Dozen!'),(11274,'LC','A wave of crime has hit Gotham City and the ferocious Bane is behind the spree. With your help, Batman will solve the puzzle of the Super-Villain Smackdown!'),(11277,'LC','Years ago actor Matt Hagen\'s career was ruined when he became the monstrous Clayface. Now he\'s back for revenge! Only you can help Batman track down and stop the dangerous shape-shifter in Clayface Returns!'),(11285,'User','This version of the book includes an exclusive campaign taking place in Salamonis, the Black Tower, Chalice, Oldcastle, Stonebridge and the Darkwood, illustrated with\nexclusive new Russ Nicholson art and some maps (Black Tower,\nSouth-Eastern Allansia).'),(11286,'User','This translation of the book includes a campaign taking place in Lendleland and Analand (including some new maps by Steve Luxton), additional rules, and several exclusive illustrations by Malcolm Barter, Russ Nicholson, John Sibbick and Bill Houston. The five maps in the folder are in color and give all the known Titan geographical data, including some exclusive Steve Jackson and Jonathan Green area names.'),(11287,'User','This translation includes new rules, two bonus adventures in which you can play a Jib-Jib chaser or a Marsh Hopper, and as in the other books in the series, many new illustrations (around 100), many by Malcolm Barter,\nRuss Nicholson, Alan Langford or Tony Hough, including some in colour.'),(11288,'User','This is a game master screen bundled with an original French-language game-mastered adventure.'),(11300,'User','Get ready to live breathtaking DEZAVENTURAS! Take on the role of the main character in this thrilling gamebook and challenge your limits! Defeat creatures, find treasures, unlock puzzles, explore scenarios, save the world and be the hero!\nOnly YOU can invade the Red Fortress, escape from the Dread Forest and destroy the Symbol of Evil. Make a Risk Delivery and explore the Dark Castle; eliminate the Black Cloak, perform a Relentless Escape, and put an end to the Terror Express; survive the Storm of the Dead and win the Metal Inferno.\n\n<p>But be careful! Danger lurks on every page! Can you muster courage and determination enough to achieve your goals and achieve victory? Fate is in your hands! Embark on this journey and dive into DEZAVENTURAS!'),(11318,'User','Two different translations of this story exist; at this time, it has not been determined which translation is present in which edition of any given collection.'),(11339,'User','As a medieval knight, you must protect your king from an enemy plot to kill him and take over his throne.'),(11386,'User','This base set includes everything needed to play with the SPAGS system, including an introductory mini-adventure. Additional adventures can be added to expand player options.'),(11406,'User','The reader makes choices to determine the fates of three protagonists in three separate narratives: Helen, Jed and Saunders. The narratives are connected, with overlapping characters.'),(11406,'Ad','A group of stories in which the reader, at the climax, is made to consider the consequences and choose between them. The fun is in seeing how the story works out. \"The most amazing combination of parlor game and fiction that has yet been published.\"--Boston Transcript.'),(11407,'User','The reader answers questions in order to receive a fortune. The book is divided into four sections, each with its own set of questions: \"Your Past,\" \"Your Future,\" \"You Can Change Your Fate\" and \"Let\'s Make Money.\"'),(11409,'User','The reader answers questions in order to select a paragraph psychoanalyzing him- or herself. There are separate sets of questions for men and women.'),(11411,'Cover','The year is 1881, and New York society awaits the marriage of handsome bachelor Lancelot Darling and beautiful bank heiress Lilly Lawrence. It is a love match made in heaven, and a joining of two splendid fortunes. What could possibly go wrong?'),(11411,'User','This gamebook is an interactive retelling of Mrs. Alex. McVeigh Miller\'s 1881 melodrama, <i>The Bride of the Tomb</i>.'),(11413,'User','BMO decides it\'s time to go off and have an adventure of his own; danger ensues.'),(11478,'User','The years since Autarch Sejanoz\'s death have been eventful indeed, with both the construction of a second Kai Monastery in southern Magnamund and a dramatic surge in attacks from the various factions of evil. The Kai Grand Masters are all assigned vital missions to keep your allies from being overrun, with yours being to safely recover part of a magical weapon before it can be claimed by an evil wizard.'),(11520,'User','Ally Motbey has always let her bossy bestie Cat call the shots in their friendship. Now that they\'re in high school it looks like Cat will continue to get her way. Should Ally join an advanced Latin class or audition for the school musical? You decide! '),(11521,'User','Phoebe Wright and her besties, Annabel and Kimmi, have been invited to the coolest party of the year! Unfortunately, it\'s the same night as her movie-night fundraiser. Should she go to the party or the movie night? You decide!'),(11522,'User','School has finished and it looks like Frankie Jones will be having a boring summer with only her guitar for company. Frankie is invited to spend time in London with her heart-breakingly cute British friend Jack. Frankie is also invited to a beach holiday with her dad. Should she go to England to meet her ex or should she holiday with her dad and his new girlfriend? You decide!'),(11523,'User','For months, Kitty MacLean has had a crush on Rio Sanchez who is probably the cutest guy in the world. Kitty goes camping with her besties and finds out Rio just happens to be staying nearby. Should she meet up with him? Should Kitty ditch her friends to hang out at the beach with popular girl Persephone instead? Will Rio even like Kitty? You decide!'),(11524,'User','When it comes to netball, Edie Thomas is a natural. She’s only ever played for fun and to hang out with her netball-mad bestie Tess. But when Edie makes the state team, it looks like netball will be taking centre stage. Should Edie drop out of the team and take a lead role in Romeo and Juliet with her long time crush Freddy or should will she resent netball taking over her life? You decide!'),(11530,'User','\"The Master Cat; or, Puss in Boots\" is a 16th century Italian fairy tale made famous by Charles Perrault. In this version of the tale, YOU are the master cat and must \"choose your fairy tale\".'),(11531,'User','\"Tortoise Triumphant,\" also known as \"The Tortoise and the Elephant\" or \"The Tortoise, The Elephant, and The Hippo,\" is a traditional tale from Africa. It has been told perhaps for centuries. In this version of the tale, YOU are the tortoise and must \"choose your fairy tale\".'),(11532,'User','\"The Frog Prince\" (originally titled \"The Frog Prince; or, Iron Henry\") is a German fairy tale first recorded by the Brothers Grimm in 1812 and first translated into English in 1823 by Edgar Taylor. In this version of the tale, YOU are the Frog Prince and must \"choose your fairy tale\".'),(11549,'User','Can you survive the satanic evil that lies within the abbey?'),(11555,'User','Can you survive battle singlehandedly against the odds to rescue a resistance leader captured by the Gestapo?'),(11559,'User','This academic text references <a href=\"/Series/1270\">Fighting Fantasy software</a> on pages 91-92 and the <a href=\"/Series/1270\">Tunnels and Trolls</a> computer adaptation on pages 192-193.'),(11573,'User','You arrive home to discover your wife and son have been kidnapped. Can you, an enthusiastic driver of a new Saab 9-3 SportWagon, solve the clues and find your family before it\'s too late?'),(11577,'LC','In this adventure a giant has to figure out what to do with an annoying human boy named Jack who climbed up a beanstalk: send him back, put him to work, or eat him -- and the choice is up to the reader.'),(11605,'User','Beyond the Morning Mountains is a two-part fantasy adventure in which you travel across a section of the continent of Quahnarren. Volume One sees you travelling from your home near Ustahm down to the major city of Balquis; Volume Two completes the adventure by taking you over the Morning Mountains to the coastal town of Liust.<BR><BR>\n\nAn exploration game where you must manage provisions, coins and health to survive the journey, you are asked to navigate through wild lands and urban environments, encountering the peoples, creatures and spirits of this ancient land. Personal values are improved by acquiring new weapons and equipment, dice tests against your Expertise and Perception values will determine your fate in a variety of situations and encounters, and the battle process involves the use of momentum, which allows both combatants to benefit from lucky dice rolls to then inflict greater damage from a powerful Heavy Attack.<BR><BR>\n\nAvailable in print as either a full-colour or black & white edition, or as a full-colour pdf.'),(11606,'User','A special companion document to help players safely navigate Volume One of Beyond the Morning Mountains. This pdf contains five RARE items not available within the adventure, offering multiple special abilities and bonuses.<BR><BR>\n\nPersonalise your character, increase your chances of successfully defeating adversaries, improve your fortune and gain the favour of the gods. Choose just one and hope that the dice roll in your favour!'),(11621,'User','A guide to the King\'s Quest series (computer game) including development information, hints for the series and maps.'),(11622,'User','A guide to the King\'s Quest series (computer game) including development information, hints for the series and maps.'),(11623,'User','A guide to King\'s Quest VII (computer game) including development information, hints for the series and maps.'),(11628,'User','A character corrupted by the desire for revenge plans to destroy Minecraft! Devious_David removed the rock matrix, the base of the entire surface of the game, and created a void that is increasing and devouring everything around it. Now Steve and his friends need your help to fight the forces of evil and save the virtual world. Only you can stop this terrible villain and prevent Minecraft from disappearing forever. Part story, part game, The Digital Enemy is a different kind of book - here, YOU are the hero!'),(11686,'User','This book is actually numbered \"zero\" and seems to serve as a prequel to a series intended to consist of twelve numbered books.'),(11700,'Cover','This text is adapted from an essay from \"Tardis Eruditorum\", a critical history of the television series\"\'Doctor Who\". This book was originally an essay for \"Logopolis\", a 1981 story best known for being the last to feature Tom Baker as the Doctor. While most of the book is entirely rewritten from the original version, the beginning of that esssay has been retained. (p. iii)'),(11705,'User','This first book in the series also contains the text of the unnumbered prequel <a href=\"/Item/11704\">Super Hero Creation Solo</a\">.'),(11713,'User','Trapped in a 80’s era haunted video arcade, Midnight Arcade is a play-your-way adventure tale in which the reader determines the course of action, ultimately controlling whether they live or die!'),(11719,'Cover','Destiny’s Role are books with a difference, books where YOU get to play the part of the hero, books that are both novels and games.\nThe four short books that form this collection are designed as an introduction to some of the concepts of Destiny’s Role:\n\n- Pit yourself against the greatest jousters in the region to win the right to be named MASTER OF THE TILTYARD\n\n- Assume the role of a hard-boiled film noir detective in your deadliest case yet as you try to unlock the secret of FRAGILE BEAUTY\n\n- Be faced with more than you had reckoned for as you head deep into the inner sanctum of THE CULT OF THE BLACK FEATHER\n\n- And step into the waking nightmare of CELTIC FROST\n\nTo play the adventures in this book you will need two six-sided dice, a pencil, an eraser, and, most importantly, an imagination!'),(11743,'User','This roleplaying game consists of three \"tomes\" which are gathered in one volume. The second \"tome\" consists of a mini-adventure that can be played by one or more players.'),(11744,'User','The supplement of this roleplaying game consists of four \"tomes\" plus \"extras\" which are gathered in one volume. The fourth \"tome\" consists of a mini-adventure that can be played by one or more players. '),(11770,'User','This gamebook is intended to be read by two players.'),(11779,'User','This item serves as a prequel to the three main volumes and was initially distributed on Free RPG Day 2018.'),(11780,'User','Boxed set in a slipcase containing the first three Corgi paperback editions.'),(11797,'User','You have been drugged and sold into slavery to a band of drow elves living in the Underdark. You must escape your captors and find a way out of the subterranean complex.'),(11798,'User','You are a halfling thief. One day you are caught trying to pick the pocket of a Lord of Waterdeep, and as punishment you are forced to locate and rescue a kidnapped baby griffon.'),(11799,'User','You are an elven magic-user living in the Forgotten Realms. One day a band of giants attacks your home. You must flee to safety and, if possible, find a way to be reunited with your family. '),(11800,'User','You\'re a dwarven cleric. You journey to a tropical jungle in western Faerun on a mission to recover a powerful magic ring.'),(11818,'User','Sherlock Holmes and his rival Irene Adler embark on two mysteries (a murder case and the disappearance of Holmes\' sidekick, Dr. Watson.)'),(11835,'User','Two children have disappeared in a mysterious forest, and their parents approach you for help finding them.'),(11844,'User','This GM module contains one solo-adventure.'),(11872,'User','It is the year 1855. You must guide a caravan of settlers safely from Missouri to Oregon.'),(11878,'User','Urizen, fourth city of Bariz, second planet of the Horizon System. Somewhere in the Galaxy. You are Caleb Storm and you solve problems, even when they come at you crashing down like rain during fall. You are a private detective and work at Gigamesh Pike, the outer western suburbs of Urizen. Despite your life between the tentacles of this floating metropolis being hard, you are harder still and you eke out a living without too much difficulty. But tonight it is better if you bring with you an umbrella, Storm. Tonight, it\'s raining troubles, troubles with guns....'),(11883,'User','The peaceful Joschol nation is facing the invasion of outlanders who came from the sea. Embark on a great gamebook quest to save them.'),(11888,'User','Episode One begins outside a traditional Maori settlement in Fiordland, New Zealand. The people are protected by Guardians, and one guardian, Maia, is censured for her strange nature.  While Maia lives outside the settlement, in the forest, her loyalty remains strong to her people as she protects them from hostile outside forces.'),(11890,'User','This is a Portuguese-language review of <a href=\"/Item/11144\">You Are the Hero: Part 2</a>.'),(11893,'User','Have you heard about the Icelandic folk tales? They are full of trolls and monsters, elves and zombies, yule lads and ghosts. But what would you do if you met those creatures?\n\n<p>Your own folk tale is different from other books - you are the hero and you decide how the story goes. The story\'s environment is the world of Icelandic folk tales and the dangers can be found everywhere. You can meet the Deacon of Myrká, see dangerous icelandic mermaids, battle the Worm of Lagarfljót itself and save the farmer\'s son and Búkolla from the most terrible trolls ever seen in this country!\n\n<p>Over fifty different endings.'),(11894,'User','Your own legend is different from other books - you are the hero and you decide how the story goes. The story takes place in the world of Nordic gods and the adventures are endless. You can have a fight with terrible monsters, witness the birth of the world, fly in a wagon with the thundergod Thor and try to survive ragnarök (Armageddon) - it all depends on your choice.\n\n<p>Over fifty different endings. Unending fun for kids at all ages.'),(11895,'User','Your own horror story is different from other books - you are the hero and you decide how the story goes. The story takes place during a dark and stormy night, stock full of monsters and creatures. You can meet vampires and werewolves, zombies and evil spirits, devious dolls and crazy clowns - it all depends on your choice.\n\n<p>Over forty different endings.<br>\nThe endings range from eternal happiness to sudden death.<br>\nA horribly good fun for any kid.'),(11896,'User','A book that is like a computer game because you decide what happens!\n\n<p>Your own adventure is different from other books. You are the hero and control the pace. The story takes place in very dangerous adventure woods, stock full of strange creatures and monsters. Will you end up in the stomach of a wolf or will you be enticed by a delicious looking cookie house? Will you climb the giant beanstalk or will the thornbushes catch you? It\'s your choice!'),(11897,'User','This book is about a smart cow, a rushing river, mad trolls, a crazy bull, a flaming fire, a huge drill - and YOU. Because you decide what happens! Just remember that if the story does not end well, you can always try again - there are over ten different endings!'),(11898,'User','This book is about a dark and deep cave, three terrible children of monsters, gods, goddesses - and YOU. Because you decide what happens! Just remember that if the story does not end well, you can always try again - there are over ten different endings!'),(11899,'User','This interactive web narrative is inspired by the works of Polish author Bruno Schulz.'),(11900,'User','This book provides a solitaire <a href=\"/Series/111\">Tunnels and Trolls</a> adventure played with the help of some cut-out cards.'),(11901,'Ad','Inspired by the original computer adventure that sparked a gaming revolution, Tsunami Media brings you the best of a classic through the entirely new experience of interactive literature. This outlandish spoof on Arthurian legend puts you in the writer\'s seat as you guide our reluctant hero, Ted Arthur, through the uncharted territory of tourist traps, dwarfs, and chivalry—a royal tour de farce!'),(11902,'User','This puzzle book has a completely linear structure but adopts a gamebook-style second-person narrative.'),(11919,'User','This competition gave away <a href=\"/Series/55\">Dragon Warriors</a> books as a prize.'),(11920,'User','This review discusses the <a href=\"/Item/10298\">Seas of Blood</a> computer game adaptation.'),(11921,'User','This review covers <a href=\"/Item/10515\">The Way of the Tiger</a>, the first computer game inspired by the gamebook series.'),(11923,'User','This review covers <a href=\"/Item/10516\">Avenger</a>, the second computer game based on <a href=\"/Series/469\">The Way of the Tiger</a>.'),(11924,'User','This brief article provides a map of the first level of the <a href=\"/Item/10516\">Avenger</a> computer game.'),(11925,'User','This review covers the <a href=\"/Item/10299\">Rebel Planet</a> computer game.'),(11926,'User','Welcome to Laitia, traveller between worlds! This is not an ordinary book, but an interactive adventure where you\'ll take on the role of Ugger, the Knight of the Gate, and you\'ll cross the Level Gates to visit the land of Laitia, a fantastic world with a distinct Mediterranean flavour. These are bad times for the Duchy of Torviero, in the heart of Brumia. Tirelius, the black baron son of a witch, has demanded the hand of the beautiful Fiordalisa, Torviero\'s Princess, in marriage, and her father, the duke, has not the resolve and the strength to refuse. But an ancient prophecy tells that, in the darkest hour of Torviero, the Knight of the Gate, a hero from the past, will return to Laitia to save the Duchy and marry his bride. This gamebooks, set in the world of Kata Kumbas, utilises a system without dice, the Venture System, to make you live incredible adventures! What are you waiting for? Open the book and come to Rarte, where the air has the scent of basil and marjoram!'),(11927,'User','Welcome on Laitia, traveller between worlds! This is not an ordinary book, but an interactive adventure where you\'ll take on the role of Ugger, the Knight of the Gate, and you\'ll cross the Level Gates to visit the land of Laitia, a fantastic world with a distinct Mediterranean flavour. The Duchy of Torviero is endangered once again! After the death of the witch Giunghiglia (Daffodil), a curse has fallen on the duchy like a terrible drought, a subtle evil that is slowly killing the land. Only one thing can stop the drought: the magic water stored in a bucket, or better, the Bucket, which has been contended for years between the rival cities of Demona and Gnalobo. But finding the Bucket won\'t be easy: the Queen Bella of Ammilaia, tired of the neverending wars between Demona and Gnalobo for the ownership of the Bucket, has announced a great tournament in the plain of Demona, which has for prize the Bucket itself! Torviero needs a champion to fight in the tournament and win. And who can do it better than you? Put on your armor, saddle your horse and brace yoursel for a second exciting adventure in the world of Kata Kumbas!'),(11928,'User','This is not an ordinary book, but an interactive adventure where you\'ll take on the role of Ugger, the Knight of the Gate, and you\'ll cross the Level Gates to visit the land of Laitia, a fantastic world with a distinct Mediterranean flavour. The citizens of Torviero need you once again. This time is the man who has called you in this world, your mentor the wizard Maugrigio, is in danger. With him trapped by a subtle but powerful enchantment, which could kill him in any moment, you\'ll be forced to race against time in strange and desolate lands to find the only person who can save him from the spell: the mysterious Baldera, the cartographer at the service of the Emperor of Maro, ruler of all Laitia. But something far darker and more sinister is hidden in the ancient streets of Maro, capital of the Empire. If you are ready to face a great adventure, don\'t wait! Open this book and come to Rarte, where the air has the scent of basil and marjoram!'),(11931,'User','This brief news article includes a photograph of Ian Livingstone and Steve Jackson.'),(11933,'User','This review covers both the <a href=\"/Item/37\">gamebook</a> and <a href=\"/Item/10296\">early computer game</a> of <i>The Warlock of Firetop Mountain</i>.'),(11935,'User','This brief news article announces the release of <a href=\"/Item/43\">Deathtrap Dungeon</a> and <a href=\"/Item/44\">Island of the Lizard King</a>.'),(11936,'User','This article discusses computer games based on books, including <a href=\"/Item/10296\">The Warlock of Firetop Mountain</a>.'),(11939,'User','This is a brief interview with Ian Livingstone and Steve Jackson.'),(11941,'User','This brief article announces early computer game adaptations of <a href=\"/Series/397\">Lone Wolf</a> and <a href=\"/Series/1270\">Fighting Fantasy</a>.'),(11943,'User','This article covers the original trilogy of Zork computer games and includes a photograph of the first two <a href=\"/Series/311\">Zork</a> gamebooks (though they are not discussed).'),(11945,'User','This review column is dedicated entirely to early gamebooks.'),(11947,'User','This interview includes some discussion of the development of the early <a href=\"/Series/397\">Lone Wolf computer games</a>.'),(11948,'User','This review covers the first two <a href=\"/Series/397\">Lone Wolf computer games</a>.'),(11949,'User','This review covers the first two <a href=\"/Series/39\">Famous 5 Adventure Games</a>.'),(11951,'User','This reader letter responds to criticism of the <a href=\"/Series/228\">Lone Wolf</a> books from <a href=\"/Item/11945\">an earlier article</a>.'),(11953,'User','This review covers a text adventure game written by Ian Livingstone.'),(11955,'User','This review covers the first two <a href=\"/Series/14\">Golden Dragon Fantasy Gamebooks</a>.'),(11958,'User','This collection of tiles and maps can enhance the play of the two adventures in the <a href=\"/Item/11285\">Défis Fantastiques - Le jeu de rôle</a> rulebook.'),(11959,'User','This is a collection of cards (tarot size) with all the game\'s spells, including some new spells from the <a href=\"/Item/11286\">Titan</a> sourcebook.'),(11960,'User','This is the second edition of the game master\'s screen, featuring a different bundled-in game master adventure.'),(11977,'User','You make decisions for a young man who gets hired to program a video game based on a (fictional) pick-a-path book.'),(11980,'User',' 	\nThe reader can participate in three different adventures, each taking place during a different <i>Star Wars</i> era: \"Hunt the Sith\" representing Episodes 1-3, \"Fight the Empire\" representing Episodes 4-6, and \"Defeat the First Order\" representing Episodes 7 and 8.'),(11982,'User','The reader must help solve the mystery of a stolen time machine.'),(11985,'User','This boxed set contains the gamebook plus a map, a soundtrack CD, a coin, and a \"Secrets of Rider of the Black Sun\" booklet.'),(11990,'User','You are a normal person living in a suburb. A mysterious disease appears to have killed everyone in the world, including your family. At the time the adventure begins you are alone at home, deciding whether you should abandon all hope or strike out in search of supplies and/or other survivors to help you.'),(11992,'User','Enter the role of Owl, the Deadcatcher, and make your way through the Macabre Italy, plagued by Beasts and Carrions. Hunt merciless rogues in the streets and palaces of Modena, between cabbalists, reanimated corpses and sellswords. Search for the treasure of Matilda of Tuscany, Queen of Italy, while around you is being fought the last battle against the hordes of the Dead.'),(11993,'User','Enter the role of Owl, the Deadcatcher from Modena, and make your way in a land plagued by Dead and Abominations, bandits and deserters, assassins and rogues. Travel far and wide through Macabre Italy, looking for your enemies. Visit the fiefdoms of the Malpaese (Horrible Country). Cross the Woods by rivers, roads and pathways. Brave the dangers of the Sorrowful Cities. You only die twice, as the Deadcatcher says. Your enemy already had its chance; you won\'t give it another....'),(11994,'User','Enter the role of Owl, the Deadcatcher, and make your way in a land plagued by Dead and Abominations, bandits and deserters, assassins and rogues. Travel far and wide through the Mediterranean Sea, from the Fighting Pits of Algiers to the Sicilian Caliphate, from wealthy and insidious Genoa to lost Constantinople. Face the most horrible intrigue that the New Kingdoms have seen, and finally bring light to the shadows darkening your past and family. <i>The Day of the Owl</i> is a solo adventure for <i>Ultima Forsan</i> and <i>Savage Worlds</i>. In this book you\'ll find two different game systems (basic and advanced), record sheet, dice, a map of the Macabre Mediterranean, many appendices and a number of new monsters and equipment, that can be used for the group play. There is no time to lose: go to section 1 and start your adventure!'),(12032,'User','A young reporter gets to interview an old woman who recounts her life\'s story (or rather, the different lives she could have experienced, depending on her decisions).'),(12066,'User','An interactive self-help book about Acceptance and Commitment Therapy.'),(12069,'Cover','It\'s another day in the life of a hustler and you\'ve got decisions to make. Are you going to hit the streets and get on your grind or will you screw around and trick it off?<br><br>\n\nYou\'ll need to think fast and do the right thing - which doesn\'t necessarily mean the legal thing - if you\'re going to make it to the top and stay out of the hospital, prison, and the morgue.<br><br>\n\nWith forty-six separate endings and hundreds of different paths to take to reach your destiny, no day will ever be the same. Bank robberies, drug deals, kidnapping, gun running, burglary, murder for hire, and more can lead to success or failure, it\'s your choice.<br><br>\n\nWith pages full of sex, drugs, violence, federal agents, car chases, shootouts, double crosses and backstabbing, you know that the struggle is real and sometimes it feels good to be a gangster.<br><br>'),(12113,'Cover','You\'re hanging out with your friend Amber and bored out of your minds. Playing a board game seemed to be a logical choice at the moment, but searching for a board game in the basement of your Archaeologist father\'s basement turns into quite the adventure! A hidden room and magical objects tucked away in the room changes your life forever! But will it be a good change? Only YOU can decide. Choose wisely and you just might have a strangely, satisfying ending to a story that is best left as a story.'),(12114,'Cover','You have always loved all things equestrian and mythological, so when the local papers start reporting that people are seeing a unicorn in a nearby park, you can\'t resist the urge to investigate.<br><br>\n\nUNICORN HUNT is a retro-style Choose-Your-Own-Adventure book where you can control the outcomes in the story by choosing what happens next. You\'re not passively reading this story. No. You are the hero, and that means you can handle things your way.<br><br>\n\nBut be careful! There are unexpected dangers in the local park. Should you trust the Crazy Conspiracy Theorist Guy wearing a tinfoil hat? He has a lead for you, if you believe him. What about the dishelveled Cat Lady? Can you hold your breath long enough to dive for clues in the lake?'),(12115,'Cover','When a mysterious birthday present arrives, the last thing you expected was that Great Uncle Zebulon would need your help to save not only the World, but the whole Universe!  As if that wasn\'t enough, it seems that to safeguard the Future, you will need to travel far back into the past, in search of treasures lost long ago.  One thing is certain: after this, things are never going to be the same again...'),(12118,'User','You are the dancer who will later be known as Mata Hari. One night a member of your dance troupe disappears mysteriously, setting off a series of strange events.'),(12129,'User','Ice King tricks Finn and Jake into giving up their free will to you, the reader.'),(12139,'LC','\"Describes the sinking of the Lusitania. Readers\' choices reveal various historical details\"--Provided by publisher.'),(12140,'User','When the Mane Seven attend a music festival, Sunset Shimmer finds herself caught in a time loop.'),(12142,'Ad','Descend into the depths of the undercity and embroil yourself in the political struggles of colonialist gnomes and indigenous goblins. Fly in air balloons, drink mysterious and pleasant cocktails, smoke opium with the dregs of gnomish society. Or dream and speak of liberation for all the races. Fall in love and abscond into the caverns. It\'s up to you, because this is an adventure of your own choosing.'),(12143,'User','You make decisions for a group of animals as they set off to find fortune in the city of Bremen (or have other adventures, depending on the choices you make.) '),(12147,'User','	Your mother runs a down-on-its-luck detective agency. A wealthy woman asks for her help finding out who is sending her death threats, but your mom is down with the flu and unable to take the case. Together with your best friend and her annoying little brother, you set out to solve the mystery.'),(12150,'User','Thousands of years ago a powerful sorcerer ruled these lands. His dark, terrible magic influenced all the great military and political leaders of the time. These men were not necessarily evil, but ultimately, they were no match for the Shadow Lord’s devious charms and spells. They easily succumbed to his will, worked (often unknowingly) as his agents, and a dark age endured for many, many generations. It is not known how or when he met defeat, but, over time and the ages, his name has faded and been forgotten. The stories about him, if remembered at all, are considered nothing more than ancient legend. This sorcerer was cunning, however, and had planned for his eventual demise. The time has come; the plan in its final stages. His spirit has awakened! An appropriate vessel captured, and soon, the revival ritual will be complete! Then, all shall tremble and despair before the Shadow Lord - <i>Bwana wa Kivuli</i>!'),(12173,'Cover','Your homeland is a place of haunted forests and shadowy marshes. Its people live in fear of the foul demons and dreaded beasts that stalk its untamed regions. In order to survive, you have become highly skilled in the art of battle, forging a name for yourself as a mighty adventurer.<BR><BR>\n\nYou are soon to learn that a terrible evil is growing in the south; an ancient power that threatens to destroy the few bastions of good in this dangerous world. From beyond the snow-clad peaks of the Druideen Mountains, a plea for aid has reached your ears. Will YOU answer the call to arms?'),(12175,'User','Master Yoda has been kidnapped by an unknown entity. As Anakin Skywalker, you must set out on a journey to locate and rescue him.'),(12190,'User','This adult choose your own adventure book was included as a supplement with an issue of Newlook Magazine (April 2005).'),(12192,'Ad','You\'re the British Prime Minister and Brexit is under way. You have just two years to negotiate the unpicking of an alliance that\'s been built up over four decades. And that\'s not the only minefield you’re going to have to cross. Your cabinet is unruly, your party is splitting itself apart, and the country remains bitterly divided over the whole issue.<BR><BR>\n\nCan you hang on and bring Britain safely into harbour? Forge new trade deals around the globe? Juggle popular support at home with the goodwill of your former EU allies? Stop the economy from spiralling down the plug hole? And all the while keeping an eye on those Parliamentary colleagues whose knives are ever-ready to plunge into your back?<BR><BR>\n\nThis is an interactive gamebook in which you call all the shots. What could possibly go wrong?'),(12196,'User','This book was originally intended to contain the bonus adventure <a href=\"/Item/13514\">Shadow Stalkers</a>, but it was moved to <a href=\"/Item/13203\">Vampirium (reissue)</a> as the main adventure turned out to be longer than originally planned.\n'),(12208,'User','You are Jay Huey, a London policeman in an unspecified future, when illegal immigration to Europe has exceeded dangerous levels. What remains of the European Union reacts to the threat with the Western Defense Treaty, a series of draconian measures that affect citizens in many more ways than were expected or desired. All of this has serious consequences on your job and everyday life –- but you’ll have to find out exactly why. '),(12217,'Ad','The god of destruction has possessed a human body, and uses its powers to wreak havoc in Ambrosinia.What do you do?As Titania Vermouth, the former leader of the fishermen\'s town of Sungaze, you, the reader, make the decisions. Will you fly a dragon toward your destiny, or instead befriend an orcblood? Do you forge a sword, or spin a magic wheel? Might you succumb to the threat of hatred, or instead conquer it with love? It\'s up to you, but be warned: The fate of your friends hangs in the balance.'),(12221,'Cover','You are a police officer with an extraordinary power.<BR><BR>\n\nYour name is Hugh Hatch, and in the year 2045 you have been allocated to a unique department of the New Zealand Police Force; one which caters for and supports people with abilities above and beyond those of regular human beings.<BR><BR>\n\nYou will find yourself embroiled in a high-stakes adventure which will see you arresting perpetrators, performing investigations and solving a mystery. Within the academy known as The Chrysalis lies a secret hidden from the world; one which may turn the human race against one another and ultimately put the planet in jeopardy. Will you become the leader needed to uncover this threat and change the fate of the Earth? Will you be able to handle your new partner, who struggles with a great affliction of her own? The next seven days could change everything.<BR><BR>\n\nBut who is the real enemy? The man who manipulates living art? The killer from another world? The madman with links to organised crime? Or will the real threat be closer to home; among your own friends and colleagues?<BR><BR>\n\nIn this interactive gamebook with multiple paths and 16 endings, you have the power to determine your own fate. Which one will you choose?'),(12232,'Ad','Quando Chiara ti ha invitato alla festa eri al settimo cielo. Arrivato alla villa, però, lei non c\'è ancora, mentre vieni subito avvicinato da Stefano, il bullo della scuola, e Dario, il suo compare. Per fortuna poco dopo eccola che arriva, splendida come sempre. La festa si svolge in giardino ed è vietato entrare in casa. Chiara ti racconta che, secondo una leggenda, lì un tempo abitava un Barone assassino. E a quanto pare il suo fantasma ancora si aggira tra le stanze. Mentre lo dice apre il portone e sguscia dentro. Che altro puoi fare, se non seguirla? Ma dopo pochi passi lei sparisce con un grido. Provi a tornare indietro per chiedere aiuto ma la porta è sbarrata. Ben presto capisci che in quella villa si annida un mistero molto più pericoloso e reale di una leggenda. Devi assolutamente trovare Chiara prima che sia troppo tardi!'),(12233,'Ad','\"No, no!\" gridi tornando indietro, e prendi a pugni il muro. Alle tue spalle senti anche Lorenzo che urla, ti dice di stare calmo e di cercare una maniglia, una serratura, qualsiasi cosa. Ma il muro che hai davanti è liscio come una parete qualunque e non vedi un modo di riaprire il passaggio. Quando il tuo amico Lorenzo ti ha portato davanti al vecchio carcere abbandonato, tutto pensavi tranne che avrebbe osato schiudere il pesante portone ed entrare. E, a quel punto, non hai avuto scelta: lo hai seguito. Una volta dentro, tra macerie, strane scritte sui muri e lugubri celle vuote, una sensazione crescente di pericolo si fa strada in voi. E la sensazione si trasforma in certezza non appena vi accorgete che siete finiti in un vicolo cieco e la via d\'uscita è bloccata. A peggiorare la situazione, non molto distanti, vi arrivano voci concitate e rabbiosi latrati di cani. I misteri che aleggiano tra i corridoi della prigione vi stanno lentamente avvolgendo, senza lasciarvi scampo!'),(12265,'User','You are a respected doctor, appreciated by your colleagues and loved by friends, who consider you a reliable man. Your yearning for knowledge has led you to explore the boundaries of science and face extreme studies, searching for the true nature of the human soul. On this path you have discovered that another dark and and licentious individual lurks inside you, and now he wants to take control. You are no longer just Dr. Henry Jekyll; Edward Hyde is sick of hiding and wants to free himself. He has already committed a horrible crime; will you succeed in splitting your souls once and for all and regain control of your life?'),(12277,'Ad','Think you have what it takes to be a Marvel Super Hero? Read this book for tips, tricks, and much more from your favorite Marvel Super Heroes. You\'ll start by figuring out your awesome origin and powers: bit by a radioactive spider? Easy. Walk into a mysterious mist and now you\'re a shapeshifter? Check. Then you\'ll have to figure out your costume, your headquarters, your allies, and your enemies! Don\'t worry, there are checkpoints along the way, plus quizzes, how-to\'s, and do-it-yourself activities! Once you have everything in place, it will be time for some astonishing adventures! What are you waiting for? Let\'s get your Super Hero career started!'),(12280,'Cover','In this story, you the reader make choices and take chances as you hunt evil’s spawn during the 1930s.<BR><BR>\n\nYou are a flawed hero battling horrors in a dangerous world of broken streetlights and lost souls. You know your vile vampiric foes. You’ve got gear and a few cantrips. Can you rescue abducted townsfolk and clear an undead nest? Can you redeem yourself? Will you even live to see dawn or will madness claim you?<BR><BR>\n\nThe stage is an abandoned church in an alternate world akin to Earth. You’ve got familiar conveniences but beyond the bright busy streets there’s magic, and monsters lurk ready to snatch the unwary. Your arsenal includes a gun, sword and stake, strong wine, light bombs, heaven radio, the ghost of your old mutt Frisk, and a few friendly “pact spirits” that can lend you their might against dark forces.<BR><BR>\n\nThis gothic adventure gamebook is part fiction, part game. It’s for one reader-player or several. It’s organized as four-dozen scenes along a dramatic arc. Some scenes are optional while others task you to fight inner nightmares as well as outer ones. All are harrowing or horrific.<BR><BR>\n\nScenes are chock-full of rich description and dialogue, offer tactical choices, and deliver to you the consequences of failures and successes.<BR><BR>\n\nFeatures pact magic: the summoning of ancient broken spirits of yore.<BR><BR>\n\nThis is a stand-alone product that requires at least one standard die (6-sides) and ideally a 20-sided die to resolve the many challenges throughout. To track your health, sanity, gear, and treasure, you also get a simple character sheet that you can print.Includes suggestions to implement the adventure using Radiance RPG or your favorite tabletop roleplaying game.<BR><BR>\n\nThis gamebook is for ages 12+.'),(12282,'User','You are a cleric. Count Strahd has transported you to Castle Ravenloft, where he intends to make you one of his servants. You must find a way to escape from the castle.'),(12283,'User','You are a thief. A client has hired you to steal the spell book of a very powerful wizard who runs a magic academy deep inside the Undermountain. In order to achieve this objective, you present yourself as an applicant to the school. '),(12284,'Cover','It\'s your turn to have an adventure...\n<br><br>\nYou\'ve lived in the sleepy seaside village of Baileytown your whole life. Under the watchful eye of your grandad Dagris Screbin, you\'ve learned tricks from the local fisherman and heard tales of wonder from the passing merchants. Yet here you\'ve stay, happily watching the tide come and go.\n<br><br>\nNow is the time to leave your home and see some of these wonders for yourself. Your grandad\'s old friend Alf Blomwell has sent word from the far-off swamp town of Hatcheria. Something is amiss. Something that will threaten all Brighthelm. An ancient evil has awoken.\n<br><br>\nOr has it? Dagris says Alf has been slowly going senile for years, and he was pretty odd to start with. However, he isn\'t taking any chances. He\'s sending you, his best adventurer across lands unknown to find out what has panicked old Alf.\n<br><br>\nThe Curse of Saltash Mine is an adventure gamebook in which YOU are the hero. Armed with a pencil, eraser and a die, YOU will decide which paths to take and which dangers to risk.'),(12442,'User','This magazine issue is marked as a \"Fighting Fantasy Gamebooks Special\" and contains interviews and reports on the subject.'),(12484,'Ad','Only a poor turn of fate could determine how a simple business trip would release a ravenous horror upon London!\n<br><br>\nYou are Jonathan Harker, travelling to Transylvania to finalise a property transaction for a nobleman named Count Dracula. The man is an enigma, undoubtedly lonely and likely eccentric, but this deal will be a boon to your employer, and a significant step forward for your own career.\n<br><br>\nThe country you traverse is steeped in history and superstition, and as you surge further eastward, the more apprehensive people become. They warn you of the terrors that live in the darkest hours of the night, but you are an Englishman, and not one to be scared off by tall tales!\n<br><br>\nIn this interactive horror mystery gamebook set in 19th Century Europe, you will take on the roles of three characters at separate points in the story.\n<br><br>\nSurvive the freezing forests of Munich. Escape a Transylvanian castle with enemies all around you. Brave rough seas on the cargo ship Demeter. Then strive to save those whom you love back in England!\n<br><br>\nYou choose where the story goes. You solve the mysteries and puzzles that lead to a happy ending, or possibly an early demise. You could be the hero of the hour or the one who propels London to its very doom!\n<br><br>\nWhich road will you choose?'),(12497,'Ad','A \'choose your own adventure\' style horror story, written and illustrated by Brother Bemps.\n<br><br>\nWhat would you do if Brighton was attacked by zombies? For most people it would simply mean a quick, messy death. For others, it would be the fulfilment of a life\'s ambition. In the meantime, this \'survival simulator\' allows you to vicariously indulge in the joys of watching society crumble whilst feeling morally-justified in committing acts of violence. This is a story in which you get to decide what happens. Yes, you!'),(12498,'Ad','A \'choose your own adventure\' style horror story, written and illustrated by Brother Bemps.\n<br><br>\nSeveral mutilated animal carcasses have been found in Queen\'s Park. At first the Argus blamed the attacks on illegal immigrants, but today\'s issue of the paper has sensationally revealed that the city is threatened by an army of mysterious vampires. You have a day to prepare.\n<br><br>\nA twenty-page CD-sized booklet with 8 illustrations, 30 paragraphs of story and four alternate endings. This is a story in which you decide what happens. Yes, you!'),(12534,'Ad','A choose-your-own adventure gamebook featuring the cast of Taffy the Fire. Make your own choices and take control of the story to see if you can achieve knighthood!'),(12550,'LC','\"In You Choose format, explores the history of the Voting Rights Act of 1965, including the struggles minorities had in achieving the right to vote, enforcement of the law, and the Civil Rights movement of the 1960s and 1970s\"--Provided by publisher.'),(12573,'Ad','As a class, we believe that more novels should be written in the second person. We also believe that readers should be able to make choices, and that leprechauns are deadly, and that it\'s totally possible to write a valid adventure story in an hour-long jam session with one\'s classmates. Hence: \"The Door and the Lake\", an experimental choose-your-own-adventure-style novella in which a lot of terrible things happen. Read and enjoy or die or survive or whatever.'),(12594,'User','The title is a literal translation of the German original \"Schätze des Wahnsinns\".'),(12595,'User','The title is a literal translation of the German original \"Die Ketten von Ghol-Tabras\".'),(12597,'Ad','\"The Quest for Cheesy Chips\" is a fun and silly Choose-Your-Own-Adventure zine documenting the noble task of searching for some trust cheesy chips one moonlit night! With five different endings to discover, you make your own way through the story by making various decisions. Can you manage to make it towards your beloved dinner?'),(12598,'Ad','\"The Hand in the Pumpkin Patch\" is a fun and silly Choose-Your-Own-Adventure zine that will tickle your funny bone! With four different endings to discover, you make your own way through the story by making various decisions. Can you discover the mystery of why there is a hand in your beloved pumpkin patch?'),(12600,'User','This is your third summer at a special camp for young princesses. You have adventures relating to a magical unicorn living somewhere close to the camp.'),(12601,'User','Two gamebook combined into one paperback. Translates both \"Ship of Ghouls\" and \"Alone in Snakebite Canyon\".'),(12602,'User','Two gamebook combined into one paperback. Translates both \"Scream of the Evil Genie\" and \"Shop Till You Drop...Dead!\".'),(12608,'Ad','A choose your own adventure style story set in the Aliens/Predator universe.\n\nAfter waking from stasis it appears that your ship is empty with no crew to be seen. You soon realise that something else is on the ship as you try to find out what has happened… and escape.'),(12640,'User','As the Batman, you must choose between foiling an evil plot by villain Kanjar Ro to control all oil on Earth, or a plot by villain Mongul to gain control over the entire universe.'),(12652,'User','You are a young Somali immigrant playing for your high school\'s soccer team. Aside from winning this year\'s championship, you have to juggle academic and family pressures, as well as your dream of becoming a writer one day.'),(12655,'Ad','Romance, friendship, and geekiness. Sean has returned home to his friendly local gameshop with renewed confidence. He finally wants to push through nerves and ask out Ami--his favorite employee. Sean knows how much they have in common. Before he can make his move, his buddy Santana shows up and needs a friend. How will Sean spend his evening now? The reader negotiates between trying for Ami and helping Santana. Can Sean do both? Can he do either? This slice of life romance story lets the reader make the decisions. This is pure choice driven branched narrative where the reader picks the next step on the path.Decide how Sean will spend the evening in this interactive fiction novella.'),(12686,'User','This booklet collects some role-playing articles written by gamebook author Paul Mason and previously published in <a href=\"/Series/1854\">Alarums and Excursions</a>. The content is not directly gamebook-related.'),(12705,'User','You can choose to have adventures loosely based on the Ralph Breaks the Internet film, playing as either Vanellope or Ralph.'),(12706,'User','You can experience the maiden voyage of the <i>RMS Titanic</i> as a passenger, as a crew member, or as a stowaway. '),(12718,'Ad','La stanza risuona degli scampanellii delle varie attrazioni, quasi coprono l\'ansimare di Alex che prova a forzare le porte. E se questa non fosse la soluzione? Eppure non hai mai sentito parlare di un luna park che ti costringe a risolvere degli enigmi per poter uscire...\n\nVoi tre fratelli in giro da soli per tutta la sera: finalmente un\'avventura in questa vacanza fin troppo tranquilla! Quando vi intrufolate in un luna park abbandonato e devastato da un incendio, e poi all\'interno di un padiglione con attrazioni stranamente funzionanti, siete certi che avrete una bella storia da raccontare quando tornerete a casa. Ma tornare a casa non è così scontato, nel momento in cui vi accorgete che la porta d\'ingresso è bloccata e l\'inquietante voce registrata del coniglio Bunny, la mascotte del parco, vi esorta a risolvere degli enigmi per poter uscire... Per scappare ci vorranno ingegno e sangue freddo, perché nel buio qualcuno o qualcosa spia le vostre mosse e farà di tutto per tenervi rinchiusi.'),(12746,'User','You begin receiving cellphone messages from an unknown person calling themselves Sam, who claims a zombie apocalypse is going on. You must guide Sam as they try to stay alive in the new world around them.'),(12754,'Cover','Can you find the culprit? Put your wits to the test with these twenty tricky mysteries. Each one contains hidden clues - all you have to do is spot them! Ready, Sherlock?'),(12755,'User','A giant tree is attacking Gateway City, and the superhero team known as The Terrifics must find a way to stop it.'),(12777,'Cover','In diesem Soloabenteuer schlüpfst du in die Rolle des legendären Sultans Hasrabal und begibst dich auf die Suche nach einem der Blauen Augen der Mada, welches sich im legendären Reich von Al’Ghûriya verbergen soll. '),(12778,'User','This volume contains three items: two group adventures and one solitaire adventure.'),(12782,'Cover','This is a mini-adventure for the I VIRUS D66 Gamebook Series. Set after book 1 but before book 2 in the series.'),(12796,'User','You are a college senior celebrating your graduation. You must navigate the night both helping your best friend with personal issues and trying to make your crush fall in love with you.'),(12826,'Ad','You lie in bed, cozy and content, sleeping the morning away. Suddenly, a chilling noise, the gut-twisting buzz of a bee, rips through your dreams and tears you awake. You peek from beneath your covers and spot the intruder, the most hideous insect you\'ve ever seen. Before you can possibly resume your slumber, you know you must rid your presence of that winged evil. Defenseless, terrified, you must decide: will you kill the bee or direct it out your open window? Written in the style of the once popular Choose-Your-Own-Adventure series, Buzzkill is a branching-path gamebook in which you are the main character and you decide the outcome of your story. As you read, you\'ll be faced with choices. Each choice will determine the path your story will take and, of twelve possible endings, how your story will end. If your first choice be to read this book, proceed with caution. You determine your fate, so choose wisely. Even the slightest blunder could be the difference between death and happily ever after.'),(12827,'Ad','20th Anniversary OpenD6 Edition You wake with a start. A cold sweat covers your body. You shiver from the cool air around you and the cold, hard bed. In that drowsy fog that clouds your mind just after sleep you don’t recall crawling from your desk into bed. With all your recent sleep deprivation you wonder if you can remember anything clearly. Perhaps you fell asleep in the museum library, but the librarians always wake you up and send you along at closing time. As your waking haze clears, you realize you can’t possibly have fallen asleep and been locked in the library...you’re wearing only your nightclothes! Trapped in the Museum is a solitaire adventure gamebook you can play like a story in which you’re the main character. The adventure text itself incorporates rules for overcoming obstacles based on the classic D6 System developed by West End Games. All the rules you need are right in this book...just add a few six-sided dice and you’re ready to play!'),(12828,'Ad','Escape in the Lap of Luxury.... Vanno del Rask had to escape Gorvann starport and reach Naava Prime. If Rayzu Syndicate operatives tracked him down they’d interrogate him to find out how much he’d discovered of their plans to destabilize the sector government for their own profit. He charmed and bribed his way aboard a luxury cruiser named Asturia, leaving Gorvann without enemy operatives noticing. You are Vanno del Rask. Now that you’ve escaped the Rayzu Syndicate thugs, it’s smooth sailing to complete your mission...or is it? The Asturia Incident is a solitaire adventure gamebook, an interactive story in which you play the role of the main character. Instead of reading straight through like a normal book, you follow instructions leading you from one numbered entry to another. You’ll need a handful of six-sided dice; a pencil and some note paper can help you keep track of Vanno’s status, clues he discovers, or other information worth remembering.'),(12839,'Ad','Scooby Doom versus the Cult of Cthulhu - Choose Your Own Adventure style featuring special guest Doctor Herbert West Rutrow! The Rult of Rurooroo! You are Scooby Doom, a hound of Carcosa, and you must stop the tentacled terror of the Cult of Cthulhu. Choose from 47 possible endings, most resulting in death! Will it be yours? Includes Easter eggs for Saturday morning cartoons, 80\'s music, Dungeons and Dragons, the Cthulhu Mythos, Abc Weekend Specials, and other cultural icons and references of the era. Don\'t be afraid of the incredible hulking hybrid star spawn of Cthulhu - Scooby Doom will protect you!'),(12840,'Ad','There are many ways civilisation could end, even with wise, benevolent leaders like Kim Jong-un, Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin watching over us. Now, in this fun interactive story of global doom, YOU decide how humanity perishes.\n\nWill we be turned to grey goo by Elon Musk’s nanobots?\n\nDriven collectively insane by Russia’s most potent memes?\n\nOr smashed to atoms by someone sitting on the wrong button in North Korea?'),(12841,'Ad','Your name is Roark. For thousands of years, you have been conducting experiments on the human race. Immortal and immune to pain, you yearn to understand what it means to be alive, yet your constant quest seldom bears fruit. To this end, you have trapped five people (two knights, an old priestess, a young acolyte and a travelling musician) in a temple filled with traps and monsters. If they can find the exit, you have promised to set them free. Unlike other gamebooks, here you take the role of the villain. It is up to you to beset the heroes with problems, to send in monsters or create walls of fire. All the while, you must watch them and try to further your understanding of their simple species. Can the heroes defeat you, and can you keep them alive long enough to learn something from them? A gamebook of 61 paragraphs.'),(12842,'Ad','You are a junior crew member of the scout ship \"Hazard Pay\". An disaster strikes and an explosion kills the rest of your crew. Are you able to use your wits to survive the immediate crisis and survive the events that follow? Or will you make a wrong choice and perish before help can find you? In this interactive fiction novella, you get to decide the action.'),(12875,'User','This volume contains three items: one group adventure and two solitaire adventures.'),(12886,'Ad','This is a short TOY MYSTERY gamebook for young readers. You choose what happens.\n<br><br>\nKei and Will are students at the School of Amusement Arts in New Toy-ko City. They help Professor Felicity Nora investigate unusual cases involving toys and puzzles. A rare set of Chatter Blocks has been stolen. These Blocks talk when you roll them like dice. Help Kei and Will catch the thief and recover the Blocks. But careful, the Perplexity Gang is involved!\n<br><br>\nThere are a few different endings. See if you can help the characters solve the case, catch the thief, and learn the secret of the Chatter Blocks.\n<br><br>\nThis gamebook has been designed for younger readers, ages 8 to 10. It can be read alone, in a group, or during bedtime reading. It introduces young readers to the interactive fiction genre.'),(12914,'User','A magical suit of armour has gone missing in suspicious circumstances and there’s only one person who can help to solve the mystery.<br><br>\n\nYou!<br><br>\n\nWith nearly 20 different endings, exploding fart potions, freezing spells and plenty of other silly twists and turns, The Magic Knight is an adventure that puts you in control of the action. You choose where the story goes by making decisions and following your instincts. But be warned, not all endings are happy!'),(12935,'Ad','Sophie Faithful works as a Sales Rep in a big company. She lives in inner Melbourne and she likes her life, but there\'s something missing.<br><br>\n\nYou need to help her choose what to do. Whether to go on a date with her colleague Jude, or to get back in touch with her ex, James, or whether to strike up a conversation with that guy in the cafe, Freddie.<br><br>\n\nThis Choose Your Own Romance Adventure has 14 endings. Some are sexy and fun, others have serious consequences.'),(12938,'User','As a member of the Sky Watch, a police force that helps protect the floating islands of Pangaria, you must investigate when the central island plunges into the sea, taking your comrades in the Sky Watch with it.'),(12943,'Ad','The ultimate handbook for pre-High School boys, the ultimate nostalgia trip for men.<br><br>\n\nHow would you fare if you could do that \'big day\' all over again. This literally immersive book will help you find out.<br><br>\n\nJack Steveson embarks on his High School career, faced with many challenges from the very first day. From dealing with bullies to other social stigma and, you, as the reader can help him navigate his way through these trials and tribulations by selecting which options you would take. At the end you\'ll get to tally up your score and compare it to an integrated social scale to see where you would fit into a class today. <br><br>\n\nWill you be a hero? A heart-throb? A bit of a git? Part story, part test, part game and ideal for everyone 10 years or older. (Contains mild coarse words)'),(12982,'User','The Mystery, Inc. gang find themselves locked in a haunted mansion, and they must solve a ghostly mystery to escape.'),(13013,'User','This history and bibliography of role-playing games includes a chapter devoted to gamebooks, making it one of the earliest scholarly considerations of the form.'),(13018,'LC','A series of puzzle pictures in which the reader helps three young Puzzle Masters and their dog search for hidden treasure while dealing with tunnels, caves, forged treasures and maps, a maze, and other obstacles.'),(13022,'User','While traveling down a road you come across a dying young man who tells you about an evil wyvern who lives nearby. Your mission, should you choose to accept it, is to track down the creature and slay it.'),(13024,'Ad','You are Stormwing, an agent of the Yeorseggr sworn brotherhood. A hero in the vein of Lone Wolf and Cub or The Mandalorian, you go where the innocent need you to be and protect them from the horrors of this world. When wreckers sink your ship you wash up on the icy shores of Kalbud, a northern frontier town. Slay giants, avenge yourself against pirates and start to unravel the mystery of the sinister Bloodshapers!<br><br>\n\nInspired by such classics as Joe Dever\'s Lone Wolf and Ian Livingstone\'s and Steve Jackson\'s Fighting Fantasy series, the Wanderer system takes gamebooks to a whole new dimension. As a \"gamebook+\" this title contains a narrative section, as well as rules to help you take your adventures off the rails. Generate your own enemies, traps, treasures, dungeons and bosses for even more dangerous and exciting tales.<br><br>\n\nThere are guidelines for turning your own adventures into gamebooks, which you can then trade with friends and collaborate to create something new and fantastic.'),(13029,'Ad','First adventure of Shelby ! A funny silent gamebook for the whole family!'),(13033,'Ad','During the COVID-19 quarantine a blogger tries to keep the blog going, but struggles to be creative in the face of uncertainty. Readers follow the blog entries.'),(13034,'Ad','During the COVID-19 quarantine a blogger tries to keep the blog going, but struggles to be creative in the face of uncertainty, until he finds purpose advocating for political change and writing fiction. Readers follow the blogs and fiction.'),(13035,'Ad','How will you handle the first day of high school? This interactive book helps you find out. Ian Dever begins high school, faces challenges from the start, but your choices help her try to fit in. Bullies, isolation, and social stigma stand between Ian and the end of the first day of school. Can you help her find a way through? At the end, compare yourself to the Social Scale to measure success. Ideal for pre-high school readers and nostalgia trip for Gamebook fans.'),(13037,'Ad','Ayasha and Stacy met in a college English class. They had a surprising amount in common, including the same boy friend. He said his name was John. Maybe it was. Maybe it wasn\'t. It is hard to decide because lies are too easy to tell. Curl up and follow Stacy\'s stream of consciousness exploration of memories, relationship with John, and unwilling place in the love triangle. Then read about Ayasha and John’s perspective in their stories. Trilogy Edition (in print) connects the entire love triangle through linked interactive fiction short stories: “is this all there is,” “i\'m a woman,” and “moments like this.”'),(13038,'Ad','Ayasha and Stacy met in a college English class. They had a surprising amount in common, including the same boy friend. He said his name was John. Maybe it was. Maybe it wasn\'t. It is hard to decide because lies are too easy to tell. Curl up and follow Stacy\'s stream of consciousness exploration of memories, relationship with John, and unwilling place in the love triangle.'),(13039,'Ad','Ayasha and Stacy met in a college English course. They had a lot in common, including their boyfriends. Too much in common. In fact, their boy friends were more than similar, they were dating the same guy.<br><br>\n\nThis interactive fiction romance short story explores Ayasha\'s angle in the love triangle, following her past years memories.'),(13040,'Ad','Ayasha and Stacy met in a college English class. They had a surprising amount in common, including the same boy friend.<br><br>\n\nStacy thought his name was John. Ayasha thought his name was Deacon. Maybe it was or wasn\'t John Deacon. Underneath the lies are a truth the girls never figured out.<br><br>\n\nThis is an interactive fiction short story following John Deacon\'s angle in the love triangle and his past.<br><br>\n\nThe love triangle is explored further in related short stories i am a woman and moments like this.<br><br>'),(13046,'User','This book contains a series of <a href=\"/Series/111\">Tunnels & Trolls</a> solo and GM adventures previously published on the pages of <a href=\"/Series/394\">Sorcerer\'s Apprentice</a> magazine, plus one solitaire adventure (<a href=\"/Item/2737\">Circle of Ice</a>) which had previously been published on its own. The adventures have been updated for play using the \"Deluxe\" edition of <a href=\"/Series/111\">T&T</a>, which appeared in the mid-2010s. The <a href=\"/Series/394\">Sorcerer\'s Apprentice</a> solos have all been joined together in a series of sections numbered from 2 to 239 (so that they resemble a single gamebook with multiple starting points). However, the different adventures remain mostly unconnected to each other (except for a single ending which is shared by several of them). The <a href=\"/Item/2737\">Circle of Ice</a> adventure included in this book retains its original section labeling scheme, where each section is denoted using a number and a letter.'),(13050,'Ad','It’s your son’s birthday and you still haven’t gotten him a gift. Luckily, The Billings Mall is open just a few minutes longer, and if you hurry you can find him something great.\n\nTonight isn’t like other nights at The Billings Mall, however. After a reported timeline tear out by the lake, people are on edge, wondering if this inner dimensional event is as harmless as the police would have you believe. Is this a minor rift in reality, or has a pathway been opened to the depths of the endless cosmic Void?\n\nIn this science fiction and horror tale of The Tingleverse, you decide which path to take. With multiple endings to discover and several consequences to face, the reader is the star of the show as you attempt to escape from The Billings Mall!\n\nWill you befriend a beautiful velociraptor with a meta awareness that you’re both just fictional characters in a books?\n\nWill you meet a terrifying reverse twin and suddenly find yourself parting with your own skin?\n\nIs the food court your best method of escape, or should you head even deeper into the mall to see what lurks in the manager’s office?\n\nThe decision is yours!'),(13051,'Ad','before you, you’re hoping to hit the big time in Tinglewood, to tell the story that ignites your soul and begs to erupt forth on the silver screen, or in a hit song, or across a television set. You’re here to become a star.\n\nOf course, this mission is easier said than done, and in Tinglewood there’s no shortage of drama and mystery to keep you occupied. The Tinglewood Slashman has been on the front page every day, claiming victims across the City of Devils with no sign of slowing down.\n\nIn this thrilling tale of The Tingleverse, you decide which path to take. With multiple endings to discover and several consequences to face, the reader is the star of the show as you fight to see your name in lights!\n\nWill you and a punk rock unicorn take over the fine art scene after a battle with giant rats in Venna Beach?\n\nWill you encounter The Valley Girls, a roving band of desert-dwelling barbarians in diesel-powered war machines, and live to tell the tale?\n\nWill you find yourself house-sitting for dinosaur superstar Bob Downer, Jr. in the Tinglewood Hills, only to discover things are not exactly as they seem?\n\nThe decision is yours!'),(13052,'Ad','After working as a long-haul truck driver for years, the time has arrived for your final journey across the wide open American landscape. You meet with your boss, Truckman, who assigns a shipment of chocolate milk between Billings, Montana and San Diego, California. However, what he doesn’t inform you of is the secret device hidden within your cargo hold, a Big Red Button that could alter the fabric of this reality forever.\n\nNow you’re caught up in a race against time as the notorious devil, Ted Cobbler, does everything he can to intercept your shipment and steal The Big Red Button.\n\nIn this thrilling tale of The Tingleverse, you decide which path to take. With multiple endings to discover and several consequences to face, the reader is the star of the show as you duel to make this special delivery!\n\nWill you arrive in style after a night out in Las Vegas with a sentient card counting jet plane?\n\nWill you turn the tables on a pack of rowdy jackalopes, or end up lost in the snow covered passes of Wyoming?\n\nMost importantly, will Ted Cobbler and his dark magic take your last ride down a highway to heck, or will you blaze a path to glory?\n\nThe decision is yours!'),(13097,'Ad','The Supporter Pack features two key components: membership in the Quahnarren Adventurers’ Guild, and the Adventurer’s Almanac. As a QAG member you will be able to access exclusive benefits in future ToQ interactive adventures – rewards that can only be unlocked via your membership number of this esteemed fellowship. The Adventurer’s Almanac has been created for fans wishing to immerse themselves deeper into the history of my imagined world. It offers greater knowledge and reward, and also includes two exclusive gameplay challenges for players to undertake in Volume One.'),(13098,'Cover','Welcome to the world of Ane Moni. By possessing this here COMIGAME, you gain the ability to control Kotharan the Weasel, an aspiring Adventurer in pursuit of Quests, desperately trying to become a member of the most famed and prestigious guild of them all, the Adventurers Guild!<br><br>\n\nIt is YOU who control Kotharan\'s actions and his success or failure will be determined solely by YOUR own choices. Will you manage or have you already started wetting your pants?'),(13101,'Ad','Join Ned, Ruby, and Mungo the dog as they venture into a crazy, discombobulating maze! They\'re off on a code-cracking, maze-solving, clue-finding quest... Each puzzle is tied to the plot, so children can get really involved in the fun and exciting adventure story that runs throughout the book. Develops problem-solving skills and guarantees lots of puzzling fun for kids aged 7 and up.'),(13102,'Ad','Join Ned, Ruby, and Mungo the dog in the Mysterious Wood for a code-cracking, maze-solving, clue-finding dragon adventure... Each puzzle is tied to the plot, so children can get really involved in the fun and action-packed story that runs throughout the book. Develops problem-solving skills and guarantees lots of puzzling fun for kids aged 7 and up.'),(13103,'Ad','Join Ned, Ruby, and Mungo the dog as set off on a trip to south America, in search of high adventure! They\'re off on a code-cracking, maze-solving, clue-finding quest... Each puzzle is tied to the plot, so children can get really involved in the fun and exciting adventure story that runs throughout the book. Develops problem-solving skills and guarantees lots of puzzling fun for kids aged 7 and up.'),(13104,'Ad','Join Ned, Ruby, and Mungo the dog as they set the ride of a lifetime, aboard a flying castle! They\'re off on a code-cracking, riddle-solving, clue-finding puzzle quest... Each puzzle is tied to the plot, so children can get really involved in the fun and exciting adventure story that runs throughout the book. Develops problem-solving skills and guarantees lots of puzzling fun for kids aged 7 and up.'),(13105,'Ad','Join Ned, Ruby, and Mungo the dog as they set off on an incredible treasure hunt! They\'re off on a code-cracking, maze-solving, clue-finding quest... Each puzzle is tied to the plot, so children can get really involved in the fun and exciting adventure story that runs throughout the book. Develops problem-solving skills and guarantees lots of puzzling fun for kids aged 7 and up.'),(13106,'Ad','Join Ned, Ruby, and Mungo the dog as they venture into a strange hotel! They\'re off on a code-cracking, maze-solving, clue-finding puzzle quest... Each puzzle is tied to the plot, so children can get really involved in the fun and exciting adventure story that runs throughout the book. Develops problem-solving skills and guarantees lots of puzzling fun for kids aged 7 and up.'),(13110,'Ad','Join young detectives Josh, David, and Lilly (and David\'s pet cockatoo, Robinson) as they decipher a mysterious message in a glass bottle washed up on the beach, find the thief who stole a precious artifact from a monastery, solve the mystery of the kidnapped prize-winning rabbit, and hunt down a famous opera singer who has gone missing.'),(13111,'Ad','Josh, David, and Lilly are on the case again, and they need your help! Join them as they catch a jewel thief at the opera, chase down a crook with a stolen bar of gold, uncover the truth behind a famous casino cheat who faked his own death, and hunt down a robber who snatched an antique golden scepter from a museum exhibit.'),(13112,'Ad','Help young detectives Josh, David, and Lily solve the mystery of a counterfeit coin, track down an international jewel smuggler, recover a diamond necklace stolen from an innocent old lady, solve a missing-person case, put a pickpocket behind bars, and find a missing horse.'),(13113,'Ad','Josh, David, and Lily solve the mystery of a missing will, find out who has been kidnapping the neighborhood dogs, discover who stole a bow and arrow from the police station and has been threatening townspeople with it, and why someone is dumping toxic waste into the river.'),(13114,'Ad','Join Ned, Ruby and Mungo the dog for a code-cracking, maze-solving, clue-finding puzzle quest! Unravel the riddle to open the magic box, decipher the code on the scroll inside and then follow the clues to work out where our heroes are going next! Each puzzle is tied to the plot, so children can get really involved in the fun and exciting adventure story that runs throughout the book. Guarantees hours of puzzling fun for kids aged 7 and up.'),(13119,'Ad','October 2020 during the COVID-19 quarantine a blogger finds a new way to express himself and come to grips with what his life needs.'),(13122,'Ad','To find freedom, you must leave behind everything you\'ve ever known. It is 1825. You and Ma have survived on the streets of London ever since the soldiers took Da away and you fled Ireland. Now, with Ma gone too, you find yourself facing life-and-death choices at every turn. Can you carry a secret treasure across the ocean and finally be reunited with Da? You\'ll be asked to betray your friends, survive storms at sea and attacks by bushrangers, and trust thieves. At every turn, the choice is yours. How far will you go for freedom?'),(13123,'Ad','To find freedom, you must leave behind everything you\'ve ever known. It is 2011. You want nothing more than to be a journalist in Somalia like your aunty. But the truth can be dangerous—and when you and your little sister are left alone, you find yourself facing life-and-death choices at every turn. Can you escape a terrorist organization and find a safe place to call home? You\'ll be asked to cross a desert on foot, hide below deck in a leaky boat, and put your life in the hands of people smugglers. At every turn, the choice is yours. How far will you go for freedom?'),(13124,'Ad','When you read this book, you are the main character, and you will make the choices that direct the plot. It is 1951. During the war, you rescued and hid an Australian airman near your small Italian village. He told you that you could be anything you dreamed of—but those dreams are fast slipping away. As you make the leap for life in a new land, you\'ll be asked to stand up to bullies, stage a mutiny, and make your contribution to one of the greatest engineering projects the world has ever seen. How far will you go for freedom?'),(13125,'Ad','The door in front of you is green and the brass number 62 hangs just below the peephole. Police tape stretches across the door frame in a zigzag pattern. The incandescent light to your left flickers. Something terrible happened here last night. For reasons you don\'t quite understand, you have to find out what it was. The Rooms is a horror novella in which you choose your course through the story and the decisions you make influence its outcome. Featuring nine possible endings and over seventy illustrations.'),(13132,'Ad','An unlikely invitation compels you to travel to the remote coastal town of Broodhaven to participate in a once-in-a-lifetime competition. There, you soon discover that nothing is as it seems. As you progress through each increasingly dangerous round of the contest, the secrets of the town and its noble families are slowly revealed. A hidden history conceals the truth of your own identity and the real reason why you were summoned here. That which sleeps awakens, and so it falls upon you to confront and overcome an ancient and unimaginable terror! Only you can unlock the past and break the dark cycle! A family legacy must be fulfilled. Destiny awaits! Can you stop the nobles of Broodhaven from unleashing a hideous chaos upon the world, or suffer a fate far worse than death?<br><br>\n\nIn this interactive gamebook, you make the decisions, and you suffer the consequences. Choose wisely or die trying!'),(13144,'User','You have been hired to investigate who is the rightful heir to a metal fabrication emporium.'),(13176,'User','Hide and Peep Thomas!, titled Hide and Peep Mystery in the US, is a booklet based on the 2012 special Blue Mountain Mystery. It is written in a choose-your-own-adventure format and involves turning pages to help Thomas find Luke in the Blue Mountain Quarry.'),(13177,'User','Agents from an empire of half-snake, half-human beings have taken your brother prisoner to a distant island. You must journey to the island and rescue him.'),(13187,'User','The title is a literal translation of the German original \"Der Kampf der Hexen\".'),(13209,'Ad','It\'s the first game ever for the Scorpions Under 14s Girls team, and they\'re up against reigning premiers, the Ravens. YOU can choose what happens in the game. Will you help the Scorpions to their first win? It\'s up to you!'),(13211,'Ad','Play the main character in your own adventure story! Each richly illustrated situation includes a disaster, and you must choose between three options for survival. As you choose, you\'ll learn real-world survival skills as well as facts about wild animals, natural disasters, and everyday accidents.'),(13264,'User','This autobiography discusses Flint Dille\'s gamebooks and novels and his relationship with Gary Gygax and TSR, among other topics.'),(13394,'Ad','<p><i>Fox Spirit: A Two-Tailed Adventure</i> is a 250,000-word interactive fantasy novel by Amy Clare Fontaine, where your choices control the story. It\'s entirely text-based, without graphics or sound effects, and fueled by the vast, unstoppable power of your imagination.</p>\n\n<p>Seek the mystical Star Ball that will grant you immortality. It is hidden somewhere in Hoshimori, the human village where your family was killed.</p>\n\n<p>Weave illusions, shapeshift, or control minds! Will you become a benevolent guardian, a playful trickster, or a fierce demon? Avenge your family or strive to change their killer\'s heart? Beguile a human love interest or woo a vulpine mate?</p>'),(13433,'Ad','How will your night out end?<br><br>\n\nYou make the rules.<br><br>\n\nYou\'re at one of the hottest bars in town, all dressed up for a fabulous girls\' night out with your best friend, when she cancels. What do you do now?<br><br>\n\nIn this novel, YOU make the decisions.<br><br>\n\nWill you do body shots with a rock star? Cozy up to the hot bartender? Follow a mysterious woman to a rather unusual exhibition? Investigate a suave millionaire\'s box of tricks? Take a joyride with a buff bodyguard? Or maybe what you want is closer to home than you realize....<br><br>\n\nSo many options.... All you have to do is choose.'),(13434,'Ad','Wedding fever creates plenty of opportunity for heat in Helena S. Paige’s sexy and funny A Girl Walks Into a Wedding—the interactive erotic novel in which YOU, the reader, make all the rules...<br><br>\n\nYour best friend is getting married, and she’s asked you to be her bridesmaid. So many decisions: for starters, do you ask the gorgeous but mysterious man you met online to come as your date? Or do you go solo, giving yourself ample opportunity to kick up your heels and scope out the talent?<br><br>\n\nOnce the wedding weekend gets underway in a romantic country setting, all kinds of adventures on offer. Will you ditch your date? Duet with the hot DJ? Dodge the disreputable best man? Or perhaps the rugged pilot you meet in the bar will open up unexpected erotic opportunities - and who knew the maid of (dis)honor had such a sultry streak?<br><br>\n\nAll this while steering your way through the bachelorette party, the bride’s wedding jitters, the Dress From Hell, and more. Perhaps the most tempting option is to flee the entire affair with a tall, dark stranger … or maybe an old friend surprises you with a sizzling encounter.<br><br>\n\nYOU make the decisions—fulfillment guaranteed. It’s your fantasy. Your rules. The choice is yours...'),(13505,'Ad','This book lets you control William Shakespeare and make him punch a friggin\' shark. No other book in the world can make this claim. There are over forty endings for you to discover. Contains the choosable-path-adventure stories \"Willaim Shakespeare Punches A Friggin\' Shark\", \"Poor Yorick\", and \"That Time Samuel Ampson Got His Thumb Bit\".'),(13511,'User','While on a family vacation, you fall into a hole and find yourself trapped in a strange world populated by monsters.'),(13514,'User','This bonus adventure was originally intended to be part of <a href=\"/Item/12196\">The Dusk of Eternal Night (collector\'s edition)</a> but was moved here as the main adventure turned out to be longer than originally planned.\n'),(13519,'Cover','This is the first part of a two part game. In this first part, you will play the role of a young French Captain of Napoleon\'s army attempting to cross Saxony in 1813. The second part, which will be available in the next issue, is a solo scenario for Rebels & Patriots by Dan Mersey, but could probably be adapted to any black powder skirmish set. This first part is played like a choose your own adventure book. The opening paragraphs will explain the situation and eventually you will be offered a choice. Select the choice you want and turn to the paragraph indicated. Your choice will determine your forces and deployment when you play the second half of the game next month. Think of it as a sort of one man campaign game before the battle. You can, of course try again, if you\'re unhappy with your choices or if you die...'),(13525,'Ad','As part of a team, you have dealt with situations in Africa, Central America, Europe and the USA and as a team, you have completed these missions successfully, but sometimes a mission calls for something else, something more covert, under the radar and off the record and these missions call for a single professional to step up and do the job. You are the professional, a tier-one operator trained to survive in the harshest conditions against insurmountable odds…<br><br>\nYou are the Lone Wolf.<br><br>\nThe first of 3 books Operation Lone Wolf puts you in charge of a highly trained operator sent to retrieve highly classified material from an enemy research base. The book comes with all the rules to play as a solo operator and to even transfer a current Ghost Ops character into the role and out again to re-join your unit.<br><br>\nThe game uses a modified version of the FeralEngine which is totally compatible with the Core Ghost Ops rules and source material. As a player you follow along and make decisions similar to other choose your own adventure style books, all you need is a pencil and some dice.'),(13533,'Ad','Join Carmen Sandiego and decide where in the world to go next in this globe-trotting, daring caper Help Carmen save wild animals of all kinds, especially the rare Amur tiger cub kidnapped from you by VILE. With twenty possible endings, your adventures can take you all over the world--or out of the game. Which will you choose? In this choose-your-own-caper story set in the world of Carmen Sandiego, you are a junior zookeeper caring for a rare newborn Amur tiger cub. VILE, in its latest plot, is stealing exotic animals to sell to a billionaire collector, and your charge is cub-napped Carmen arrives and you decide the best way to get your cub back is to help her defeat VILE and rescue all the animals they\'ve captured. Or do you? Twenty different endings to this story keep readers coming back for more adventures with Carmen Sandiego.'),(13534,'Ad','Join Carmen Sandiego and decide where in the world to go next in this globe-trotting, daring caper Stop VILE from stealing the superior jetpack technology you\'ve developed and using it for nefarious deeds. With twenty possible endings, your adventures can take you all over the world--or out of the game. Which will you choose? In this choose-your-own-caper set in the world of Carmen Sandiego, you are unwittingly working as a technician developing a highly maneuverable jetpack for VILE. The prototype is almost complete when Carmen sneaks into your lab to steal it. That\'s when she tells you about VILE and their dastardly deeds. You decide to help Carmen try to keep this cutting-edge technology away from anyone who\'d use it as the ultimate thieving tool. Or do you? Twenty different possible endings keep readers coming back for more adventures with Carmen Sandiego.'),(13616,'Ad','A fully illustrated Adventure Game-Book based on many different conspiracy theories. Some of the theories may hit close to home, others will be extremely outlandish. Will you go down as one of the greatest leaders that America has ever seen? Or will you be despised by the population? Through your choices you will greatly influence the fate of all humanity! Choose well!'),(13637,'User','Your boring school day becomes much more interesting when you discover a doorway to a fantasy universe.'),(13645,'Ad','A new reading experience from horror author Matt Shaw. When the character rolls a dice to make his decisions for him, the reader rolls a dice too! Whatever the result on the dice is where the story steers! EXTREME HORROR.'),(13654,'LC','Our story begins with Dr. Zomboss\' latest plan of evil genius -- disguising his zombies as each other, in an effort to confuse plants and plant pals Crazy Dave, Nate, and Patrice. Can the friendly fronds get past these dastardly disguises before the zombies sneak into Neighborville tourist attractions - and even Watson Elementary school - to unleash their hungry ways? Every major decision along the path will be made by you and determine if our horticultural heroes end up facing their unfortunate demise ... or victory! Eisner Award-winning writer Paul Tobin (Bandette, Genius Factory) collaborates with artist Kieron Dwyer (Captain America, The Avengers) for a brand-new interactive Plants vs. Zombies journey!'),(13712,'Ad','One puzzling mystery. Several slippery suspects. Endless possibilities!\n\nWelcome to Haventry, a town where the ordinary and extraordinary collide! With ghosts, werewolves and zombies living side by side, trouble is always brewing. And when a fiendish crime is committed, YOU are the detective in charge of the case.<br><br>\n\nDr Franklefink’s precious Monster Maker has gone missing and there are lots of suspects! Along with your yeti partner, it’s up to YOU to find the culprit. Should you trail Bramwell Stoker, the terrifying vampire, or Grundle and Grinola, the mischievous goblin twins? Should you follow up a lead about the cunning witches? Or will investigating the doctor’s monstrous son Monty lead you to the thief? YOU decide!<br><br>\n\nWith hundreds of paths to choose from and no dead ends, you’ll solve the mystery every time!<br><br>\n\nA fantastically imaginative detective story for readers looking for an interactive adventure.'),(13713,'Ad','One puzzling mystery. Several slippery suspects. Endless possibilities!<br><br>\n\nWelcome to Haventry, a town where the ordinary and extraordinary collide! With ghosts, werewolves and zombies living side by side, trouble is always brewing. And when a fiendish crime is committed, YOU are the detective in charge of the case.<br><br>\n\nThe Museum of Magical Objects and Precious Stones is putting on a special time-travelling showcase, but when the main exhibit is stolen, it’s up to YOU to find the thief. The Time Sponge has the ability to stop and start time for whoever squeezes it, so who has the strongest motive? The minotaur chief of police who has a lot on at work or the shoplifting band of mermaids? Should you trail the museum’s petrifying gorgon curator? Or could your very own yeti partner be responsible? YOU decide!<br><br>\n\nWith hundreds of paths to choose from and no dead ends, you’ll solve the mystery every time!\n\nA fantastically imaginative detective story for readers looking for an interactive adventure.'),(13841,'Ad','Corre l’anno del Signore 1520: un misterioso messaggio del tuo antico maestro e un’allusione alla sua enigmatica eredità danno il via a un angosciante viaggio nei segreti più riposti della magia e dell’occulto. Riuscirai a riemergere dagli oscuri baratri dei saperi proibiti?\n\nQuesto è un librogioco: si legge come un libro, si gioca come un gioco. Fa’ le tue scelte e vivi la\ntua avventura nel ruolo di protagonista.\n\nSarai in grado di risolvere il mistero delle 49 Chiavi?\nUn sistema di suggerimenti ti permetterà di proseguire nella storia se sarai in difficoltà.'),(13875,'User','You navigate your country\'s soccer competitions, beginning with five-a-side soccer until you reach the top division of professional soccer.'),(13889,'User','Interview with Sir Ian Livingstone on the Fighting Fantasy series.'),(13899,'LC','In this map-your-destiny book, you make the decisions as Barbie, a girl from Phoenix who finds herself tangled in teh life of an old friend, Mike. When you discover he\'s a member of a group called the Liners, who run a meth business out in the desert, you feel more helpless than ever. In a relationship wrapped in violence and addiction as well as love, you must discover your own sense of power.'),(13971,'LC','Text leads readers through a Jurassic Period adventure in which they can choose what to do and where to go next.'),(14097,'User','Top Trumps Card Game.'),(14137,'User','You work for the government and must successfully navigate your last day of work before leaving on vacation.'),(14152,'Cover','Un coraggioso rigattiere, una chimerica e misteriosa città da esplorare, quattro oggetti dal passato oscuro su cui fare luce: comincia così un insidioso quanto stupefacente percorso di scoperta dei pilastri dell\'esoterismo occidentale.\n\nGli arcani segreti di Carcosa vi attendono! Riuscirete a svelarli tutti?\n\nQuesto è un librogioco: si legge come un libro, si gioca come un gioco. Fa’ le tue scelte e vivi la tua avventura nel ruolo di protagonista.'),(14153,'Ad','Riccardo Cuor di Leone parte alla volta di Gerusalemme, guidando una delle più grandi spedizioni in Oltremare mai viste prima. È l’occasione per te, giovane cavaliere, di dimostrare il tuo valore e il tuo coraggio!\n\nRiuscirai a raggiungere la lontana Terrasanta?\n\nQuesto è un librogioco: si legge come un libro, si gioca come un gioco. Fa’ le tue scelte e vivi la tua avventura nel ruolo di protagonista.'),(14154,'Ad','A Sule quasi manca il fiato: \"C\'è qualcosa lì in fondo...\". D\'un tratto anche tu sei intimidita: che cos\'è questa stanzetta segreta? Davvero siete i primi a mettervi piede dopo migliaia di anni? \"Può essere pericoloso\" dice il tuo amico tra i denti. \"Non dovremmo entrare...\" \"Nemmeno un\'occhiata?\"\n\nCosa c\'è di meglio per concludere una vacanza in Egitto che intrufolarsi in una piramide appena scoperta e ancora semisepolta dalla sabbia? Se poi ad accompagnarti c\'è Sule, figlio di una guida turistica del luogo ed esperto di geroglifici e storie di faraoni, non c\'è nulla da temere. Ma forse non avete considerato l\'abilità degli antichi costruttori, che per proteggere il riposo eterno dei loro sovrani si inventavano passaggi segreti, botole nascoste e trabocchetti mortali. Per poter uscire vivi da questa trappola buia in cui ancora riecheggiano misteriosi sussurri, dovrete risolvere enigmi che attendevano da millenni, e stare bene attenti a dove mettete i piedi, perché nessuno sa cosa può accadere se un faraone assetato di vendetta viene risvegliato...'),(14155,'Ad','In gita scolastica, in compagnia del tuo amico più fidato, trasgredire le regole è quasi un dovere. E allora, nonostante i professori vi abbiano vietato di avvicinarvi troppo al castello abbandonato che sorge sulla collina, l\'occasione per scattare un selfie davanti alle sue antiche mura vi pare troppo ghiotta per lasciarvela scappare. Ma una semplice bravata potrebbe trasformarsi in una trappola che non lascia scampo. Sì, perché nelle segrete sotterranee piene di scheletri e nelle sale solo in apparenza abbandonate da secoli un vampiro avido della vostra energia vitale vi sfiderà senza sosta con i suoi enigmi. Risolverli potrebbe non bastare a salvarvi, perché una strana stanchezza vi sta togliendo le forze e, se non vi sbrigate a trovare il modo di scappare, rischia di travolgervi senza pietà.'),(14158,'Ad','The First Arcade Gamebook Experience! - An \'80s Videogame inspired Solo TTRPG project: experience the thrill of shooting and fighting, combined with a coin-op graphic!'),(14159,'Ad','The First Arcade Gamebook Experience! - An \'80s Videogame inspired Solo TTRPG project: experience the thrill of shooting and fighting, combined with a coin-op graphic!'),(14160,'Ad','The First Arcade Gamebook Experience! - An \'80s Videogame inspired Solo TTRPG project: experience the thrill of shooting and fighting, combined with a coin-op graphic!'),(14168,'User','Young heiress Dinah Wyck wakes up in a castle full of monsters with no memory of how she got there, and must recover her memories or remain trapped there forever.'),(14187,'User','An insane cult has taken over Dinah\'s school, and now she must make as many friends as possible before taking her turn in the campus kangaroo court.'),(14253,'Cover','Dalla streamer più seguita un libro a bivi dove tu se il protagonista.'),(14256,'User','The earliest printings do not have the subtitle \"Ewiges Blau\".'),(14424,'Cover','The design of multi-plot narratives presents a series of singularities and problems that have only been dealt with in technical literature. This manual deals with their creation in a practical way, with the aim of being a quick reference manual for professionals and aficionados.'),(14487,'User','This volume collects all 14 stories from the original run of Diceman, plus a Slaine adventure that was previously serialized in 2000 AD. The stories are grouped by character and do not reflect the publication order of the original five issues.'),(14547,'LC','Using clues derived from mathematical knowledge, Mathnet detectives Pat Tuesday and George Frankly solve a case involving a ventriloquist\'s stolen dummy and a suitcase filled with counterfeit money.'),(14606,'User','You receive a summons from the allegedly-cursed Haert Manor, and there are given an offer you can\'t refuse: succeed at a dangerous mission, and you will learn more about your forgotten identity.'),(14607,'User','Armed with a handful of clues, you head south, continuing the search for your own identity.'),(14608,'User','Your quest to rediscover your identity is nearly complete, but the shape it takes will likely surprise you.'),(14609,'Ad','Una foto preziosa da recuperare, due ex amanti, due cervelli finissimi che si sfidano! Sarai tu, Sherlock Holmes, in questo classico di Sir Arthur Conan Doyle rivisitato, ad avere la meglio come sempre? Oppure tu, Irene Adler, a infliggere al re dei detective l’unica, bruciante sconfitta della carriera? In uno SherBlock, puoi interpretare ben due protagonisti! Scegli da che parte stare, capovolgi il blocco e gioca!'),(14610,'Ad','Un sinistro criminale fa tremare Londra! Avventurati in questa storia avvincente, tra indagini, inseguimenti, deduzioni ed enigmi. Sciogli il mistero e risolvi il caso! In uno SherBlock, puoi interpretare ben due protagonisti! Coordina le indagini di Sherlock Holmes e del suo fidato amico, il Dr. Watson. Capovolgi il blocco e gioca!'),(14684,'Ad','Un epico torneo di basket sta per iniziare e la tua squadra è pronta ad affrontare rivali agguerritissimi.'),(14692,'User','Includes an interview with Doug Headline.'),(14693,'User','Includes an interview with J. H. Brennan.'),(14694,'User','Includes an interview with Steve Jackson.'),(14695,'User','Includes an interview with Joe Dever.'),(14696,'User','Includes an interview with Gildas Sagot.'),(14697,'User','Includes an interview with Dave Morris.'),(14698,'User','Includes an interview with Ian Livingstone.'),(14699,'User','Includes an interview with Marc Gascoigne.'),(14700,'User','Includes an interview with Jonathan Green.'),(14701,'User','Includes an interview with Ian Bailey.'),(14702,'User','Includes an interview with Mark Smith.'),(14708,'User','Includes an interview with Jamie Thomson.'),(14773,'User','This book is about a ghostly house and its motley crew of inhabitants: sleeping and waking ghosts, mysterious dolls, moldy milk - and YOU. Because you decide what happens! Just remember that if the story does not end well, you can always try again - there are over ten different endings!'),(14774,'User','This book is about a tasty looking house made out of gingerbread and candy, a happy gingerbread man, a wicked witch, prisoners - and YOU. Because you decide what happens! Just remember that if the story does not end well, you can always try again - there are over ten different endings!'),(14775,'User','This book is about hungry Raptors, curious Pterodactyls, a happy T-rex chick - and YOU. Because you decide what happens! Just remember that if the story does not end well, you can always try again - there are many different endings!'),(14776,'User','This book is about a video game, the cutest critter you have ever seen, dangerous enemies - and YOU. Because you decide what happens! Just remember that if the story does not end well, you can always try again - there are many different endings!'),(14777,'User','This book is about a brave girl, a resourceful grandma, a vicious wolf, a dark forest - and YOU. Just remember that if the story does not end well, you can always try again - there are many different endings!'),(14778,'User','This book is about a dangerous travel into the ocean deeps. There are sea monsters everywhere and YOU decide what happens!\nJust remember that if the story does not end well, you can always try again - there are many different endings!'),(14779,'User','This book is about a brave thunder god, a terribly frightened giant, a hungry worm - and YOU - because you decide what happens! Just remember that if the story does not end well, you can always try again - there are many different endings!'),(14780,'User','This book is about kids, a teacher, a Raptor in a hooded jumper - and YOU. Because you decide what happens! Just remember that if the story does not end well, you can always try again - there are many different endings!'),(14781,'User','In this book you are the hero and you are in control. Do you want to meet vikings, Romans or dinosaurs? Do you have the courage to see what is happening on Earth after 100 years? What about 1000? Just make sure you do not lose your time travel machine so that you can make it safely back home!'),(14782,'User','In this book, you are the hero and you are in control. You get sucked into a really dangerous video game and in order to make it back home you have to fight an army of zombies, escape cannibal plants, solve an unsolvable mystery, tame a dragon and win a national game in soccer!'),(14783,'User','In this book, you are the hero and you are in control. The scene is a submarine where three strange captains are in charge. You are invited onboard and during your trek through the ocean deeps you search for a sunken treasure, explore the deadly Bermuda triangle and chase the world\'s biggest sea-monster.'),(14784,'User','In this book, you are the hero and you are in control. But the mission is not easy. One day you wake up and nothing is as before. All the phones are broken. Social media does not work anymore. Video games have been erased. What on earth happened? You are charged with solving the mystery, as you have shown before that nothing is too complicated for you. Or is it?'),(14811,'User','Orpheus, son of the god Apollo, was the most talented musician of all time. His great love, the nymph Eurydice, suffered a terrible accident on their wedding day, and Orpheus was unable to accept her death. So, armed only with his lyre, he set out to venture into the Underworld to rescue her. Can you guide Orpheus on this daring quest?'),(14812,'User','A terrible plague is ravaging the kingdom of Ascan. Its source lies in the power of Galios, the Lich King, who is coming back to life. As one of King Throden\'s champions, you must venture into Galios\'s crypt and put an end to him.'),(14813,'User','You are the heir to a ruined and constantly endangered fief. Will you be able to manage it and prevent it from collapsing under the weight of war, hunger, and plagues?'),(14814,'User','In 1945, in the midst of post-war Spain, several groups of guerrillas are still resisting Franco\'s regime. One of their leaders, Juan Vacar, has been spotted near Montecastillo. Will you be able to find his whereabouts?'),(14815,'User','You are Chameleon, a young mercenary living at Hermes Naval Station. Thanks to your uncle Burak, you escaped death when the governor\'s wife sought revenge. Furious about her husband\'s affair with your mother, she tried to kill both you and her. Now, you survive by taking on jobs aboard your Lymanter fighter, which Burak bought for you with his savings. Your first goal is to pay him back by earning rewards from whatever missions come your way, no matter how shady they may be.'),(14816,'User','Malentin, son of Malerio and Malberta, returns to his village after deserting the army, thinking he will be safe there. However, upon arrival, he discovers that some unpleasant adventurers have settled there, and his uncle Bartoldo forces him to confront them and drive them away. Will he be able to defeat them and free Neversummer from their unwelcome presence?'),(14817,'User','The time has come. Since the virus spread to every corner of the world, many suspected it was not just a simple flu. After the discovery of the vaccine, it seemed under control, but you are about to discover the latest and terrible mutation of this invisible enemy that seems determined to win the battle against us. Will you be able to escape this nightmare?'),(14818,'User','You are Bill Lasker, a bitter, alcoholic ex-cop making a living as a private detective. One day, a heartbroken couple arrives at your door, mourning the death of their daughter, Aveline Waite. Her body was discovered in her room, showing signs of an opioid overdose. However, her parents insist that she despised drugs and would never have taken them willingly. Will you uncover the dark truth behind this case?'),(14819,'User','You are a brave sailor aboard a ship sailing the Pacific. After a pirate attack, you were kidnapped and later abandoned on Dead Man’s Island. Anyone who arrives there is doomed, for the Estantigua, a ghostly procession of restless souls, roams the island in search of the living to enchant and guide them to their deaths. Now, your only hope is to attract the attention of passing ships for rescue... or to break the curse before it claims you as its next victim.'),(14825,'Ad','Your name is Aria the Black. Your mother was burned at the stake for being a witch, and that has marked you with a lifelong stigma; you have always been seen as an outsider wherever you\'ve been. A pariah. Fate has come knocking at your door, and only YOU, as the protagonist of this adventure, can decide how to face it. For the outcome of Aria the Black\'s story will depend on your choices, your skills, and the fortune determined by the roll of the dice.'),(14826,'Ad','Ulrica blends history, epic tales, and fantasy. Grab a pencil, an eraser, and a few dice... and dive into an unforgettable adventure! It was meant to be the happiest day of your life, but the new lord changed everything. In God\'s name, he destroyed all you loved and made you an outlaw. You are Hilda, chosen by the Mother Goddesses, and you won\'t rest until justice is done. Now it\'s time to reclaim Ulrica, the sword of Count Gundemaro, and seek your revenge!'),(14827,'Ad','Welcome to the world of television!\n\nYou are one of the contestants in a TV show from a deranged future called Final Fight. Face ruthless competitors, killer robots, and deadly traps, with the chance to win a ticket to the Martian colonies, far from the polluted Earth. Five hundred million viewers are waiting for blood and mind-numbing commercials.\n\nWill you claim the title of champion, or end up as a laughingstock in the losers\' gallery?\n\nThe choice is yours!'),(14828,'Ad','The troops of the sinister Yrmill march across the vast lands of the kingdom of Aradamia, determined to destroy every league of fertile ground and exterminate all its inhabitants. Your name is Jarenna, and you serve under the command of the Duke of Vangen as the leader of a scout squad. Now that the ducal army has been mobilized to hold back the invaders at the Arender Pass, your orders are to advance with your scouts to survey the territory occupied by the enemy.\n\nWhat unspeakable horrors lurk in the wooded slopes of Arender?\n\nSoon, much to your dismay, you are about to find out...'),(14829,'Ad','They call you Hunter. In all your years of service, you never lost a target. You are the nemesis of those androids incapable of grasping the irony of an almost limitless life. Because when one of those silicon types starts to think too much, that’s when the real fun begins. After a long time out of work, you find out that someone wants to hire you. Apparently, your mysterious employer has some first-hand information: Vulka, the terrorist who killed a million spectators in a stadium, is hiding on your planet. Action must be taken quickly, before he commits another massacre.\n\nThe question now is, who will be the hunter and who the prey...?'),(14830,'Ad','Berlin, April 30, 1945. Soviet troops roam the streets of the German capital in search of final victory and valuable technological trophies. It’s a race against time, where the victor will go down in history forever, and not only the outcome of the war is at stake, but perhaps the fate of the world itself. You are Soldier Ivan Petrov, assigned to Commissar Solokov’s group, a shady character with precise orders: find the whereabouts of the mysterious Doctor Schweitzer and seize his secrets, preferably before anyone else does. It’s not about the atomic bomb. It’s worse. Soon, very soon, you’ll wish you had never enlisted...'),(14831,'Ad','Japan, second year of the Kōji era.\n\nMatsudaira Motoyasu, the young lord of the province of Mikawa, is now a hostage of the powerful daimyo Imagawa Yoshimoto, who aspires to rule the entire empire. You are Oyuki, a young shinobi in the service of Motoyasu. When Yoshimoto\'s troops enter your village and arrest your entire family, you are tasked with crossing the borders to warn Mikawa of the annihilation of your entire clan. Disguised as a traveling performer, you embark on a blind escape through the forest, on a journey that very well might be the last of your life. Will you accomplish your mission?\n\nOnly Heaven knows...'),(14832,'Ad','You wake up in the darkness.\n\nYou\'ve just had a serious car accident. Although you don’t seem to be injured, you can barely remember anything else, except that you saw a bright light shining above you just before you plunged down the embankment and ended up in a swamp.\n\nYou could call emergency services if you had your cell phone with you, but unfortunately, that\'s not the case. And then there’s the other thing. You can’t shake the feeling that someone—or something—is lurking around here. Something sinister, whose inhuman eyes keep watching you with curiosity from the murky depths of the forest.\n\nCome on, get out of the car. The night has only just begun for you...'),(14915,'User','This four-page booklet promotes the educational value of the series and includes three related classroom activities. It is undated but includes a list of all eighteen published volumes, so it must have been released toward the end of the series\' run.'),(14968,'User','You work for a company that offers guided tours of the USA to European vacationers. You are allowed to choose your next assignment from five options: two in New York City, one in Las Vegas, and two at the Grand Canyon, either on foot or by raft.'),(15012,'Ad','O ENIGMA DO SOL OCULTO\nO enigma do sol oculto is a gamebook: here, you decide the course of the story! Choose your archetype from detective, teacher, exorcist and military or build your own character sheet. Explore a complete rules system tailor-made for action adventures and supernatural horror and decide how to tackle each challenge. Discover the innovative legacy mechanics, which make each game influence the next, and build a unique saga. Deciphering the riddle of the Hidden Sun will be no easy task - but all of humanity depends on your success.\nSYNOPSIS\nThe 20s. The world is experiencing a period of prosperity, rocked by the golden age of jazz. A time of luxury, glamor and glittering lights. But every light casts shadows and, in the ancient city of Oxford, a young woman from the aristocracy has been taken by darkness.\nWhere is Elizabeth Holloway? From the wilds of the Irish countryside to the vibrant cabarets of Paris, the mystery will take you on an investigation across Europe. You will cross the borders of nations... and of Reality itself. As part of a clan of investigators, you agree to give your blood and sweat to solve this case. However, when the crime turns out to involve cruel cultists and ancient gods, that may not be enough. You may have to give your life.\nMORE INFORMATION\nThe book comes with a dust jacket/mini-poster + sticker booklet and envelope for legacy mechanics.'),(15030,'Cover','Meet Esther Starling, a witch, nerd and writer, very clever and not at all prudent; who investigates the mysteries of this mansion occupied by horrors from a past still present.\nThis is a gamebook, an interactive work in which YOU choose the protagonist\'s attitudes. It will be YOU who will rummage through haunted rooms, decipher secret codes, invoke magic and unravel the Enigma of Death.\nHave the courage to unravel this mystery.'),(15031,'Cover','Peter, Martha and Grandpa Braun are about to embark on a breathtaking adventure, and only you can help them cross the River Bells and discover the surprise that awaits them at the end of this journey! Following an ancient treasure map, you must be prepared to make decisions, overcome challenges and explore incredible places: discovering more about the region is essential for success!'),(15032,'Cover','One evening you are invited to a party in a luxurious, secluded condominium. At first you feel out of place among strangers, until you notice something even stranger and more dangerous than forced socialization - waves of zombies start spreading through the surrounding houses and streets. It\'s possible to find weapons here and there, but the great advantage of a gated community turns out to be its biggest problem - just as it\'s a difficult place to access, it proves difficult to escape from. You have to find a way out before it becomes an open-air graveyard, populated by horrible, bloodthirsty creatures.\nCERCADO POR MORTOS is a gamebook - a book in which you are the main character, making decisions that can lead to a happy ending or great failure. A pencil, paper, and a 6-sided die is all you need to venture into a world that is both realistic and fantastic - as if a zombie epidemic were to occur next night, as if the first zombies were the animated corpses of your next-door neighbors...'),(15033,'Cover','A gamebook is a work of fiction that allows the reader to participate in the story, making choices and decisions that can change the character\'s design.\n“Sobreviver” invites you to be a character in this story on day zero of a zombie apocalypse. Through your choices, you will find your way through this adventure in the chaotic scenario that has taken over the city of São Paulo.\nSo hurry up, you don\'t have much time, take only the most important things, make the right choices and good luck!\nCan you survive?'),(15034,'Cover','São Paulo. You and 80,000 other people arrive in the city to see the biggest geek event in the country up close. Excited, you wake up ready to meet your best friend and enjoy the comic book fair even more. The problem is that a mysterious disease starts infecting people overnight, making them act like the undead. On your cell phone, a confused message from your friend and no internet signal. You\'re alone in a chaotic São Paulo, fear creeps into your heart and the only question on your mind is: Will you be able to overcome the obstacles and challenges to escape the zombies while, above all, trying to SURVIVE?'),(15035,'User','Solo adventure found in the book \"Maturidade em pinceladas\". Probably the smallest solo adventure ever.'),(15036,'Cover','In UMA AVENTURA NO EGITO ANTIGO we are invited to learn more than just a piece of history, but the very thinking that the ancients used to solve “special” problems. Far beyond being an exercise in thinking, solving these problems could save an entire dynasty! Will you venture out to save not only our hero, but the whole of Ancient Egypt?'),(15071,'User','A mix-up of bags leads a man into a web of intrigue when he unexpectedly ends up in possession of a mysterious human skull.'),(15082,'Cover','Una isolata e misteriosa villa di montagna, un efferato omicidio e un unico sospettato: tu. Riuscirai a ricostruire l’intera vicenda e a scagionarti dalle accuse? Ma la via per la verità passerà attraverso l\'oscurità e l\'ignoto... Sei pronto ad affrontarli?\nUn giallo cerebrale e coinvolgente, dall\'autore del pluripremiato \'49 Chiavi\'. \n\nQuesto è un librogioco: si legge come un libro, si gioca come un gioco. Fa’ le tue scelte e vivi la tua avventura nel ruolo di protagonista.'),(15083,'Cover','Francia, fine Ottocento. Nelle rovine infestate dai rovi dell’abbandonato e tetro castello della casata Belmont, la bella Aurora, punta da una spina, sta per svegliarsi da un sonno centenario… Il sonno della non-morte! Tu sei Aurora: un tempo delicata principessa di Francia, ora trasformata in temibile vampira! Sei pronta a prendere in mano il tuo destino?\n\nQuesto è un librogioco: si legge come un libro, si gioca come un gioco. Fa’ le tue scelte e vivi la tua avventura nel ruolo di protagonista.'),(15084,'Cover','Milionari senza scrupoli e unicorni da salvare in questo primo caso per l’agente Tang. Ma attenzione: la notte di luna piena si avvicina! Chi terrà a bada i licantropi giù in città?'),(15085,'Cover','Halloween è alle porte e nessuno vuole perdersi il parco tematico inaugurato in città da Cenerentola; proteggere questo famoso personaggio delle fiabe sarà un gioco da ragazzi… O forse no?'),(15086,'Cover','Lo stalking è una faccenda seria, e lo è ancora di più se lo stalker è… un asino mostruoso! Quale segreto si cela dietro alle sue misteriose apparizioni?'),(15087,'Cover','È giunta la resa dei conti! Il diabolico milionario-stregone Santoleri sta per fare la sua mossa… La Magikal Crimes riuscirà a fermarlo in tempo?'),(15118,'Ad','È già da un po\' che il dubbio ti tormenta: e se stessi sognando? Ogni dettaglio sembra reale ma allo stesso tempo tante cose, troppe cose non tornano. Sentendoti un po\' sciocca ti dai un pizzicotto. Provi a chiudere gli occhi, a immaginare di alzare la testa dal cuscino, ma niente. Allora provi con un pizzicotto più forte, torci la pelle della mano fino a lacrimare. Ancora niente. Corri a perdifiato per le strade del quartiere, verso la scuola materna di tuo fratello. L\'orario di uscita è già passato da un pezzo quando varchi il cancello d\'ingresso. Ma perché le luci sono spente? Dove sono tutti? E dove si è cacciato Luigi? Mentre ascolti la sua voce che intona una cantilena dietro una porta chiusa a chiave, ti rendi conto che il tuo pomeriggio non andrà come avevi sperato. E ben presto capirai che un luogo di solito pieno di colori, giochi e risate può trasformarsi in un mondo cupo, dove realtà e fantasia si mescolano per far emergere le emozioni più segrete in fondo al cuore di un bambino. Per tornare alla luce, occorrerà usare la logica, non tralasciare alcun particolare e scavare nei ricordi, ma soprattutto sarà indispensabile guardare dentro di te per scoprire chi è la persona che vuoi essere davvero.'),(15120,'Ad','Il tuo primo ESCAPE BOOK! Giorgio e Lucia sono in gita con la loro classe al museo di storia naturale. Ma qualcosa dev\'essere andato storto, perché dopo essersi addormentati durante la proiezione di un video si ritrovano da soli. O meglio: nelle sale del museo si aggirano creature meccaniche fuori controllo, tra cui un implacabile uomo di Neanderthal con tanto di clava. Mettere fuori uso questi robot per uscire è possibile, ma servirà aguzzare la vista, essere rapidi e non dare nulla per scontato. Soprattutto sarà fondamentale mantenere il sangue freddo, come dei veri agenti segreti, anche perché quei ruggiti da dinosauro che provengono dal fondo del corridoio non promettono nulla di buono...'),(15166,'User','You have an opportunity to attend Jane Bingley\'s first Netherfield ball in this interactive <i>Pride and Prejudice</i> sequel.'),(15243,'Cover','One hole. Countless questions. And one truth, hidden in the darkness.\n\nAt the end of 1990, in the small village of Tsarichina, something began that would remain one of the most mysterious events in modern Bulgarian history. Soldiers and psychics unite around a strange mission - to dig up something buried deep beneath the ground. What exactly are they searching for? An extraterrestrial object? An ancient creature? Or a key to a past we are not ready to understand?\n\n“The Mystery of Tsarichina” is not just a gamebook - it is a journey through the labyrinth of human curiosity, fear, and hope.\n\nTurn every page into a step toward the unknown. But beware - some truths do not want to be unearthed…\n\nSomething is waiting down there…'),(15244,'Cover','Before you were ever known as the Avenger, before your quest for vengeance reshaped the world of Orb, you had to confront a great evil on the idyllic Isle of Plenty. You are the youngest of the five Initiates of the Inner Circle, all striving to become Grand Master of the Five Winds. Your journey will take you to ancient cities, across towering mountains, and into wild forests. In these lands, an evil presence lurks—determined to destroy you and your allies—and it will turn your trial into the greatest challenge you have ever faced.'),(15245,'Cover','The first issue of the magazine includes the medieval fantasy game-story “Bloody Snow” by Branimir Săbev, where Bulgarians, Byzantines, Ottomans, and Cossacks cross paths alongside a wide variety of mythical creatures. This is followed by the short story “On the Power of Imagination” by Vilian Stefanov, set in a typical Bulgarian reality.\n\nThe issue also announces the short-story competitions based on a book by Elena Pavlova and the Third National Gamebook Competition, as well as a prize game accompanying the review of “The Mystery of Tsarichina.”\n\nOn the following pages, readers will find information about the series “The Way of the Tiger” and thematically related materials on D&D, Samurai and Ninja gamebooks, along with a glimpse into the world of James Clavell, creator of Shōgun and its film adaptations.\n\nThe final article also mentions the samurai rabbit Usagi Yojimbo, a popular comic-book character and kindred spirit of the Ninja Turtles.'),(15246,'Cover','The second issue is thematically centered on the adventure stories of Alan Sharp: “The Gold of Abilene,” which tells a tale of cowboys, Native Americans, and a robbery of the state railway, and “The Tomb of Amenosis,” a journey to Egypt at the end of the nineteenth century. Both stories are illustrated by the renowned comic artist Evgeniy Yordanov.\n\nThe magazine also features biographical materials about Alan Sharp, as well as articles on the comics set in the world of Kull the Conqueror by Robert E. Howard, on the gamebooks from the American “Time Machine” series, and on the Bulgarian gamebook series about Ringlas, a kind of local counterpart to Kull. Included as well is the short story “And Three Fought Against Five Hundred,” set in the same world, by Elena Pavlova.\n\nThe remaining pages include a review of the gamebook “Ninja!” and a brief overview of Bulgarian gamebooks set in the Wild West.'),(15283,'Ad','An adventure at sea has led to disaster, and now YOU are adrift. Water surrounds you as far as the eye can see. How will you find your way back to land? What will you eat and drink? And how long can you last on your own in the ocean? It’s time to make some difficult choices. With some smart decision making and a little luck, perhaps you’ll be able to survive being lost at sea!'),(15284,'Ad','The sun beats down on YOU in the dry, barren desert. Somehow, you’ve found yourself lost there. How will you find water and protect yourself from dangerous animals? And will you be able to get help before it’s too late? It’s time to make some difficult choices. With some smart decision making and a little luck, perhaps you’ll be able to survive being lost in a desert!'),(15285,'Ad','Blinding snow and piercing wind whip at YOU. An ordinary day has turned into a life-or-death survival. How will you stay warm? Can you find shelter? And will you be able to get help before it’s too late? It’s time to make some difficult choices. With some smart decision making and a little luck, perhaps you’ll be able to survive being lost in a snowstorm!'),(15286,'Ad','YOU are lost in the unforgiving terrain of a mountain. Your survival is hanging by a thread. How will you get down? Will you be able to steer clear of dangerous animals? And will you be able to get help before it’s too late? It’s time to make some difficult choices. With some smart decision making and a little luck, perhaps you’ll be able to survive being lost on a mountain!'),(15290,'Cover','The third issue focuses thematically on gangster gamebooks and stories drawn from real life. The main game-story in this edition is written by Boris Vodenicharov, in which a young man is chosen to track down a rare collector’s postage stamp from the era of Tsar Ferdinand — read “The Imperial Series.” This is followed by two stories by Snezhana Tasheva about the apocalyptic end of the world and the discovery of new planets — though not necessarily inhabited by great intelligence: “The Moles and the End of the World” and “The Planet of Fools.”\n\nFurther on, readers will find an engaging article by David Walters — author of the gamebooks from the Way of the Tiger series, Ninja! and Avenger! — who was deeply moved by the gift we presented to him some time ago. A feature on Equus Art is contributed by Damyan Hristov – Yan. The issue also includes statistical materials about the “Old Wave” of gamebooks, an article on Magic cards by Garo Marukyan, coverage of the awards of the “Citadel” Club, and a piece dedicated to Ivaylo Runev and the IKFEP “IVAN EFREMOV” by Venko Dimitrov.'),(15328,'Cover','<p><b>A Mission to Save the Music and the Future of a Nation</b>\n\n<p>Dive into the interactive world of <i>Operation CanCon</i>, where your mission is to collect Canadian Content. Navigate Eighties music stores in search of iconic songs. The hope of a country\'s future will depend on preserving its cultural artifacts.\n\n<p>Using dice and a checklist, take your chances with the Sweep minigame, a treasure hunt where every roll reveals another hit. It\'s not all random chance, however. Your decisions really matter. Choose which tracks to target, which stores to visit, and how long to search. How will you spend your limited time in Toronto? Whether you play a single game or a multi-day campaign, you\'ll discover opportunities for tactics and strategy. Advanced modes, tweaks, and New Game Plus provide even more challenges.\n\n<p>Perfect for gamers, music lovers, and fans of Canadiana, <i>Operation CanCon</i> is a new take on nostalgia. With an interactive narrative, flexible gameplay, and customizable goals, it’s more than a game, it’s a retro celebration.\n'),(15329,'Cover','<p><b>It\'s Time to Take \"Shopping Local\" to the Next Level!</b>\n\n<p>Welcome back to the Nineties. Canada’s music scene is rocking, and the store shelves are packed with winners, if you\'re ready to roll. In <i>Operation CanCon</i>, you’re not just flipping through dusty bins, you’re chasing priceless cultural artifacts. As a lone collector on a mission, your goal is to target a checklist of tracks scattered in iconic Toronto shops.\n\n<p>Part interactive fiction, part solo roll-and-write game, every visit is a gamble, whether for ten minutes or a campaign. All you need to play is three six-sided dice and something to write with.\n\n<p><i>Operation CanCon</i> is your passport to an era of gone-but-unforgettable Canadian Content. The music that inspired a generation is ready to rise again, but it needs YOU to bring the decade back to life. Fully steeped in nostalgia, this standalone sequel to the Eighties original lets you relive a time when finding the right album seemed like fate.'),(15330,'Cover','<p><b>Drop the Needle on One Last Flashback. Game Time Canada!</b>\n\n<p>It all comes down to this: the final verse in <i>Operation CanCon</i>. Leap between two capitals, across two centuries, on a mission to recover dozens of Canadian Content classics.\n\n<p>All you need is something to write with and three six-sided dice to roll your way through eight record stores in search of national treasures.\n\n<p>Equal parts branching-path adventure and bin-diving minigame, this interactive journey is a nostalgic tour of Canadian music. Whether you play for the memories or simply to know the score, this gamebook is your ticket to the past and, hopefully, a future.'),(15331,'Cover','<p><b>A Very Festive Flashback!</b>\n\n<p>Celebrate the holidays in this <i>Operation CanCon</i> expansion. Part series sampler, part year-end surprise, this festive adventure sends you back in search of true north classics, seasonal songs throughout Canadian history, tucked between shops by an angel... or someone stranger.\n\n<p>This standalone supplement adds new variants to the original trilogy’s gameplay: Holiday Jackpot, an easy, feel-good spree of discovery, and White Elephant, a suspenseful swap-or-drop challenge. You’ll search for dozens of elusive tunes, attempt a scavenger hunt, and earn deeds to mark your holiday achievements.\n\n<p>This booklet is offered as a token of thanks for returning <i>OCC</i> fans, or a sampler for newcomers to the series. You can download the full contents for free as a PDF at LockdownLudonaut.com, or purchase a physical copy as a keepsake. All you need is something to write with, three six-sided dice, and the core rules from any <i>Operation CanCon</i> gamebook.\n\n<p>Bundle up! ’Tis the season for bin-diving!'),(15332,'Cover','<p><b>How many days since March 14, 2020?</b>\n\n<p><b>That\'s how long the lockdown has lasted.</b>\n\n<p>Swiss-Canadian author Derek Schraner presents <i>Hikikomori</i>, an immersive \"lucky lockdown life simulator\" inspired by the concept of social isolation. It offers a unique approach to balancing daily activities. Players complete a series of simple minigames representing different aspects of day-to-day life. What makes the gameplay challenging are the ever-evolving rules. In this interactive experience, decisions made each day reveal how those rules change over time.\n\n<p>Players will need six-sided dice and something to write with, as they record their progress and track various activities.\n\n<p>At its core, <i>Hikikomori</i> is a meditation on balance. It explores the tension between conflicting obligations and the pursuit of fulfilment in routine. It is the culmination of the author’s experience living this way for five years, offering personal reflection, and inviting you to share in the challenges and insights of the journey.\n'),(15333,'Cover','<p><b>Spring Break in Hawaii is no vacation.</b>\n\n<p>You think it\'s just another job. It isn\'t.\n\n<p>You\'re a small-time thief in paradise, chasing a fresh start, when a pawn shop heist goes sideways and drags you into a more challenging score.\n\n<p>This is where it all begins. Before the Alps, before the casino, and even before Kyoto, this prequel to the <i>Break</i> system series follows the run that started everything... the one that nearly broke the game before you made a move.\n\n<p>Spring into action. Break the system.\n\n<p>Your epic adventures start here.\n'),(15334,'Cover','<p><b>Summer in Kyoto. The City is Alive... with Danger!</b>\n\n<p>An international syndicate has set its sights on a heist in the heart of Japan, and YOU are the fledgling thief at the center of it all. It isn’t just their mission; it’s your adventure.\n\n<p>As the <i>Gion Matsuri</i> festival pulses through the streets, you’ll face unexpected twists that could change everything for your future. Every decision made affects the world, your path... and the end. Dozens of different stories are waiting for you.\n\n<p>Set against the vibrant backdrop of Kyoto’s most famous festival, <i>The Summer Job</i> is the first <i>Break</i> system gamebook. Accessible, fun, and full of surprises, the unexpected is waiting. Ready to roll? The heat — and the heist — is on!'),(15335,'Cover','<p><b>Unfinished business at an unfinished casino!</b>\n\n<p>Your mission takes you away from the bustling streets of Kyoto to a long-abandoned casino in Ontario. It\'s the weekend after Halloween, and the chill isn\'t from the autumn. Your target: a doomsday device with a secret link to your past. Its lingering effects make even the simplest things terrifying. With the stakes now higher than ever, success may cost more than expected.\n\n<p><i>The Fall Affair</i> is a standalone trip in the <i>Break</i> system series. A six-sided die is recommended, but not required for your journey. The gamebook also includes several additional activities, from bonus mini-games to a curated musical playlist.\n\n<p>The heist is on and, this time, it will haunt you!\n'),(15336,'User','<p><b>The math says no. The season says yes.</b>\n\n<p>An impossible opportunity lures you from the streets of Toronto to the treacherous peaks of Switzerland in mid-December. You can\'t resist the target -- something you thought was lost forever -- but traps lie in wait. The enemy knows you’re coming.\n\n<p>Surviving alone may be possible, but it would take a miracle. Success demands more than skill and luck. You\'re going to need some allies.\n\n<p><i>The Winter Mission</i> marks the conclusion to the <i>Break</i> system series of gamebooks. With branching choices, dice-based challenges, and new crew management, this adventure will test every lesson you\'ve learned, with every move you make.\n\n<p>The dead of winter. The heart of Helvetia.\n\n<p>A holiday heist to remember.\n'),(15337,'Cover','<p><b>Some plans were made to be broken...</b>\n\n<p>Claw your way from low-level operative to master strategist in <i>The Break System</i>, a solo heist adventure. Scout, negotiate, infiltrate, and (hopefully) escape! Every decision shapes your experience. How will you manage your timeline? How will you spend your loot? Do you have what it takes?\n\n<p>You won’t be without resources. <i>The Spring Break</i> prequel story is included with new annotations to guide your early steps. Key moments reveal their mechanics and show how chance and choice shape a mission. You don’t need to study the rules upfront; they’re introduced gradually. Take it slow or jump ahead. In this heist, you call the shots.\n\n<p>Beyond the tutorial, the full <i>Break</i> system offers a self-paced framework for roll-and-write campaigns of increasing challenge. Six-sided dice and tactical decisions keep you on your toes, while you track your progress, building your reputation. Even failure isn’t the end; here, learning beats luck. Adapt your plans and carry on to master the art of the steal.\n\n<p>In <i>The Break System</i>, the end is just a beginning.\n'),(15343,'Ad','Explore an enchanting world, learn magic, craft potions, fight monsters, and discover secrets in this open-world, story-driven game about becoming the first witch in over 100 years.\n<br>\nThe famous island of Coven Cove was once home to all the witches of the world. People travelled far and wide to visit the mystical magic makers, seeking all manner of things: from love potions to hair growth spells, from get-rich-quick rituals to the occasional “turn my annoying sibling into a frog” charm. That, however, was over a century ago. The witches are all gone, and the mysterious island is now a mere tourist attraction.\n<br>\nUntil now.\n<br>\nBe it a mistake or fate, a young adventurous girl named Reni has awakened her magic, becoming the first witch in over one hundred years. There’s just one problem: Reni was only supposed to be visiting the island for the summer, but it turns out, witches are magically bound to the island—forever.\n\n<br>\n\nStep into Reni’s boots and embark on an epic adventure in Witchbound, a captivating story-driven game set in a vibrant world brimming with mysteries and dangers. Explore a charming village full of whimsical characters, and venture beyond the safety of its walls into the wilds to discover what the witches left behind. Collect items, learn spells, craft potions, and make impactful decisions that will shape Reni’s journey and the world around her!'),(15351,'Ad','It’s 1929. You are Captain Sofi Odessa and her crew lost at sea in a strange world.\n\nAboard the steamship Manticore, you must work together to survive by exploring mysterious islands, battling creatures, and meeting the world’s inhabitants. Along the way, seek out the totems of the gods.\n\nWake the gods and perhaps you’ll be able to return home.'),(15352,'Ad','It’s 1937. Explore a massive, open world in a game atlas of connecting maps.\n\nEncounter deadly monster, mysterious characters, lost ruins, and mystical treasures in a storybook filled with multiple choices and endings.'),(15353,'Ad','Expands the world with a second atlas, accompanying storybook, new adventure cards, enemies, events, and more.'),(15354,'Ad','Explore a treacherous river that winds through lush jungle. Be careful of the dangerous creatures beneath the murky waters. Will you survive or will you become a yet another victim of the river?'),(15363,'Ad','Exciting board game with an adventure factor! The players awaken in a dark dungeon. The way out seems impossible, especially since no one can remember what happened before. Similar to an adventure PC game, players must now explore the location, talk to people, find clues, combine objects, and uncover secrets. This way, they gradually unravel the story and can (hopefully) escape. Exciting until the very last move. A board game in three chapters for ages twelve and up, with simple rules – let\'s go!'),(15364,'Ad','The adventure begins! In this thriller, players break into a research facility of Monochrome AG. Once there, they are on their own. Similar to a PC game, players must now explore locations, combine objects, find clues, and talk to people. Only then can they gradually uncover the connections. A cooperative board game in three chapters, for ages 16 and up, with simple rules and exciting until the very end!'),(15365,'Ad','Attention brave adventurers! With the cooperative board game \"Grand Hotel Abaddon,\" players aged 12 and up experience an eerie adventure. To uncover the strange events taking place in the old building, they must explore their surroundings step by step and cleverly combine objects – just like in a point-and-click adventure. Success in this adventure game is only possible by working as a team! Each player takes on a role, follows clues, and makes decisions in consultation with the other players, determining the course of the story. In addition to the instructions and adventure book, cards, items, and location boards help to discover and experience the mystery story. An analog PC game that provides excitement from the first to the last move!'),(15366,'Ad','\"Adventure Games - The Volcano Island\" is a cooperative experience game. It works like a PC game – just in analog form. Simple rules allow the board game to start quickly. Players slip into the roles of four students who are on the trail of smugglers and mysterious events on a volcanic island. Like in a detective story, they have to solve puzzles, follow clues, examine and use objects, and make decisions that influence the course of the adventure. In doing so, they experience a story together. The gameplay is variable and plays out differently in every group, also due to the two different final chapters. If desired, the texts can be read aloud via app. Another exciting team experience from the series of cooperative event games from KOSMOS!'),(15367,'Ad','Turbulent times in Gloom City! In three chapters, players will tackle a complicated case that puts them in great danger themselves. Who brought the hostages to the abandoned asylum? Only as a team can the culprit be found. To do this, players go on a search for clues in the cooperative experience game, solve puzzles, scour multiple locations, and meet residents of Gloom City. Each player takes on a specific role in the analog PC game. How does the story end? That\'s up to the players. Because all decisions are made together. Mystery and Crime - an unforgettable game night awaits!'),(15368,'Ad','Tainted Grail: the Fall of Avalon is an unforgettable, solo or cooperative adventure experience for 1-4 players. Blending Arthurian legends and Celtic mythology with a unique vision, allows you to impact the game world in deep and meaningful ways.'),(15369,'Ad','Tainted Grail: Kings of Ruin is a new stand-alone game built upon 3.5 years of experience we gained in developing Tainted Grail adventures. As always, it will take you neck-deep into an amazing story, designed and written by Krzysztof Piskorski (Tainted Grail, ISS Vanguard) while offering the most polished gameplay so far in the Tainted Grail saga.'),(15370,'Ad','An entirely new, full campaign<br>\nSet 400 years after the Core Box storyline<br><br>\n\nThese 220 pages of The Last Knight Campaign are brimming with new interactions, choices, secrets, and long-term consequences of actions made 400 years ago, during the first campaign. You will now travel a cold, desolate landscape of apocalyptic Avalon in search of answers and - perhaps - salvation.'),(15371,'Ad','Go back 1000 years and be one of the first humans to set foot in Avalon. Discover the truth behind legends.<br>\nJoin the Knights of the Round Table in their quests and trials.\n<br><br>\n\nThese 220 full-color pages of the Age of Legends campaign are bringing you yet another treasure trove of interactions, choices, and secrets. This time, you will join first humans to set foot in Avalon, 600 years before the events of the first campagin, and see the Fore-dweller empire at the height of its power. Join Arthur and his knights in their trials and tragedies. Discover the truth behind your myths.'),(15372,'Ad','Travel to a continent ravaged by Red Death, discover the secrets of this plague and face the ultimate enemies in an expert-level campaign.'),(15375,'Ad','Learn about the Dreamers, their forgotten past, and their desperate mission. Uncover the surreal, sprawling dreamscapes. Just don\'t be surprised when, just like dreams often do, they become a little disturbing... Prepare to be challenged by escape-room-like riddles. Spot a clue in the image. See a hidden link between several pieces of information. Use your instinct as much as your logic.'),(15376,'Ad','You will take a part in the huge mask parade.<br>\n\nYou will be taking part in a mad race, chasing... something...<br>\n\nYou will visit an enormous junkyard, with something really evil waiting there.<br>\n\nyou will be looking for those, who you value the most and be able to witness just how much you really need them.'),(15377,'Ad','We will come back here many times to gigantic endless forests.<br>\n\nBut in addition, we will also visit a large greenhouse, where something really strange is growing from pots.<br>\n\nWe will resit in a sunny, quiet village, though not entirely peaceful, because even seemingly perfect places can hide disturbing secrets.<br>\n\nWe will take part in an accident on the road, we will run away from the pursuit of the crowd, we will watch how the setting sun changes the whole world around us.'),(15378,'Ad','You will visit the excavation station at the end of the world.<br>\nA cinema playing the most memorable hits from all decades.<br>\nYou will travel on a boat through a sea of mist.<br>\nSlide down in an elevator in the endless abyss.'),(15379,'Ad','We will climb the stairs and ride up in the old elevator to the highest floors of a crumbling, half-broken, block of flats.<br>\n\nWe will come across a strange cemetery, located on the roof of a building.<br>\n\nWe will visit the Museum of Death and the Great Cathedral.<br>\n\nWe will struggle with the snow void.<br>\n\nAnd we will take part in the game of hide and seek.'),(15383,'Ad','Arydia: The Paths We Dare Tread is a cooperative adventure game that will have you and up to three friends exploring the world of Arydia! The game can be played in any number of sessions, and is designed for you to easily save and store the game.<br>\n\nAs you play, the game keeps track of your actions and decisions. Your characters will grow in power, collecting new items, weapons, and skills!<br>\n\nMany of the locations you\'ll visit in Arydia are hostile. You will need weapons, skills, and cooperation to overcome the challenges you encounter!<br>\n\nArydia comes with 60+ pre-painted miniatures, 900+ cards, 300+ map cards, mulit-layer worldmaps, mul-layer player boards, and 40+ hours of hand-crafted gameplay!<br>\n\nWhat paths will you dare tread?'),(15384,'Ad','Enter a magical world of mythical beasts and ancient dragons in Dragon Eclipse, the exciting new board game for 1-2 players! Uncover the secrets of the eclipse that changed everything and discover the dangerous and treacherous world that awaits you.'),(15385,'Ad','Welcome to the enchanting world of Dragon Eclipse, where magic, adventure, and incredible creatures await! Whether you\'re stepping into this realm for the first time or returning as a seasoned Tamer, this campaign lets you experience both the original Dragon Eclipse and the new standalone sequel Dragon Eclipse: The Grand Quest.<br>\n\nThe Grand Quest takes you to an age of peace, honor, and fierce competition. As Tamers gather for the Grand Tournament, a dark Metal force rises, turning the contest into a battle for the world’s fate.Will you rise as a champion... or succumb to the coming darkness?'),(15386,'Ad','Vantage is an open-world, cooperative adventure game for 1-6 players designed by Jamey Stegmaier. Vantage features an entire planet to explore, with players communicating while scattered across the world. With nearly 800 interconnected locations on cards and over 900 other discoverable cards, the world is your sandbox.<br>\n\nYou begin each game of Vantage on an intergalactic vessel heading towards an uncharted planet. After crashing far from your companions, you have complete freedom as to how you explore, discover, and interact with the planet. You view your location from a first-person perspective–you can communicate with and support other players, but you are separated by vast distances, so only you can see your current location. <br>\n\nIn addition to a mission victory, a destiny victory, or an epic victory (completing both the mission and a destiny), you may define success in Vantage through anything you pursue and achieve.'),(15387,'Ad','Earthborne Rangers is a customizable, cooperative, adventure card game set in the wilderness of the far future for 1 – 4 players. You’ll begin by building a deck that reflects your character’s personal history. Then, as you explore the open world and your story takes shape, you’ll augment your deck with improved equipment, refined skills, and the memories of your journey.'),(15388,'Ad','Continue your Rangers’ adventures as you journey beneath the surface of the Valley and uncover the secrets of the Ancient Estian Arcology. Delve into the arcology’s subterranean caverns and corridors to explore new locations and path sets. This expansion includes new story missions, side activities, reward cards, a new map, and dedicated campaign guide.'),(15389,'Ad','1907. A renowned explorer, you have just come back from the first expedition on the seventh continent, a mysterious land that was recently discovered off the coast of Antarctica. Lift curses or die trying in the first “choose-your-own-path” exploration board game.'),(15390,'Ad','The 7th Citadel is an all-new cooperative exploration and adventure game by the designers of The 7th Continent.<br>\nIn this post-apocalyptic medieval fantasy world, you play as a slave-gardener who just escaped from necrodruid Ninidazir’s citadel, only to find yourself faced with an even greater threat!<br>\nExplore the Collapsing Lands freely by gradually unveiling the board using numbered terrain and event cards. Interact with your environment and converse with its inhabitants.<br>\nAs the scenarios unfold, your choices, for better or worse, will lead you inexorably to the epic finale against the Threat!'),(15391,'Ad','Explore a strange land, battle fearsome monsters, and uncover ancient mysteries in this unique interactive gamebook with an integrated card game.<br>\n\nIn this story, you will play the role of a hex knight, gifted with combat skills and magical powers. You must venture into an unfamiliar continent to discover the secrets of the mysterious Clockwork City. On every page, you\'ll be faced with decisions that will change the course of your journey.<br>\n\nIf you engage in battle, deal yourself a hand of cards! Combat is resolved with the 52 combat cards included in the box—so the key to winning is not the luck of a dice roll, but skillful card play.'),(15392,'Ad','In Lost in Adventure, you explore an unknown world together, where your every action determines the story\'s unfolding. Discover the game scenario as you go, placing cards side by side, talking to people, collecting clues, and using objects wisely: your decisions will influence the adventure and lead you to one of the endings.\nThe myth of the labyrinth has fascinated the whole world for centuries: dress up as the hero of the story, and dive into the search for the Minotaur in an adventure that runs in the balance between myth and reality.'),(15393,'Ad','Lost in Adventure – The Curse of Jack Parrot is a cooperative narrative board game designed for 1-6 players ages 10 and up. Ideal for those who love graphic adventures, strategic choices, and shared exploration.<br><br>\n\nFollow in the footsteps of the infamous Jack Parrot on a journey through mysteries, dangers, and ancient legends. Discover the scenario as you go along by placing cards side by side, collecting items, talking to characters, and choosing how to interact with them: every decision changes the course of the story. That\'s why no two games are the same!<br>\nThis second chapter of the Lost in Adventure saga offers an immersive experience with short texts, intuitive rules, and a strong visual impact. Created by Marco Pranzo and illustrated by Michael Menzel and Alberto Bontempi, it is perfect for playing with friends... or alone!'),(15395,'Ad','Lost Ones is a stunningly illustrated, fully cooperative game where 1-4 players take on the role of a young person who finds themselves in a nightmare, inexplicably taken to the Fae world, and are trying to find a way home. <br><br>\n\nPlaying a character, you must use your mental and emotional resolve (in the form of action cards) to solve riddles, defeat foes, acquire boons, and explore the map. As you travel, place new map tiles that unravel the mystery of this land, by reading the matching page in the Story Book. This narrative will give you choices of how you may interact with the magical creatures you encounter. Every choice may be a piece of the puzzle to find a way out, or it may be a trap to keep you in the Otherworld forever. You must consider your choices carefully, and spend your resolve wisely, or forever be a Lost One.'),(15401,'Ad','Discover the first adventure in the BACKSTORIES Saga: Alone under the Ice!\n\nBackstories is a game with mechanisms as simple as they are revolutionary: a bit like you would do in a Point and Click video games, interact with your environment as you progress through your thrilling adventures. Some cards (Panorama) represent the environment in which you’re evolving. Other cards (Actions) are perforated, and represent the actions you can perform (Talk, Search, Objects in your possession, etc.). To interact, all you have to do is place a perforated card on the back of the Panorama card you’re interested in, then turn the card over and read the result of your choice.\nBe careful, though: in every scenario you play through, each of your choices will have real consequences… Be ready to face them!\n<br>\nIn Alone under the Ice, you play the role of Sophie. Set out to find your brother Jean, who has disappeared under mysterious circumstances. The latest news you’ve received comes from a refuge on the summit of Mont-Blanc, via a letter Jean sent you. It seems he was looking for a treasure lost since the 1940s: The amber Chamber!\n<br>\nNow it’s up to you!\n<br>\nAnd remember: Your choices, Your Adventure!'),(15402,'Ad','A hard drive of vital importance to the security of the entire planet has been stolen by the terrible General Darcosa.\nPlay as Nyx, a…very special agent, and try to carry out this perilous mission.\n<br>\n\nDiscover the second adventure in the BACKSTORIES series, with this new installment entitled The Emerald Wedding Anniversary!\n<br>\nBackstories is a game whose mechanics are as simple as they are revolutionary: in the manner of Point and Click video games, interact with your environment to advance your thrilling adventure. Certain cards (Panorama) represent the environment in which you’re evolving. Other cards (Actions) are perforated, and represent the actions you can perform (Talk, Search, Objects in your possession, etc.). To interact, all you have to do is place a perforated card on the back of the Panorama card you’re interested in, then turn the card over and read the result of your choice.\nBe careful, though: in every scenario you play through, each of your choices will have real consequences… Be ready to face them!\n<br>\nIn Les Noces d’Emeraude, you play the role of Agent Nyx. During a high-flying mission, try to foil the plans of the sinister General Darcosa, by stealing the Top Secret hard drive in his possession.\n<br>\nNow, it’s up to you.\n<br>\nAnd remember: Your choices, Your Adventure!');
