INSERT INTO `Links` VALUES (1,'Flying Buffalo','http://www.flyingbuffalo.com/','This long-lived adventure game company sells solitaire adventures for the <a href=\"/Series/111\">Tunnels & Trolls</a> RPG along with some <a href=\"/Series/49\">Lost Worlds</a> books.','2019-04-12',1),(2,'Lairs.com TomeHoard','http://www.lairs.com/tomehoard','This online book store sells nothing but gamebooks!! Check it out if you need to fill in some holes in your collection; it mostly sells American books, but there are some nice rarities mixed in...','2004-06-09',1),(3,'Gamebook Collectors Yahoo! Club [Dead Link]','https://web.archive.org/web/*/http://clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/gamebookcollectors','This Yahoo! club encouraged gamebook trading, but it no longer exists.','2017-12-07',1),(4,'Wayne\'s World of Books - Krakow RPGs','http://www.waynesbooks.com/KrakowRPGs.html','This page mostly offers links to places where you can buy old RPG items, but the occasional gamebook is included among the listings, and site\'s owner is willing to help track down specific titles (though a donation for the service is appreciated).','2004-06-09',1),(5,'Richard A. Bartle','http://www.mud.co.uk/richard/','This page belongs to the author of the early solo role-playing effort, <a href=\"/Series/392\">The Solo Dungeon</a>.','2004-06-09',2),(6,'Kelly Bennett\'s Facebook Page','https://www.facebook.com/Kelly-Bennett-Artist-Illustrator-180800388759131/','This gallery provides some artwork by the illustrator of the <a href=\"/Item/1605\">Daniel the Pirate</a> <a href=\"/Series/49\">Lost Worlds</a> book.','2025-02-16',2),(7,'Herbie Brennan\'s Bookshelf','http://www.herbiebrennan.com/','This is the official home of Herbie Brennan, creator of <a href=\"/Series/188\">Grailquest</a>, <a href=\"/Series/203\">Horror Classics</a> and other gamebooks.','2004-06-09',2),(8,'Andrew Chapman\'s Blog','http://andrew-e-chapman.blogspot.com/','This blog belongs to Andrew Chapman, author of several <a href=\"/Series/11\">Fighting Fantasy</a> gamebooks.','2016-05-27',2),(9,'Clayton Emery\'s Page','http://www.claytonemery.com/','This is the home of one of the co-authors of the first <a href=\"/Series/34\">Amazing Stories</a> book.','2004-06-09',2),(10,'Michael Fishel - Classic Fantasy Art','http://larklanegallery.com/stuff/fishel.htm','This page contains some work by <a href=\"/Series/151\">Fantasy Forest</a> illustrator Michael Fishel.','2004-06-09',2),(11,'Carol Gaskin - Editorial Alchemy','http://www.editorialalchemy.com/','This page offers editorial service from Carol Gaskin of <a href=\"/Series/8\">Forgotten Forest</a> and <a href=\"/Series/78\">Time Machine</a> fame.','2014-12-31',2),(12,'Jim Gasperini\'s Page','http://www.well.com/user/jimg','<a href=\"/Series/78\">Time Machine</a> author Jim Gasperini maintains this page to keep track of his various projects and interests.','2004-06-09',2),(13,'Rita Golden Gelman, Female Nomad','http://www.ritagoldengelman.com/','This site belongs to Rita Golden Gelman, co-creator of the <a href=\"/Series/29\">Which Way</a> series.','2004-06-09',2),(14,'Griffon\'s Aerie [dead site; in Wayback Machine]','https://web.archive.org/web/*/http://www.destinyrealms.com/griffon/','This is the home of Peter Schweighofer, the author of several Star Wars-themed solo adventures, among other things.','2004-06-09',2),(15,'John Higgins - Turmoil Colour Studios','http://www.turmoilcolour.com/','This page belongs to <a href=\"/Series/188\">Grailquest</a> illustrator John Higgins.','2004-06-09',2),(16,'Peter Andrew Jones\' Page','http://www.peterandrewjones.net/','This page is the home of noted <a href=\"/Series/11\">Fighting Fantasy</a> illustrator Peter Andrew Jones.','2004-06-09',2),(17,'Marc Kornblatt\'s Page [Dead Link]','https://web.archive.org/web/*/http://www.marckornblatt.com/','A former <a href=\"/Series/78\">Time Machine</a> author, Marc Kornblatt has moved on to filmmaking. His personal domain name is no longer active as of this writing.','2017-12-07',2),(18,'Emily Drake [archived page]','https://web.archive.org/web/20040924172919/http://www.magickers.com/','This page was the official site for <a href=\"/Series/121\">Dragontales</a> author Rhondi Vilott, who now writes non-interactive fantasy novels under a pseudonym.','2004-06-09',2),(19,'Nancy Lamb\'s Page','http://www.nancylamb.com/','This site belongs to Nancy Lamb, co-creator of the <a href=\"/Series/29\">Which Way</a> series.','2004-06-09',2),(20,'Kim Newman & Eugene Byrne: The Alternate History Pages','http://www.angelfire.com/ak2/newmanbyrne/','This page is run in part by <a href=\"/Series/2\">Life\'s Lottery</a> author <a href=\"/Person/1\">Kim Newman</a>.','2004-06-09',2),(21,'Panurgic Publishing [Dead Link]','https://web.archive.org/web/*/http://www.tcp-ip.or.jp/~panurge/','This site belongs to <a href=\"/Person/3\">Paul Mason</a>, <a href=\"/Series/11\">Fighting Fantasy</a> author and <a href=\"/Series/463\">Virtual Reality</a> republisher.','2017-12-07',2),(22,'Alex Price Creative','http://www.alexpricecreative.com/','Here you\'ll find information on the company run by <a href=\"/Series/8\">Forgotten Forest</a> illustrator <a href=\"/Person/27\">T. Alexander Price</a>. The site includes pictures from the series.','2004-06-09',2),(23,'Shiga Books','http://www.shigabooks.com/','This page is run by Jason Shiga, designer and publisher of a number of <a href=\"/Series/322\">nifty interactive comic books</a>.','2004-06-09',2),(24,'Jacques Terpant\'s Page','http://www.terpant.com/','The <a href=\"/Series/315\">La saga du Prêtre Jean</a> illustrator has a site here.','2004-06-09',2),(25,'Tracey West\'s Page','http://www.traceywest.com/','This site belongs to Tracey West, author of the <a href=\"/Series/385\">Scream Shop</a> series (among others).','2004-06-09',2),(26,'Chronicles of Arborell','http://www.arborell.com/','An original, online-only fantasy gamebook series can be found here!','2011-10-24',3),(27,'EnigmaQuest [Dead Link]','https://web.archive.org/web/*/http://www.enigmaquest.btinternet.co.uk/','This online gamebook, which can be expanded by user input, is designed in the spirit of the <a href=\"/Series/213\">Knightmare</a> and <a href=\"/Series/98\">Crystal Maze</a> series.','2004-06-09',3),(28,'FightingFantasyGamebooks.com','http://www.fightingfantasygamebooks.com/','This is the official home of the Wizard Books <a href=\"/Series/853\">Fighting Fantasy</a> reprints.','2004-06-09',3),(29,'Knuckleduster Publications','http://www.knuckleduster.com/','This site is the official home of the <a href=\"/Series/215\">Knuckleduster Interactive Western Adventures</a>.','2004-06-09',3),(30,'lobo-solitario.com','http://www.lobo-solitario.com/','This is the Spanish-language home of <a href=\"/Series/228\">Lone Wolf</a>.','2004-06-09',3),(31,'Project Aon','http://www.projectaon.org/','This wonderful page provides free online <a href=\"/Series/228\">Lone Wolf</a> (and other) gamebooks, courtesy of author Joe Dever!','2004-06-09',3),(32,'Sryth: The Age of Igtheon','http://www.sryth.com/','This web-based game plays like a gamebook but takes full advantage of web browser features.','2004-06-09',3),(33,'Zork #3: The Cavern of Doom','http://www.boraski.com/zork/','You can play the third <a href=\"/Series/311\">Zork</a> book online here, and yes, it\'s legal!','2004-06-09',3),(34,'David Archwamety\'s Choose Your Own Adventure page','http://www.angelfire.com/ne/jackfrost/cyoa.html','Here are some reviews of the <a href=\"/Series/30\">Choose Your Own Adventure</a> books along with some useful information on the series.','2004-06-09',4),(35,'Never-Ending Story Engine','http://www.infinite-story.com/','This is an online community where members can collaboratively create interactive stories.','2004-06-09',15),(36,'Cyber Reviews - HeartQuest, The [Dead Link]','https://web.archive.org/web/*/http://cyberreviews.skwc.com/cr_heartquest_gamebooks.html','This page offers lengthy information and reviews relating to the <a href=\"/Series/196\">HeartQuest</a> series.','2017-12-07',4),(37,'Fang\'s Finest Emporium','http://www.fightingfantasy.org.uk/','This <a href=\"/Series/11\">Fighting Fantasy</a> site should appeal to more visually-oriented fans thanks to its interesting interface.','2004-06-09',4),(38,'FightingFantasy.Com','http://www.fightingfantasy.com/','This was the ultimate <a href=\"/Series/11\">Fighting Fantasy</a> site for a while, but it\'s gone into hibernation or something and hasn\'t been updated in ages. It\'s still worth a look, though.','2004-06-09',4),(39,'Fighting Fantasy Reviews Archive','http://user.tninet.se/~wcw454p/ff.html','This site collects fan reviews of <a href=\"/Series/11\">Fighting Fantasy</a> books from around the web.','2004-06-09',4),(40,'Lands of Shabak [Dead Link], The','https://web.archive.org/web/*/http://www.geocities.com/hughteg/','This content-rich Fighting Fantasy site features an original, full-length gamebook and some historical information that might be useful in a multiplayer campaign, among other things.','2004-06-09',4),(41,'Malédiction de la Momie (fan translation), La','https://web.archive.org/web/20040202085422/http://www.chez.com/dagonides/','This unofficial fan translation of <a href=\"/Series/11\">Fighting Fantasy</a> #59 into French was written before an official translation was produced several years later.','2023-12-27',4),(42,'Mansion of Maleficence','http://user.tninet.se/~wcw454p/mansion/mansion.html','This is a brief online horror gamebook by Per Jorner.','2004-06-09',4),(43,'Mantikora\'s Gamebook Library','http://gamebooks.mantikora.com/','This page includes reviews and links for free online gamebooks along with advice on gamebook-writing and other relevant material.','2004-06-09',4),(44,'Moloch\'s Gamebook Garden [Dead Link]','https://web.archive.org/web/*/http://clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/molochsgamebookgarden','This is a Yahoo! club devoted to gamebooks... It\'s definitely worth checking out if you\'re searching for other fans!','2017-12-07',4),(45,'MyAdventureGame.com','http://www.myadventuregame.com/','An online community for playing and designing gamebook-type adventures.','2004-06-09',15),(46,'QML: Create Your Own Adventure','http://www.questml.com/','This page is home to QML, an XML-based markup language designed to ease the creation and distribution of electronic gamebooks.','2004-06-09',15),(47,'Realm of Warhawk [Dead Link]','https://web.archive.org/web/*/http://www.jpatt.net/wh/realm/','This is an online collaborative gamebook project.','2017-12-07',4),(48,'Andrew Schultz\'s Gamebook Page','http://www.geocities.com/SoHo/Exhibit/2762/books/gamebooks.htm','This page has lots of <a href=\"/Series/311\">Zork</a> and <a href=\"/Series/6\">Be an Interplanetary Spy</a>-related information along with links to some humorous online gamebooks.','2004-06-09',4),(49,'Aaron Thorne\'s Gamebook Page','http://www.geocities.com/~athorne/gamebook/','This page offers a few reviews of gamebooks and useful links to other sites where gamebooks can be purchased.','2008-01-27',4),(50,'Xhoromag','http://www3.sympatico.ca/theoiseau','This French site provides several original online gamebooks.','2004-06-09',2),(51,'A.D.V.E.L.H.','http://litteraction.fr/presentation/livre-dont-on-est-le-heros/logiciels','This French gamebook creation system also includes an English version.','2013-05-11',15),(52,'Open Directory: Gamebooks Category','http://www.dmoz.org/Games/Roleplaying/Gamebooks/','This directory contains a list of additional gamebook-related links. It\'s worth a look if you\'re still not satisfied!','2004-06-09',5),(53,'Gamestalks.com Directory - Gamebooks [Dead Link]','https://web.archive.org/web/*/http://www.gamestalks.com/directory/Roleplaying_Gamebooks.html','A directory of gamebook-related web links.','2017-12-07',5),(54,'LIS News','http://www.lisnews.com','','2004-06-09',10),(55,'Phil Bradley\'s Blog','http://www.philb.com/blog/blogger.html','','2004-06-09',10),(56,'Project Gutenberg\'s Distributed Proofreaders Project','ht