s apparently never released in Argentina, but it did see publication in Mexico.',6),(2529,'Miscellaneous works by Roberto Fontanarrosa','This famous Argentinian cartoonist and writer authored a short story structured in a fashion similar to a Choose Your Own Adventure book. The story has no game system.',6),(2530,'Quest Path Fantasy','This ambitious free-roaming amateur series is planned to span over six volumes, but only the first one has been published.',1),(2531,'Fortean Times','One issue of this magazine contains an interview with Sir Ian Livingstone on the Fighting Fantasy series.',1),(2532,'Dark Roads','',1),(2533,'Miscellaneous Works by Steffie Brocoli and Catherine Bidet','',1),(2534,'Make Your Own Ending','',1),(2535,'Super Librogame Giunti','',5),(2536,'Shadows of Esteren','This RPG has produced one solitaire adventure.',1),(2537,'Miscellaneous Works by Karl-Heinz Zapf','',3),(2538,'Among Us','Il romanzo-game non ufficiale del gioco che ha conquistato il mondo',5),(2539,'Zio Paperone','',5),(2540,'Metal Heroes and the Fate of Rock','',1),(2541,'Survival Horror Game Book, A','',1),(2542,'IFG Sequence, The','',1),(2543,'Astro LibroGAME','',5),(2545,'Book of Legends: The Eternal Empire','\"Book of Legends - The Eternal Empire is a planned series of 11 choose your own adventure style gamebooks. They are set in an alternate reality where a shooting star shattered Roman Europe in an event known as the Divine Fire, and brought with it both wonderous magic and horrific creatures along with the powers of the ancient gods.<p> Each volume in the series covers an area of Planet Earth 800 years ago where the Roman Empire is locked in battle with the other great empires and the insidious denizen brought into existence by the Divine Fire. Being an \'open world\' series of books, you are free to move between volumes just as you would travel the world in real life today.\" (https://www.bookoflegends.co.uk/faq)',1),(2546,'Miscellaneous Works by Pedro Panhoca','The alpha version of the gamebook Ângela: a vingança transcontinental is the 1st appendix of the author\'s doctoral dissertation.',7),(2547,'Saga','\"Saga is an open-world gamebook series project by Martin Barnabus Noutch, author of Steam Highwayman, and Spidermind Games. A solo-roleplaying experience based on historic adventures of the people we know as the Vikings, you will be able to explore the Viking world from Vinland to Constantinople, leading a fellowship of memorable characters, fighting battles, out-witting your foes, prospering your home settlement and creating a great saga.\"(https://martinbarnabusnoutch.com/saga/)',1),(2548,'One Roll Gamebooks','',1),(2549,'Vier gegen die Finsternis','',3),(2550,'Echo 931','La nave colonica Dante X399 della Van Der Mer Corporation è in viaggio verso Echo 931...',5),(2551,'Ab Necessitate Excusi','In principio era Natura, l\'unica Dea, indifferente e crudele...',5),(2552,'Lone Wolf, Definitive Edition','In 2022, as the limited-edition run of the <a href=\"/Series/1106\">Lone Wolf Collector\'s Editions</a> neared completion, the Definitive Edition was introduced. These books, issued first in hardcover and later in paperback, were designed as an \"unlimited edition\" of the series with fully corrected texts and appendices, though they lack the bonus adventures found in the <a href=\"/Series/1106\">Collector\'s Editions</a>. The hardcover of the first volume contains the expanded version, whereas the paperback contains the original version.',1),(2553,'Choose Your Own Adventure Hardcovers','Some special titles were released only in hardcover by ChooseCo.',1),(2554,'Marvel Multiverse Missions','',1),(2555,'Scooby-Doo! Case Files','These full-color puzzle books combine a linear Scooby-Doo narrative with a series of visual puzzles (secret codes, word searches, etc.).',1),(2556,'You Choose: Could You Survive?','',1),(2557,'Heads or Tails','',1),(2558,'Ever After High','This series consists primarily of linear novels, but one story has a brief