r. The first of these adventures is a rework of the introductory adventure appearing on the <a href=\"/Series/383\">Runequest: Slayers</a> role-playing rulebook.',1),(2675,'Stwórz swoją przygodę','',28),(2676,'Miscellaneous Works by Łukasz Radecki','',28),(2677,'ACE Gamebooks (Polish)','The Polish editions do not have explicit series branding or use the \"ACE Gamebooks\" name, but they were released in a fairly uniform edition with similar graphic design across the titles.',28),(2678,'docu dont tu es le héros, Le','',2),(2679,'Twoja misja','',28),(2680,'Discovering with the Scientists','',1),(2681,'Choose Your Own Adventure: Your First Adventure','This series consists of board book abridgements of classic <a href=\"/Series/30\">Choose Your Own Adventure</a> books.',1),(2682,'Ma Première Aventure','',2),(2683,'Peter und die Juwelendiebe','',3),(2684,'My First Adventure','',1),(2685,'Mein erstes Abenteuer','',3),(2686,'Mi primera aventura','',6),(2687,'Heroes and Legends','',1),(2688,'Skin Horse','This web comic featured a (non-interactive) tribute to <a href=\"/Series/30\">Choose Your Own Adventure</a> as part of a storyline running from strips 890 to 980 (and reprinted in volume 4 of the collected editions). An actual gamebook was produced as a Kickstarter reward during the funding of the collected edition.',1),(2689,'Boy in the Book, The','This interactive documentary involves the search for the writer of a decades-old diary discovered inside a <a href=\"/Series/30\">Choose Your Own Adventure</a> book. It began life in 2014 as a traveling live show called <i>Choose Your Own Documentary</i> and was later adapted to an online format.',1),(2690,'Agencia Kronos. Tú decides la historia','',6),(2691,'Tú decides','',6),(2692,'Cartaventuras','This tabletop game provides a gamebook-like experience, using a deck of cards to generate narratives during play.',6),(2693,'Miscellaneous Works by Jacobo Feijóo','',6),(2694,'Miscellaneous Works by Charlotte Erpenbeck','',3),(2695,'Quasar','This RPG is related to the various <a href=\"/Category/116\">Quasar</a> gamebooks.',2),(2696,'Tajemne Oblicze Świata','',28),(2697,'Miscellaneous Works by Dominik Matusiak','',28),(2698,'Miscellaneous Works by Dominik Matusiak and Ewa Bednarek','',28),(2699,'Miscellaneous Works by Maciej Słomczyński and Beniamin Muszyński','',28),(2700,'Miscellaneous Works by Andrzej Betkiewicz','',28),(2701,'Miscellaneous Works by Kowalczyk Wojciech','',28),(2702,'Usborne Wybierz swoją opowieść','',28),(2703,'Miscellaneous Works by Kitty Curran and Larissa Zageris (Polish)','',28),(2704,'Miscellaneous Works by Paweł Bogdaszewski','',28),(2705,'Miscellaneous Works by Agnieszka Wiatrowska','',28),(2706,'Miscellaneous Works by Adam Jankowski','',28),(2707,'Miscellaneous Works by Michał Rosiński','',28),(2708,'Miscellaneous Works by Paweł Sikorski','',28),(2709,'Miscellaneous Works by Dorota Sidor','',28),(2710,'Miscellaneous Works by Paweł Celiński and Zuzanna Grębecka','',28),(2711,'Un livre dont tu es le héros ou l’héroïne','',2),(2712,'Książka-gra, której bohaterem jesteś ty!','',28),(2713,'Du entscheidest was passiert!','',3),(2714,'Miscellaneous Works by Igor Małyszczak','',28),(2715,'Miscellaneous Works by Alterlimbus','',28),(2716,'Miscellaneous Works by Filip Wójcik','',28),(2717,'Miscellaneous Works by Jarosław Klofta','',28),(2718,'Tkacze Burz','This solo tabletop game consists of a gamebook as well as figures and combat maps.',28),(2719,'Miscellaneous Works by Krzysztof Firkowski','',28),(2720,'Miscellaneous Works by Mikołaj Kołyszko','',28),(2721,'Powerless Series, The','',1),(2722,'Pick Your Own Quest','',1),(2723,'Star Trek Board Games','West End Games published multiple Star Trek properties with gamebook-like characteristics. <i>Star Trek: The Adventure Game</i> is playable either solitaire or by two players representing opposing Federation and Klingon sides and includes a paragraph book as part of its gameplay. Their <i>Star Trek III</i> collection of solitaire games includes one (<i>The Sherwood Syndrome</i>) with gamebook-like elements.',1),(2724,'Ellery Queen\'s Mystery Magazine Game','This board game challenges players to solve mysteries using mechanics very similar to <a href=\"/Series/2725\">Sherlock Holmes Consulting Detective</a>.',1),(2725,'Sherlock Holmes Consulting Detective','In this game, players can compete or collaborate to solve mysteries. After reading an introductory story, players consult with maps, newspapers, directories and a paragraph book to gain clues. After a limited number of turns, they must propose a solution; victory or defeat depends on whether the proposed solution matches the provided answer.\n\n<p>The game has been published in several editions and is supported by a number of expansions that add more cases (some of which require the base game, and some of which are stand-alone).',1),(2726,'Lone Wolf and Cub Game','This board game, based on the manga and totally unrelated to Joe Dever\'s Lone Wolf character, utilizes a paragraph book as part of its gameplay. While primarily designed as a solitaire experience, it also includes a two player competitive variant.',1),(2727,'New Yorker, The','This long-running magazine featured an interactive article about <a href=\"/Category/38\">Choose Your Own Adventure</a> in one issue.',1),(2728,'Choose Your Own Adventure (Bad Publisher Books)','This satirical publication is not officially licensed to use or affiliated with the <a href=\"/Category/38\">Choose Your Own Adventure</a> brand.',1),(2729,'One Minute Mysteries','',1),(2730,'Pokémon Chapter Books','These non-interactive novels are based on the video game series (and its associated television spin-off).',1),(2731,'Super Sleuth','',1),(2732,'Bakugan Battle Brawlers Chapter Books','These non-interactive novels are based on the game and media franchise.',1),(2733,'Scooby-Doo and You: Collect the Clues Mysteries','This series of \"guess-the-ending\" mysteries based on the popular cartoon was sold as a subscription service. The initial pack provided a \"clue keeper\" for gathering notes while reading the books. The books periodically prompt the reader to answer questions based on what they have read so far, and they provide a pausing point where the reader should try to solve the mystery based on what they have learned.',1),(2734,'Mathnet Casebooks','These books, based on the segment from the <i>Square One</i> television series, provide a linear narrative that incorporates occasional puzzles for the reader to solve.',1),(2735,'Quest Calendars','These gamebooks are presented in the form of page-a-day calendars. The first few pages go over rules and character creation, while the rest represent encounters. While the calendar format gives the adventures a necessarily linear structure, there is still significant decision-making within encounters as well as character development and inventory management along the way.',1),(2736,'One Shot Adventures (Dungeons & Dragons)','This a series comprising both solitaire and multiplayer RPG adventures, all of which are made available for free over the Internet on the author\'s blog. The first two solo adventures in the series were released in both <a href=\"/Series/13\">Dungeons & Dragons</a> (5th edition) and <a href=\"/Series/191\">GURPS Fantasy</a> (Fourth Edition) versions. <a href=\"/Series/2954\">A third solo adventure</a> is available in versions for both <i>GURPS Horror</i> and the <a href=\"/Series/60\">Call of Cthulhu</a> roleplaying game. There is no series numbering; the numbering below is intended to convey the release order. The first of these adventures is a rework of the introductory adventure appearing on the <a href=\"/Series/383\">Runequest: Slayers</a> role-playing rulebook.',1),(2737,'Last Knight Series, The','',1),(2738,'Miscellaneous Works by Marie Phillips','',1),(2739,'Miscellaneous Works by Bradley J. Jacobson','',1),(2740,'Miscellaneous Works by Jacob Allred','',1),(2741,'Your Choice Books','',1),(2742,'Last Wanderer','',1),(2743,'Miscellaneous Works by Steven Bennett','',1),(2744,'Miscellaneous Works by George Wylesol','',1),(2745,'Miscellaneous Works by Iain Hollingshead','',1),(2746,'GNAT Adventure Gamebooks','',1),(2747,'Game of Runes','',1),(2748,'Arkham Horror Investigators Gamebooks','',1),(2749,'Legacy Fantasy Spielbuch','',3),(2750,'Solo RPG Adventure Set in Irish Myth and Folklore, A','',1),(2751,'Huntress, The','<p>This series, set before the events of the main <a href=\"/Series/228\">Lone Wolf</a> series, casts the reader as The Huntress, an amnesiac who has turned to mercenary work as she seeks her true identity. The game system is similar to other series in the <a href=\"/Category/53\">Lone Wolf</a> family, with character creation centering around the selection of abilities from a diverse list, with inventory management taking an important role in strategy, and with a fast-paced, table-driven combat system.</p>\n\n<p>A prequel with a simplified game system, <a href=\"/Item/14743\">Shadows Over Fire</a>, was released for free online play to promote the series.</p>',1),(2752,'fils du Soleil, Les','',2),(2753,'AstroLibrogame','Serie di librogame editi da Astro edizioni',5),(2754,'Psychological Horror Gamebook, A','',1),(2755,'Welt von Odéa, Die','',3),(2756,'World of Odéa, The','',1),(2757,'monde d\'Odéa, Le','',2),(2758,'Mu\'n','',1),(2759,'Five Nights at Freddy\'s\\ Interactive Novels','',1),(2760,'Varney the Vampyr','',1),(2761,'Storymaster\'s Tales, The','These books can be played solo or used for group role-playing.',1),(2762,'Magical Kitties Save the Day','This RPG includes a solo adventure in the rulebook.',1),(2763,'Miscellaneous Works Published by Héritage','',2),(2764,'Zombie Gamebook, A','',1),(2765,'You Choose (Judaica Press)','This series appears to be completely unrelated to other series which use the same title.',1),(2766,'Miscellaneous Works by Dr. Tammy Watchorn','',1),(2767,'Domain of the Deathless King','Funded by Kickstarter.',1),(2768,'Open World Adventure Books','',5),(2769,'Legendary Kingdoms','',5),(2770,'Choose Your Own Psychopathy','',1),(2771,'Miscellaneous Works by Marianna Coppo','Marianna Coppo is author of <a href=\"/Item/14675\">The Book That Can Read Your Mind</a>, which uses gamebook and picture-book techniques to present an interactive magic trick to the reader.',1),(2772,'Librogame','Il ritorno della storica E.Elle alla pubblicazione di librogame dopo oltre vent\'anni!',5),(2773,'Mago Spacca','Apri questo libro per accompagnare Mago Spacca, detecrive privato, in un\'avventura senza precedenti, civili o penali che siano!',5),(2774,'A.S.P.E. - Lav Dit Eget Eventyr','',22),(2775,'Dungeon Gamebook','',1),(2776,'Bravest Warriors: This Way or That','',1),(2777,'Marteau & L\'Enclume, Le','Each issue of this magazine is devoted to a particular gamebook series or author. Some issues also include mini-gamebooks.',2),(2778,'Forge Divine','',2),(2779,'Fighting Fantasy – Vincent Books','Riedizione da parte di Raven-Vincent Books',5),(2780,'Hellwinter','Hellwinter è l\'ambientazione Twilight Fantasy di Andrea Tupac Mollica.',5),(2781,'Homo Homini Lupus','Questo non è solo un librogioco… questo è un gioco al massacro.',5),(2782,'Miscellaneous Works Published By Tora Edizioni','',5),(2783,'Miscellaneous Works by Alterlimbus','This author used crowd-funding to produce the largest single-volume gamebook published in Russian.',27),(2784,'Midsomer Murders','This is a tie-in with the long-running British television mystery series. The book includes a \"performance review\" section at the end where the reader\'s outcome is evaluated based on which ending was reached.',1),(2785,'Destiny\'s Role','Czech language translations',17),(2786,'Destiny\'s Role: Dimensions','Sci-fi spin-off from the main Destiny\'s Role gamebooks series. These form a single four-part epic storyline allowing the player to continue their character from one book to the next. Events and decisions from one book can greatly impact events and outcomes in subsequent books. Employs different polyhedral dice for different combat types: hand-to-hand and weapons combat using D6, phaser combat using d8, and ship-to-ship combat using D10',1),(2787,'What Happens Next?','',1),(2788,'Decide Your Own Destiny','',1),(2789,'Halloween ComicFest','',1),(2790,'Choose Your Own Adventure [Graphic Novels]','',1),(2791,'Zorn\'s Quest','Author Steven Kandas has self-published a significant number of \"Zorn\'s Quest\" books. Some are gamebooks while others are linear novels; only the gamebooks are listed here. Some of these books use the \"Fighting Fantasy\" name in their taglines and marketing without permission. Some titles were frequently revised, published with different cover and title variations.',1),(2792,'Miscellaneous Works by Saltatio Mortis','',3),(2793,'Teknoyd','Affronta un mucchio di bivi e attività per aiutare Ahiaaa a salvare la sua amata, nel primissimo manga-game italiano!',5),(2794,'Super You! Pick-Your-Path Adventures','These superpower-themed adventures offer the reader the opportunity to become a hero or villain.',1),(2795,'Press Start!','This series of easy-to-read chapter books about (fictional) video game hero Super Rabbit Boy primarily consists of traditional linear novels aimed at \"reluctant readers.\" However, the one volume listed here is an interactive gamebook.',1),(2796,'Miscellaneous Works by James Aukett','',1),(2797,'Letzte Silberklinge, Die','5e Solo-Abenteuer.',3),(2798,'Legendární království','',17),(2799,'Curse of Cthulhu, The','',1),(2800,'Devilish Dilemmas: An Edra Tales Gamebook','Kickstarter project.',1),(2801,'Armchair General, The','',1),(2802,'Lone Wolf Junior Editions','This series reprints the original <a href=\"/Series/228\">Lone Wolf</a> adventures with a slightly simplified game system designed to make them more accessible to younger and reluctant readers.',1),(2803,'ROLF!: The Rollplaying Game of Big Dumb Fighters','This RPG spawned at least one solo adventure.',1),(2804,'Choose Your Own Catholic Adventure','',1),(2805,'Þín eigin saga','These original Icelandic gamebooks are a companion series to <a href=\"/Series/2001\">Þín eigin...</a>, aimed at younger readers.',16),(2806,'Du er en rumspion','',22),(2807,'Carlsen 7-9-13 serien','',22),(2808,'Cold Blood Cooper','This gamebook series is inspired by the Fortnite video game, but is not officially licensed.',3),(2809,'Cold Blood Cooper','',22),(2810,'Du vælger handlingen i','',22),(2811,'EldritchQuest','',1),(2812,'Tenebrous Press Gamebooks','',1),(2813,'Miscellaneous Works by Ian Livingstone','',1),(2814,'Might & Morality Gamebook, A','',1),(2815,'En las cenizas','“En las cenizas” (In the Ashes) is a rather atypical gamebook. Divided into different battle scenarios set on hexagonal grids, the player controls a character who moves through these grids to achieve an objective, which typically involves defeating enemies. Although it features a complex game system, it only requires a pencil to play. The player uses it to mark the position and movement of the character and their adversaries on the book\'s pages for each scenario. This almost turns it into a board game in the form of a book.',6),(2816,'Microdédalos','Microdédalos (Micromazes) is a series of mini-adventures contained on a sheet of paper folded into thirds. They are designed to be played anywhere, using just a pencil and an eraser. The games last between 30 and 60 minutes and offer a high level of replayability.',6),(2817,'Flash Interactivo','This collection aims to revive the spirit of the popular pulp novels as well as dime novels, through a unique fusion with interactive fiction.',6),(2818,'drei ???, Die','This series translated the original non-interactive <i>The Three Investigators</i> books into German; after the original English series was exhausted, two of the <a href=\"/Series/163\">Find Your Fate - Random House</a> adventures were adapted into linear novels to extend the series, after which many original German-language titles were added. Eventually, multiple interactive series were spawned, including translations of the remaining English-language gamebooks (in the <a href=\"/Series/2819\">Top Secret Edition</a> series) along with further German-language originals (in the <a href=\"/Series/2821\">1000 Spuren - du hast die Wahl</a> and <a href=\"/Series/2820\">Dein Fall</a> series).',3),(2819,'drei ??? - Top Secret Edition, Die','This pair of boxed sets of previously untranslated <i>Three Investigators</i> materials included a gamebook in each set.',3),(2820,'drei ??? - Dein Fall, Die','This series consists of original German gamebooks spun off from <a href=\"/Series/2818\">Die drei ???</a>, the German version of <i>The Three Investigators</i>.',3),(2821,'drei ??? Kids - 1000 Spuren - du hast die Wahl, Die','This series of original German gamebooks is a spin-off from the junior version of <a href=\"/Series/2818\">Die drei ???</a>, the German translation of <i>The Three Investigators</i>. The series title changed to <i>Die drei ??? Kids - Dein Fall</i> with book number 22.',3),(2822,'Art Quest','Similar to other series of educational puzzle-based gamebooks by the same publisher, except apparently only one book was released for this series.',1),(2823,'Fifth Hero, The','',1),(2824,'Mizar III','Romanzo Interattivo! Qui il confine tra il lettore e il protagonista della storia si fa labile',5),(2825,'Hero Point','',1),(2826,'Punto de Héroe','',6),(2827,'Legender fra Lavlandet','',22),(2828,'Skæbnekrøniker','',22),(2829,'Miscellaneous Works by Jaiveer Asthana','This author has written a gamebook about online dating.',1),(2830,'Futurama Comics','This comic book series included one fully interactive issue. Some earlier issues also included experimental (but not quite gamebook-like) mechanics like multiple readings (by following different sequences of panels) or finding a secret ending by folding the page.',1),(2831,'Mythos Tales','This game is mechanically very similar to <a href=\"/Series/2725\">Sherlock Holmes Consulting Detective</a> but features mysteries involving H. P. Lovecraft\'s Cthulhu mythos.',1),(2832,'Gregor\'s Adventures','',1),(2833,'New Scientist','This weekly popular science magazine included a gamebook-format article in one issue.',1),(2834,'Miscellaneous Works by Dennis Wheatley and J. G. Links','British novelist Dennis Wheatley was an early pioneer of the \"solve it yourself\" genre, collaborating with J. G. Links to produce four \"crime dossiers\" consisting of collections of clues that the reader must study carefully in order to solve mysteries. These were original printed in the 1930\'s and were reissued in the late 1970\'s/early 1980\'s.',1),(2835,'Star Trek: Lower Decks','',1),(2836,'Tenkai Knights Pick Your Path','',1),(2837,'Escape Room Adventures','',1),(2838,'Gabriel Knox','This original Czech fantasy gamebook series follows the continuing adventures of a character named Gabriel Knox. It features a full game system and contains approximately 400 entries per book. Its marketing directly targets fans of <a href=\"/Series/11\">Fighting Fantasy</a> and <a href=\"/Series/228\">Lone Wolf</a>.',17),(2839,'Miscellaneous Works by Jan Kšanda','This Czech author has written a variety of gamebooks.',17),(2840,'Miscellaneous Works by Jiří Zahradníček','This Czech author has written a variety of gamebooks.',17),(2841,'Miscellaneous Works by Lenka Moravcová','This Czech author has written a variety of simple gamebooks aimed at younger readers and without formal game systems.',17),(2842,'Miscellaneous Works by C. M. Seabrook','This romance author has produced at least one interactive novel.',1),(2843,'1000 Gefahren (English releases)','A small number of gamebooks were released in English under the German series title <i>1000 Gefahren</i>, presumably as a tool for German readers learning the English language. There is <a href=\"/Series/26\">a separate listing for German-language releases in this series</a>. These books are not numbered; the numbering here is intended only to reflect original release order.',1),(2844,'1000 Gefahren Junior','This is a spin-off of <a href=\"/Series/26\">1000 Gefahren</a> aimed at younger readers, containing original German-language gamebooks. Some titles feature licensed Disney characters. The books are unnumbered; numbering here reflects the release order.',3),(2845,'Doctor Who: Solitaire Story Game','This fan-made print-and-play solitaire game features gameplay based on random tables and gamebook-like mechanisms, with gaps filled in by the imagination of the player.',1),(2846,'Choose-Your-Own-Path Shakespeare (Chinese translations)','',14),(2847,'Táo chū lángrén cūn [逃出狼人村]','',14),(2848,'Weenies','One volume in this series of light/humorous horror anthologies includes a short gamebook parody.',1),(2849,'Rumors from the Role-Inn','',1),(2850,'Choices Novels','',1),(2851,'Thriller-Spielbuch','',3),(2852,'Miscellaneous Works by Gabriel Garcia','',7),(2853,'Miscellaneous Works by Karen Soarele','',7),(2854,'Miscellaneous Works by Athos Beuren','',7),(2855,'Miscellaneous Works by Gustavo Ramos','',7),(2856,'Miscellaneous Works by Shuky and Gorobei','',2),(2857,'Miscellaneous Works by Roland Stenglin','',3),(2858,'Miscellaneous Works by Luiz Claudio Gonçalves','',7),(2859,'Miscellaneous Works by Vitor Soares and Giovanni Arceno','',7),(2860,'Shifting Quest, The','',1),(2861,'ACE Gamebooks (Brazil)','',7),(2862,'Miscellaneous Works by João Anzanello Carrascoza','',7),(2863,'Miscellaneous Works by Tiago Filipe Costa','',7),(2864,'Miscellaneous Works by Luís Dinis','',7),(2865,'Miscellaneous Works by Ayn Rand','In 1933, Ayn Rand wrote a play, <i>Night of January 16th</i>, that depended on audience participation and had multiple possible endings.',1),(2866,'Miscellaneous Works by Filipe Faria','',7),(2867,'Miscellaneous Works by José Roberto Torero & Marcus Aurelius Pimenta','',7),(2868,'Miscellaneous Works by Marcelo Cassaro','',7),(2869,'Miscellaneous Works by Gustavo V. Ramos','',7),(2870,'Miscellaneous Works by Rafael Rix Gerônimo','',7),(2871,'I Ragnaroks Aske','',22),(2872,'In cerca di fortuna','',5),(2873,'misteri delle catacombe, I','',5),(2874,'Miscellaneous Works by Andrea Angiolino','',5),(2875,'Ecos da fantasia','',7),(2876,'Sci-Fi Spielbuch','',3),(2877,'Miscellaneous Works by Harry Stephen Keeler','This author, known for his \"web-work mysteries,\" wrote at least one relatively early example of the \"guess-the-ending\" mystery: a linear book which, at a certain point, challenges the reader to write down the solution before reading further.',1),(2878,'Chi è stato?','',5),(2879,'MagiKal Crimes','',5),(2880,'Miscellaneous Works by Will Rogers','',1),(2881,'Lovecraftian Horror Gamebook, A','',17),(2882,'Stygian Swordscapes','',1),(2883,'Klabauter Chronicles, The','',1),(2884,'Prince Ken-Rhyl: Ashar Cycle','',1),(2885,'Prince Ken-Rhyl: Cycle Ashar','',2),(2886,'Reality','Serie di librogame in cui interpreti il protagonista di un Reality televisivo. Le tue scelte saranno in grado di farti vincere il montepremi in palio?',5),(2887,'Adventures in Alanor','',1),(2888,'Miscellaneous Works by Stephen Hart','Financed by Kickstarter.',1),(2889,'Gamebook Officina Meningi','',5),(2890,'Escape Book Junior - Il battello a vapore','Collana \"Junior\" (9+) degli Escape Book de Il battello a Vapore. Rispetto alla collana principale (10+), prevalentemente genere Horror, questa ha un sapore più di avventura e mistero.',5),(2891,'Game Book Giunti','Il ritorno di Giunti Editore (ex Giunti Marzocco) al mondo del librogame, a distanza di trent\'anni dall\'ultima pubblicazione.\nNella stessa collana (Game Book) presenta più filoni: Escape (\"Esci, se riesci!\"), Mystery e Creative.',5),(2892,'Ensomme Ulv (Faraos Cigarer)','',22),(2893,'Miscellaneous Works by Antony Johnston','Antony Johnston is a versatile author who worked on various genres, from supernatural to thriller to crime mystery; from books to videogames.',1),(2894,'Nuova Narrativa Newton','',5),(2895,'Escape the Dark','This series of cooperative board games incorporates gamebook-like decision-making and mechanics.',1),(2896,'Old-School Essentials','',1),(2897,'Romance-Fantasy-Spielbuch','',3),(2898,'Choose Your Own Adventure Algebra Gamebooks','',1),(2899,'Decide Your Fate Books from Alternate Histories','',1),(2900,'Choose Your Own Regency Romance','',1),(2901,'Supernatural','This ties in with the American TV series of the same name.',1),(2902,'Weltenwanderer','One issue of this German magazine has a number of articles on solo RPGs and gamebooks.',3),(2903,'Choose Your Bondage Fantasy','',1),(2904,'Lone Wolf, 40th Anniversary Omnibus','This limited edition (of 400 copies) collected the first two <a href=\"/Category/53\">Lone Wolf</a> books plus an original mini-adventure. The first book is reproduced in its original 350-section version, not the later expanded form.',1),(2905,'Choose Your Quest','',1),(2906,'Decide & Survive','',1),(2907,'7-Minute Your-Choice Adventures: For Building Character','',1),(2908,'Meg Mackintosh','',1),(2909,'Fighting Fantasy (2025-, Steve Jackson Games)','',1),(2910,'Lone Wolf Anthology','These collections contain non-interactive fiction set in the world of Magnamund.',1),(2911,'Star Academy, Die','',3),(2912,'Pick Your Own Path - Choose Your Own Fate','',1),(2913,'Miscellaneous Works by Vilian Stefanov [Вилиан Стефанов]','',8),(2914,'Section 3','',8),(2915,'АЛФА & ΩМЕГА','\"ALPHA & ΩMEGA\" is a magazine dedicated to interactive and all kinds of literature—gamebooks, comics, games, films, books, and everything that excites us. With this publication, our goal is to create a shared platform for fans of quality fantasy, science fiction, adventure, and other forms of literature, comic series, as well as players of gamebooks, board games, and role-playing games.',8),(2916,'ALPHA & ΩMEGA','ALPHA & ΩMEGA is a magazine dedicated to interactive and all kinds of literature - gamebooks, comics, games, films, books, and everything that excites us. With this publication, our goal is to create a shared platform for fans of quality fantasy, science fiction, adventure, and other forms of literature, comic series, as well as players of gamebooks, board games, and role-playing games.',8),(2917,'Du er skurken!','',22),(2918,'Planetfall','This science fiction anthology includes a gamebook interspersed with short fiction and other content. The mechanics are simplistic: the player reads some text, makes note of decisions, then turns the page to learn the consequences. There is a hint of a forthcoming <i>Planetfall Two</i>, so this seems to have been intended as a series; however, it seems that the second volume was never released.',1),(2919,'Choose Your Own Ending Bedtime Story','',1),(2920,'Murder You Wrote','This interactive mystery novel was collaboratively written by twenty authors. L. J. M. Owen served as lead editor as well as one of the contributors.',1),(2921,'Choose Your Own Adventure: New Classics','Starting in 2021, this series of original adventures was released in parallel with the <a href=\"/Series/870\">Choose Your Own Adventure reissues</a>. These books have a larger format than the reissues. While they are listed and numbered in catalogs as the \"New Classics\" series, there is no series subtitle or numbering printed on the books themselves.',1),(2922,'Sandbox Series','',6),(2923,'Sandbox Series','',1),(2924,'Sunfall','Funded by Kickstarter.',1),(2925,'You Choose: Life or Death','A subseries of the Capstone You Choose series focusing on life or death scenarios in different environments.',1),(2926,'Fighting Fantasy','',23),(2927,'mondo delle 1000 avventure, Il','',5),(2928,'Stærkoddersagaen','',22),(2929,'Legendary Kingdoms','',6),(2930,'Vive tu propia aventura!: Nancy Drew y los Hardy, ¡','',6),(2931,'Operation CanCon','<p>Relive the history of Canadian music in this flashback trilogy. The <i>Operation CanCon</i> series blends nostalgic storytelling, solo gaming, and retro treasure hunting. Your mission: recover lost Canadian Content hidden in iconic shops, across the twentieth century and beyond.\n\n<p>Grab something to write with, three six-sided dice, and roll through branching paths, strategic choices, and bin-diving minigames. You’ll leap through decades and destinations, each standalone instalment forming part of an epic journey through the culture that shaped a nation.\n\n<p>Ideal for fans of roll-and-write games, interactive fiction, and Canadiana, <i>Operation CanCon</i> is more than nostalgia; it’s a quest to preserve a musical legacy, one hit after another.',1),(2932,'Miscellaneous Works by Derek Schraner','Individual gamebooks which are not part of a wider series.',1),(2933,'Break','<p>In the <i>Break</i> system series, you don\'t just read a story, you\'ll play it. Each book is a standalone heist adventure, yet they all connect to form an overarching narrative that follows your journey as an evolving thief. This series ramps up progressively, to turn you from a passive reader into an active player.\n\n<p>Your journey begins with <i>The Spring Break</i>. Set in 1970s Hawaii, this prequel story drops you into an urgent pawn shop heist, an initiation into the world behind the <i>Break</i> system. It serves as a natural entry point into both the unfolding narrative and the deeper mechanics at play, laying the groundwork for everything to come.\n\n<p>The interactivity begins with <i>The Summer Job</i>, a branching story set in an open world, against the backdrop of Kyoto’s Gion Matsuri festival. This first mission is a high-stakes heist where your choices alone determine your path and shape dozens of potential outcomes.\n\n<p>The stakes and complexity rise in <i>The Fall Affair</i>. You’ll travel to an old, haunted casino in Ontario to find a doomsday device with a secret link to your past. Here, the narrative evolves, blending your decisions with dice-rolling mechanics to create a mix of choice and chance.\n\n<p>This adventure culminates in <i>The Winter Mission</i>, which ties up the overarching story. Set in the Swiss Alps during the December holiday season, this finale challenges you to assemble a team for a daring rescue. This gamebook introduces strategic elements like planning and team management, preparing you for what\'s next.\n\n<p>Upon completing the gamebooks, you\'ll be ready for the ultimate challenge: <i>The Break System</i>. This master rulebook -- which includes an annotated version of <i>The Spring Break</i> as its tutorial -- will provide all the tools you\'ll need to create and play your own ongoing heists!',1),(2934,'Fighting Fantasy (Celaeno Books)','',6),(2935,'Witchbound','From the Kickstarter description:  \n\nExplore an enchanting world, learn magic, craft potions, fight monsters, and discover secrets in this open-world, story-driven game about becoming the first witch in over 100 years.',1),(2936,'1930 Horror Crime Adventures','',3),(2937,'Sleeping Gods','This solo/co-op board game series features atlas books representing the player\'s location, and paragraph books to provide descriptions and narrative choices for points of interest.\nPlayers control a crew of multiple character with their own attributes and abilities.',1),(2938,'Adventure Games','This series of boardgames features paragraph booklets which are referenced when exploring points of interest, using items, and combining items. In this way the series simulates PC point-and-click games.',3),(2939,'Adventure Games','Several of the German <a href=\"/Series/2938\">Adventure Games</a> board games were translated into English.',1),(2940,'Tainted Grail','This series of dark fantasy board games has players exploring maps built up from numbered cards, and exploring points of interest and making narrative choices via a paragraph books.',1),(2941,'Etherfields','This board game features a paragraph book for points of interest and narrative choices.',1),(2942,'Magic Tales','',5),(2943,'Torino Arcana','',5),(2944,'Arydia','This co-operative RPG board game features cards with story text offering narrative choices to players.',1),(2945,'Dragon Eclipse','This series of Pokemon-inspired board games feature paragraph books for points of interest and narrative choice.',1),(2946,'Vantage','This board game uses a paragraph book to provide players with narrative outcomes for how they choose to interact with points of interest.',1),(2947,'Earthborne Rangers','This open-world narrative card game features a paragraph books for narrative choices in its campaigns.',1),(2948,'The 7th Continent','This board game features numbered cards to provide players with story text and narrative choices.',1),(2949,'The 7th Citadel','This board game features numbered cards to provide players with story text and narrative choices. It is a spiritual successor to <a href=\"/Series/2948\">The 7th Continent</a>.',1),(2950,'Endless Destinies','This gamebook is published as a box set with a main book with color maps and illustrations, and cards for combat mechanics.',1),(2951,'Lost in Adventure','This series of board games features numbered cards with story text, with mechanics inspirationed by point-and-click video games.',1),(2952,'Lost Ones','This board game features a paragraph book for story text and narrative choices.',1),(2953,'Classified','Canadian rapper Classified released an album featuring branching narrative choices by skipping to different track numbers.',1),(2954,'One Shot Adventures (Call of Cthulhu)','This a series comprising both solitaire and multiplayer RPG adventures, all of which are made available for free over the Internet on the author\'s blog. <a href=\"/Series/2736\">The first two solo adventures in the series</a> were released in both <a href=\"/Series/13\">Dungeons & Dragons</a> (5th edition) and <a href=\"/Series/191\">GURPS Fantasy</a> (Fourth Edition) versions. The third solo adventure (listed here) is available in versions for both <i>GURPS Horror</i> and the <a href=\"/Series/60\">Call of Cthulhu</a> roleplaying game. There is no series numbering; the numbering below is intended to convey the release order.',1),(2955,'Backstories','This series of board games features numbered cards for story text, to build up location panoramas with points of interest, as well as for player status and inventory. Certain cards, such as actions and items, have holes cut into the sides or faces, and are can be placed on the backs of cards representing interactive points of interest to combine the two and show text describing the result and consequences. In this way the series simulates PC point-and-click games.',1);
